{
	chapter.1088DE9219BFAC7C.title: " &f&lWelcome"
	chapter.12CDF5CBC3F3857A.title: " &f&lPowah"
	chapter.29327EDA7EABA2D7.title: " &f&lModern Industrialization"
	chapter.38B491FF56A249C0.title: " &f&lImmersive Engineering"
	chapter.5C3FF9D1ECAC4860.title: " &l&fCreate \\& Addons"
	chapter.6DF110DEE277173B.title: " &f&lApplied Energistics 2"
	chapter.6FD1496307A969ED.title: " &f&lOritech"
	chapter.B1E6D954A7F8032C.title: "Applied Energistics 2"
	file.0000000000000001.title: " &r&lOverclock: Tech Automation"
	quest.003DA39A1577F438.quest_desc: ["Smelt stainless steel dust in an Electric Blast Furnace to obtain hot ingots, then cool them back into solid ingots using a Vacuum Freezer. It's the gateway material to MV-tier machinery and most midgame progression."]
	quest.003DA39A1577F438.quest_subtitle: "A premium alloy that unlocks the Advanced Machine Hull and the midgame tech tree."
	quest.00511651BDBCBE0B.quest_desc: ["Assembled in the atomic forge from processing units, heisenberg compensators, and platinum. Required for the super AI chip and a handful of other endgame systems."]
	quest.00511651BDBCBE0B.quest_subtitle: "A high-end processor for complex logic and control systems."
	quest.00F44F4FA88A59F9.quest_desc: ["Right-click a Rope Winch and a Rope Connector with a Rope Coupling to attach a rope between them. Once given Rotational Force, the Winch reels the rope in or out depending on rotation direction. Shears cut the rope, and right-clicking the rope while holding a Wrench lets you slide down it like a zipline."]
	quest.00F44F4FA88A59F9.quest_subtitle: "A motorized spool that reels rope in or out under Rotational Force."
	quest.01A35962129F85B8.quest_desc: ["Connect pipes to any block with fluid handling. Right-click the relevant pipe part to toggle extraction. No wrench is needed. However, a wrench can be used to disable pipe connections."]
	quest.01A35962129F85B8.quest_subtitle: "Transports liquids between machines and tanks. The default transfer rate is 0.5 buckets every 3 ticks. Fluid pipes do not have internal storage."
	quest.01AF8F8A669974E4.quest_desc: ["Printed in the Inscriber using a Calculation Processor Press found in meteorite loot. Combine the printed circuit with printed silicon and a logic processor in the Inscriber to assemble the final Calculation Processor."]
	quest.01AF8F8A669974E4.quest_subtitle: "The Calculation Processor is required for crafting advanced AE2 components such as terminals and storage devices."
	quest.01C7A2DB13CD1747.quest_desc: ["Manufactured through chemical reactions and freezing, then used in the Quantum Circuit Board and the Gravichestplate. Represents the frontier of cryogenic tech in the mod."]
	quest.01C7A2DB13CD1747.quest_subtitle: "A supercooled module used in quantum-tier machinery."
	quest.0231C7713767FDE9.quest_desc: ["Smelt plutonium dust extracted from spent uranium rods to obtain a full ingot. Used to craft MOX-style fuel rods for much higher reactor efficiency."]
	quest.0231C7713767FDE9.quest_subtitle: "A fissile ingot used to craft high-efficiency nuclear fuel rods."
	quest.025A48679E01A696.quest_desc: ["Greatly improves ratios when combining dusts into alloys like bronze, fire clay, and uncooked steel. Also produces cobblestone and clay from simple inputs, making it one of the first bronze machines you should build."]
	quest.025A48679E01A696.quest_subtitle: "A steam-powered machine that mixes dusts into alloys."
	quest.027BA3FBAE0592AA.quest_desc: ["Each fluid pipe stores 1 bucket internally, and directly connected pipes share their buffer — so every extra pipe increases network throughput. Right-click the center of a pipe with a wrench to toggle connections, or shift-right-click to dismantle it."]
	quest.027BA3FBAE0592AA.quest_subtitle: "Transports fluids between tanks, machines, and hatches."
	quest.028EA9E631877ABE.quest_desc: ["Budding Certus blocks grow Certus Quartz Buds similarly to amethyst. Flawed is the second-lowest tier — each time a bud advances a growth stage, the block has a chance to degrade, eventually becoming a plain Certus block. Repair or upgrade by throwing it in water together with Charged Certus Quartz Crystals. Place Growth Accelerators adjacent to massively speed up bud production."]
	quest.028EA9E631877ABE.quest_subtitle: "A degradable certus quartz source found in meteorites. Grows Certus Quartz Buds from its faces over time."
	quest.02BA3F75BA3429CC.quest_desc: ["Laser-specific addons such as quarry, silk touch, hunter, and crop filter all attach to the laser arm. Combine them to shape your laser into the mining or defense tool you need."]
	quest.02BA3F75BA3429CC.quest_subtitle: "Specialist addons that modify how an enderic laser behaves."
	quest.02E3A39A95EE6F22.quest_desc: ["Throw all three ingredients into water at the same time to trigger the reaction. This process can be automated using Formation and Annihilation Planes on a subnetwork."]
	quest.02E3A39A95EE6F22.quest_subtitle: "Fluix Crystal is a key AE2 material made by combining charged certus quartz, nether quartz, and redstone in water."
	quest.02EF953AA55E2123.quest_desc: ["Passes FE between adjacent blocks and the Ender Network at the Blazing rate. A cheaper alternative to the Ender Cell when capacity upgrades are not needed."]
	quest.02EF953AA55E2123.quest_subtitle: "Blazing Network Gateway"
	quest.02FCA29535F30817.quest_desc: ["Each tier cuts the energy consumed per operation but slows the machine down. Often paired with a speed addon to rebalance throughput while keeping running costs low."]
	quest.02FCA29535F30817.quest_subtitle: "Higher-tier efficiency addons from Oritech Things for reduced power draw."
	quest.02FCA29535F30817.title: "More Efficiency"
	quest.0399B710043D3817.quest_desc: ["Bind a Wireless Terminal to the access point by right-clicking it. Range can be extended with Wireless Booster upgrade cards. Requires 1 channel to operate."]
	quest.0399B710043D3817.quest_subtitle: "Enables wireless access to your ME Network from anywhere within range."
	quest.03F79DC1D00217F5.quest_desc: ["Fluids stored in the network are accessible through the ME Terminal. Fluid cells fit into the same Drive slots as item cells. Use Import/Export Buses or the Interface to automate fluid handling."]
	quest.03F79DC1D00217F5.quest_subtitle: "ME Fluid Storage Cells store liquids in the ME Network, working just like item cells but for fluids."
	quest.03F79DC1D00217F5.title: "ME Fluid Storage Cell"
	quest.041C1088D9DEE433.quest_desc: ["Produced in the atomic forge from superconductors and platinum. A core ingredient for the advanced augment station, superconductor cables, and several late-game control blocks."]
	quest.041C1088D9DEE433.quest_subtitle: "Flux gates are high-tier control parts used where Oritech needs to regulate large amounts of power."
	quest.045DDEE342CC7D0F.quest_desc: ["Central to autocrafting setups. Place next to a Molecular Assembler or any crafting machine. Supports blocking mode to prevent overlapping batches, and can distribute work across multiple machines in round-robin."]
	quest.045DDEE342CC7D0F.quest_subtitle: "The Pattern Provider pushes crafting ingredients to adjacent machines and collects the results back into the network."
	quest.046B24BB8F09AF04.quest_desc: [
		"To set the target direction, use a target designator on the laser block. The laser has a maximum range of 128 blocks and will continue firing until obstructed or disabled by a redstone signal. Note that you're only setting a target direction, not target block. It will try to destroy all blocks in that direction."
		""
		"When mining, the laser automatically collects drops into its internal inventory."
	]
	quest.046B24BB8F09AF04.quest_subtitle: "The enderic laser uses large amounts of energy to fire a high-power beam in a specific direction. It is primarily used for rapid long-range mining or as an long-range power transmission system."
	quest.04A514CC5CDC9440.quest_desc: ["Produced from superconductor components through the chemical and freezing processing lines. Required alongside cooling cells and a quantum circuit board to assemble Quantum Circuits."]
	quest.04A514CC5CDC9440.quest_subtitle: "A quantum bit — the basic unit of quantum computation."
	quest.04B893E41EA91853.quest_desc: ["Higher I/O than the Hardened Rod. Stack multiple Blazing Rods around the Energizing Orb to further increase processing speed."]
	quest.04B893E41EA91853.quest_subtitle: "Blazing Throughput"
	quest.04BFB3091C5A2AD2.quest_desc: ["Once inserted, the particle travels along a route defined by the guide rings. They can be right-clicked to add a 45-degree turn on one side. Another guide ring needs to be in the particle's path as defined by the guide rings. Depending on the speed, the allowed distance between guide blocks increases."]
	quest.04BFB3091C5A2AD2.quest_subtitle: "Guide rings shape the path of particles inside the accelerator. The first one must sit directly behind the controller, aligned with its visual indicator."
	quest.04D21104CBDC4FE9.quest_desc: ["Dense cables are essential for high-channel backbones connecting your Controller to distant parts of the network. The smart variant shows how many of the 32 channels are currently in use."]
	quest.04D21104CBDC4FE9.quest_subtitle: "The Smart Dense Cable carries up to 32 channels while displaying individual channel activity via colored indicators."
	quest.04E0B6B6D3A04972.quest_desc: ["Put iron, copper, or tin ores in it to receive 2 raw ores per block. Adding a Hammer in the slot increases the output ratio and unlocks more recipes. The Forge Hammer is your first step toward automated processing."]
	quest.04E0B6B6D3A04972.quest_subtitle: "A manual workstation for basic ore and material processing."
	quest.04EB6DC23F87A915.quest_desc: ["Used in crafting Import Buses and Annihilation Planes. The Annihilation Plane breaks the block directly in front of it and stores the drops. Pair it with a Formation Core for full item I/O."]
	quest.04EB6DC23F87A915.quest_subtitle: "The Annihilation Core is the input half of AE2's plane system, pulling items and blocks from the world into the network."
	quest.051477732CB88DC3.quest_desc: ["Attach to any machine to toggle operation based on redstone input. Can be switched between normal and inverted mode, making it easy to gate expensive machines on demand."]
	quest.051477732CB88DC3.quest_subtitle: "Enables redstone control over a machine's operation."
	quest.0520236A417538FA.quest_desc: ["A powered multiblock that combines fluid and item inputs into a mixed output fluid. Used for producing Concrete, Potion fluids, and other mixed recipes. Requires power and fluid piping to operate."]
	quest.0520236A417538FA.quest_subtitle: "Mixes fluids and items together to create new products."
	quest.053FDD5AD459D89A.quest_desc: ["Place the bearing facing the structure that will become the propeller: any group of at least two sail-like blocks counts as a valid blade, and more sails produce more Thrust. Reverse the rotation, or right-click the bearing with a Wrench, to reverse the Thrust direction. Air Pressure reduces output at high altitude."]
	quest.053FDD5AD459D89A.quest_subtitle: "Mounts a propeller in front of itself and converts the input Rotational Force into Thrust."
	quest.054B196C55432353.quest_desc: ["Feed it an overcharged crystal and plenty of RF to begin extraction. It pulls high-tier resources straight from deep chunk samples, bypassing the need to quarry huge areas by hand."]
	quest.054B196C55432353.quest_subtitle: "An endgame mining machine that extracts rare materials from the bedrock layer."
	quest.0572CCD3BBC71103.quest_desc: ["Converts hot fluids into large amounts of FE. At Niotic tier, maintaining a large lava tank is critical to keep the generator running continuously."]
	quest.0572CCD3BBC71103.quest_subtitle: "Niotic Lava Power"
	quest.05DC05AF38649B73.quest_desc: ["Required by the Oil Drilling Rig and Electric Quarry to access deeper, rarer deposits such as platinum and titanium. Far more durable than the Bronze Drill."]
	quest.05DC05AF38649B73.quest_subtitle: "An advanced drill head consumed by the electric quarry and oil rig."
	quest.0648BF8253CA29BD.quest_desc: ["Link two Light P2P tunnels using the Memory Card: sneak-right-click the input tunnel to copy its frequency, then right-click the output tunnel to link them. One input can serve multiple output tunnels."]
	quest.0648BF8253CA29BD.quest_subtitle: "Transmits light levels from one location to another through the ME Network."
	quest.06B63DD4AF1541A6.quest_desc: ["Used to craft Redstone and Capacity Cards. Insert upgrade cards into the upgrade slot found in any compatible AE2 device's interface."]
	quest.06B63DD4AF1541A6.quest_subtitle: "A basic upgrade card that enables simple control options on AE2 devices."
	quest.07165E0EB1BE2850.quest_desc: ["Highest-output solar generator in Powah. A compact Nitro Solar array provides substantial passive FE throughout the day with zero running cost."]
	quest.07165E0EB1BE2850.quest_subtitle: "Nitro Solar Array"
	quest.075E97B2BB5F93DF.quest_desc: ["Items cannot be added or removed by the player, but by components such as Chutes, Funnels, and Item Hatches."]
	quest.075E97B2BB5F93DF.quest_subtitle: "By default, each Item Vault block has a storage space of 20 stacks."
	quest.081BF8F9E3C8F2B3.quest_desc: ["Overclocks wire production up to 32 EU/t. Paired with Assemblers producing cables, it removes one of the biggest bottlenecks of early electric setups."]
	quest.081BF8F9E3C8F2B3.quest_subtitle: "The electric version of the Steel Wiremill."
	quest.0840C62E91BAD7FE.quest_desc: ["Right-click to toggle the Typewriter, granting control over each key's bound frequency. Sneak-right-click opens the Configuration Interface; right-clicking with a Linked Controller copies its bindings; and right-clicking a Redstone Link Receiver with a key item enters Bind Mode for one-press assignments. Bindings persist when broken."]
	quest.0840C62E91BAD7FE.quest_subtitle: "Binds keyboard keys to Redstone Link frequencies: a custom keyboard for an entire Contraption."
	quest.087FC87AA653E808.quest_desc: ["Stores FE in a channel of your Ender Network. Any Ender Cell linked to the same channel can access the stored energy anywhere in the dimension."]
	quest.087FC87AA653E808.quest_subtitle: "Wireless Energy Storage"
	quest.098624BAEC3965A5.quest_desc: ["Placed adjacent to an inventory, it automatically charges any FE items stored inside. Useful for passively keeping tools and batteries topped off."]
	quest.098624BAEC3965A5.quest_subtitle: "Auto Item Charger"
	quest.099A4C2181B22A34.quest_desc: ["Extracts FE from charged items at a very high rate. Place it beside a storage system for rapid power recovery from stored items."]
	quest.099A4C2181B22A34.quest_subtitle: "Spirited FE Extractor"
	quest.09BE3D92053AE1F8.quest_desc: ["When attempting to place the Roller on the top face of a block, it will be placed one block above it, similarly to a Mechanical Mixer or Mechanical Press. Though it appears to take up a few blocks of space, it only takes up one. There is also Placement Assist functionality, allowing for easy placement of Rollers to either of two sides of a roller. The Roller can be picked up by sneak using a Wrench on it."]
	quest.09BE3D92053AE1F8.quest_subtitle: "The Mechanical Roller can be used on Contraptions to clear and pave a path."
	quest.0A3B92620D7B6EDC.quest_desc: ["Interact with it by right-clicking with a bucket or another tank to transfer fluids. Tanks stack in your inventory when their contents match, and they connect directly to machines for automated fluid I/O."]
	quest.0A3B92620D7B6EDC.quest_subtitle: "A placeable tank that stores up to 4 buckets of a single fluid."
	quest.0A55B411AB662280.quest_desc: ["Place items on the Blaze Forger's Depot. While supplied with Liquid Experience, it smelts the items even faster than a regular furnace, including some materials that cannot be smelted vanilla. The XP fluid is consumed in proportion to the value of each operation."]
	quest.0A55B411AB662280.quest_subtitle: "Smelts items by burning Liquid Experience under the heat of a Blaze Burner."
	quest.0A8814659B697F55.quest_desc: ["Runs on RF and bonemeal-like materials. Each tick has a chance to accelerate the growth of nearby crops, saplings, and other plants that react to bonemeal."]
	quest.0A8814659B697F55.quest_subtitle: "Applies bonemeal to crops in a small area around it."
	quest.0B68610D72F11257.quest_desc: ["Produced by mixing Coke Dust with Water in a Mixer. Burning this raw oil in a Steam Blast Furnace refines it into Synthetic Oil, the precursor to all early rubber production."]
	quest.0B68610D72F11257.quest_subtitle: "The first step in the synthetic rubber chain."
	quest.0B7D86BB91AEED2F.quest_desc: ["Buffers a modest amount of RF and can be connected to machines and generators with energy pipes. A simple way to smooth out production before you reach the large storage block."]
	quest.0B7D86BB91AEED2F.quest_subtitle: "A compact energy storage block for early power networks."
	quest.0B86006B88A2F2E0.quest_desc: ["Each tier of cell component requires the previous tier to craft. Combine any component with a cell housing to create the corresponding ME Storage Cell."]
	quest.0B86006B88A2F2E0.quest_subtitle: "The 1k Cell Component is the base ingredient for all ME storage cells."
	quest.0BA721CA39D6A358.quest_desc: ["Feed it power and it will mine the block directly in front of its face. Use an inventory proxy or pipe to pull drops out — perfect for controlled quarries or cobblestone generators."]
	quest.0BA721CA39D6A358.quest_subtitle: "Automatically breaks the block in front of it."
	quest.0BA80D8E876994D6.quest_desc: ["Charges items in a linked player's inventory wirelessly, anywhere in the dimension. Higher capacity and faster I/O than the Hardened version."]
	quest.0BA80D8E876994D6.quest_subtitle: "Blazing Wireless Charger"
	quest.0BB7765E3190C88A.quest_desc: ["Built from Nuclear Casings and Nuclear Hatches, the reactor heats water into steam using fuel rods and can produce hundreds of times more EU/t than diesel. It's also the only source of Plutonium, Deuterium, and Tritium."]
	quest.0BB7765E3190C88A.quest_subtitle: "A scalable multiblock that generates enormous power from nuclear fuel."
	quest.0BBE6CADED48A971.quest_desc: [
		"Click a Stock Link with the Stock Ticker to connect it to that network. Place a Mob in a Seat or a Blaze Burner behind the Stock Ticker to turn it into a Stock Keeper."
		""
		"The Stock Keeper can see all the items on the network. The UI displays how many Stock Links are connected. If the Stock Keeper is left unlocked, players can search the network, request items, and give their requests an Address to be sent to."
		""
		"If the Stock Keeper is locked, other players will not be able to access its UI. The Stock Keeper will still be able to accept Shopping Lists."
	]
	quest.0BBE6CADED48A971.quest_subtitle: "A Stock Ticker is used to request items from a Logistics Network."
	quest.0C2058ED0EF41590.quest_desc: ["Applied Energistics 2 (AE2) introduces a unique approach to inventory management and automation. Its futuristic sci-fi theme centers around the concept of converting matter into energy and vice versa for instantaneous resource transportation."]
	quest.0C2058ED0EF41590.quest_subtitle: "A Mod about Matter, Energy and using them to conquer the world.."
	quest.0C2BFE016DF61A2D.quest_desc: ["Used in cable crafting, circuit boards, and nearly every electronic component. An early reason to automate the Steel Wiremill with an Assembler."]
	quest.0C2BFE016DF61A2D.quest_subtitle: "Thin copper wire produced by the Wiremill."
	quest.0C9D044821AA0C64.quest_desc: ["A specialized crafting table for IE's electronic circuit recipes. Place it in the world and insert the required components via GUI. Used to produce Circuit Boards that are then assembled into full Electronic Components."]
	quest.0C9D044821AA0C64.quest_subtitle: "Crafts Circuit Boards and assembles electronic components."
	quest.0CBE86996CD49BAF.quest_desc: ["Pulls heat from adjacent fuel rods and spreads it to neighboring vents or absorbers. The maximum transfer per tick grows with the temperature difference between the two sides."]
	quest.0CBE86996CD49BAF.quest_subtitle: "Transfers heat between reactor components."
	quest.0D46D11DF8968CF5.quest_desc: ["Craft cartridges with the Metal Press bullet casing mold. Available ammo: Casull (10 damage), Armor-Piercing, Buckshot, Dragon's Breath, Homing, and Wolfpack. Upgrade the magazine capacity at the Engineer's Workbench."]
	quest.0D46D11DF8968CF5.quest_subtitle: "An 8-round revolver with diverse ammunition types."
	quest.0D6B980A109BDD67.quest_desc: ["An upgraded version of the basic augment station. Required for late-game augments such as flight and combat enhancements, which the standard station cannot install."]
	quest.0D6B980A109BDD67.quest_subtitle: "Applies high-tier cybernetic augments to the player."
	quest.0E5FC39E6C71A872.quest_desc: [
		"A &6&oshaft&r&r can be used to connect two mechanical components such that the rotation of one rotates the other."
		""
		"When two mechanical components are connected to each other by a shaft, any &2rotational force&r provided to either component will be provided to the other component in addition to that &dspeed&r. As such, if both components provide stress, this can cause the machine to become overstressed."
	]
	quest.0E5FC39E6C71A872.quest_subtitle: "The shaft is a basic mechanical component in Create. "
	quest.0E5FC39E6C71A872.title: "&l&6Shaft"
	quest.0E78B1230C3C72FF.quest_desc: ["Right-click and drag on the Throttle Lever to set its position. The lever stays where you leave it and outputs a steady analog signal, perfect for engine power, propeller pitch, or burner intensity. Right-clicking with a Wrench inverts the output, so the same physical position can mean full or zero depending on configuration."]
	quest.0E78B1230C3C72FF.quest_subtitle: "A compact, hand-set lever that emits a precise analog Redstone signal."
	quest.0EE2E9EB6DC01E34.quest_desc: ["Crafted via sequenced assembly: place a Golden Sheet on a Depot, then deploy Iron Nuggets, Cogwheels, and Iron Sheets onto it in the right order while it travels along a belt. The Precision Mechanism is the key component for the Mechanical Crafter, the Rolling Mill, Trains, and many other advanced Create blocks."]
	quest.0EE2E9EB6DC01E34.quest_subtitle: "The Precision Mechanism is one of many Crafting Components."
	quest.0EE6A2DA8CC33480.quest_desc: [
		"This metal is used in several alloys, such as adamant and energite, and is used in most machines and machine parts."
		""
		"Processing raw nickel or nickel ore in a fragment forge is a good way to get some platinum as a byproduct."
	]
	quest.0EE6A2DA8CC33480.quest_subtitle: "Nickel is one of the first resources you'll need to gather in Oritech. Nickel ores generate in the overworld between Y -65 and Y 40."
	quest.0F19A5ECCE602889.quest_desc: ["Right-click the controller block of a multiblock structure to form it. Also rotates machines and blocks. On an Anvil, use it to hammer ingots into metal plates."]
	quest.0F19A5ECCE602889.quest_subtitle: "The primary tool of any Immersive Engineer."
	quest.0F35B4F66DCE25F2.quest_desc: ["Produced through complex processing involving nuclear-era materials. Required for quantum-tier components, the Gravichestplate, and high-end cables."]
	quest.0F35B4F66DCE25F2.quest_subtitle: "An exotic metal with zero electrical resistance."
	quest.0F5EE9AA42AAC393.quest_desc: ["Used to build the outer shell of any reactor multiblock. Reactor walls withstand enormous heat and pressure, keeping radiation and damage contained if something goes wrong."]
	quest.0F5EE9AA42AAC393.quest_subtitle: "The blast-resistant casing that must enclose a nuclear reactor."
	quest.0F8A0BCA29114A38.quest_desc: [
		"When fragmenting raw ores, the fragment forge always outputs one ore clump and 3 additional small ore clumps of the same type. It also creates 3 small clumps of a different resource as byproduct."
		""
		"The production of these byproducts can be doubled by attaching a yield addon to the machine. Only 1 yield addon is supported."
	]
	quest.0F8A0BCA29114A38.quest_subtitle: "The fragment forge is a major step in improving the yield of your ore processing chain. Fragmenting ore blocks creates raw ores, and fragmenting raw ores creates ore clumps."
	quest.0FAA13768BE48E5C.quest_desc: ["Crafted by pulverizing ender pearls together with other reagents. Serves as the precursor material for Enderic Lenses, which in turn unlock the Enderic Laser and long-range Oritech tools."]
	quest.0FAA13768BE48E5C.quest_subtitle: "A stable compound infused with the teleportation properties of the End."
	quest.0FB5D3D6F3B72C89.quest_desc: ["Crafted in a Basin by mixing seeds, sugar, and water with heat from a Blaze Burner. Bioethanol can be burned in the Diesel Generator from Create: Crafts \\& Additions for steady FE/RF power generation, providing a fully renewable electric source."]
	quest.0FB5D3D6F3B72C89.quest_subtitle: "A renewable liquid fuel produced by fermenting plant matter into ethanol."
	quest.0FFBE9E17B891A03.quest_desc: ["Printed in the Inscriber using an Engineering Processor Press found in meteorite loot. Combine the printed circuit with printed silicon in the Inscriber to make the final Engineering Processor."]
	quest.0FFBE9E17B891A03.quest_subtitle: "The Engineering Processor is required for the most advanced AE2 devices, including the Drive and Dense Cables."
	quest.108BCD0312837D00.quest_desc: ["Each tier adds a bigger internal RF reserve, letting machines ride out power dips from intermittent sources like solar panels or low-priority generators."]
	quest.108BCD0312837D00.quest_subtitle: "Higher-tier capacitor addons from Oritech Things for larger internal energy buffers."
	quest.108BCD0312837D00.title: "More Capacity"
	quest.10D3487EA2B6F95C.quest_desc: ["Right-click any network component to inspect its channel allocation and connected devices. Holds 9 upgrade card slots that are accessible from any device's interface while the tool is in your inventory."]
	quest.10D3487EA2B6F95C.quest_subtitle: "A diagnostic tool that shows channel usage, device connections, and network information."
	quest.10EDEA4D89FB7865.quest_desc: ["Crafted with stainless steel plates and electronic circuit components. Combines with silicon wafers and other parts in the Assembler to produce Digital Circuits for HV-tier machines."]
	quest.10EDEA4D89FB7865.quest_subtitle: "The HV-tier board used in Digital Circuit assembly."
	quest.1104570BF68AD415.quest_desc: ["Smelts any vanilla furnace recipe using EU instead of fuel, overclocking up to 32 EU/t. Pair it with Assemblers and item pipes for hands-free smelting of any material."]
	quest.1104570BF68AD415.quest_subtitle: "An electric-powered replacement for the vanilla furnace."
	quest.11178481529B6D01.title: "Overclock: Endless Automation"
	quest.111DE9EC42E7AFEE.quest_desc: ["Produced by energizing Steel Ingots in the Energizing Orb. Core crafting material for all Powah tiers."]
	quest.111DE9EC42E7AFEE.quest_subtitle: "Energized Steel"
	quest.1126E6CB8E90C171.quest_desc: ["One of the five basic components required to craft Analog Circuits. Assembled from carbon, copper wires, and rubber sheets."]
	quest.1126E6CB8E90C171.quest_subtitle: "A passive electronic component that limits current in circuits."
	quest.11DD34E91AE6B53B.quest_desc: ["Access stored fluids directly from the item in your inventory. Insert it into a Drive or Chest to synchronize its contents with the network."]
	quest.11DD34E91AE6B53B.quest_subtitle: "A portable ME Fluid Cell that stores liquids and can be accessed without a network connection."
	quest.11DD34E91AE6B53B.title: "ME Portable Fluid Cell"
	quest.11F60954825FEF2B.quest_desc: ["Insert into an Export Bus to request a craft from the network if the target item is unavailable. Also enables Level Emitters to trigger crafting at set thresholds. Requires the Advanced Card to craft."]
	quest.11F60954825FEF2B.quest_subtitle: "Allows Export Buses and Level Emitters to trigger autocrafting when an item is not in stock."
	quest.121F07DA327BC0E6.quest_desc: ["Each piece of the Quantum Armor set grants a 25% chance to fully nullify incoming damage. Wear the complete set to become immune to all damage and gain creative-style flight."]
	quest.121F07DA327BC0E6.quest_subtitle: "Endgame head armor, part of the full Quantum set."
	quest.124C78D84A86D64B.quest_desc: [
		"Extenders must be attached directly to the machine or to another connected extender. The maximum number of extenders a machine can support is determined by its Machine Core quality. Higher quality cores allow more complex and layered addon setups."
		""
		"The machine quality can be viewed in the top-left of the machine UI when hovering over the machine core icon."
	]
	quest.124C78D84A86D64B.quest_subtitle: "The Machine Addon Extender is used to increase the number of available addon slots for a machine. By itself, it does not provide any bonuses, but it lets you place more addons than the machine's base quality would normally allow."
	quest.1252B455DCF21453.quest_desc: ["Right-click a connector with the coil to string a wire to another connector. LV wires carry up to 2,048 IF/t over 16 blocks with 1.25% loss. Use insulated variants in player-accessible areas to prevent shock."]
	quest.1252B455DCF21453.quest_subtitle: "Copper wire coil for the LV (Low Voltage) power tier."
	quest.127610CE7CD5B2F5.quest_desc: ["Place next to a Pattern Provider to receive ingredients and return results automatically. Multiple Assemblers on one Provider all receive work simultaneously. Supports Speed Card upgrades."]
	quest.127610CE7CD5B2F5.quest_subtitle: "Executes individual crafting steps as instructed by adjacent Pattern Providers."
	quest.128D626EAF2986EA.quest_desc: ["The mob type is determined by the first entity that walks over the controller. This type can only be changed by breaking and replacing the controller. Once a mob type is set, the controller will highlight the required size of the spawner cage needed underneath it."]
	quest.128D626EAF2986EA.quest_subtitle: "The Spawner Controller controls the automated mob spawning system. When placed above a spawner cage, it can be used to spawn specific mob types."
	quest.12E87700B0003145.quest_desc: ["Carries the exact redstone signal strength from input to output. Link tunnels with the Memory Card: sneak-right-click the input, then right-click the output to bind them."]
	quest.12E87700B0003145.quest_subtitle: "Transmits redstone signals between two points through the ME Network."
	quest.135D6B0AC9FE2478.quest_desc: ["It is the base material for Silicon Wafers and Fluid Pipes. It is also used in Machine Redstone Addons and Fertilizers."]
	quest.135D6B0AC9FE2478.quest_subtitle: "A purified semi-metal used in electronics and advanced computing. It is based on sand and quartz."
	quest.135E27A19B935CD7.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click the chain of a Chain Conveyor to set the frogport’s target, then place the frogport. Frogports can be placed up to 4 blocks to the side and down from their target chain."
		""
		"The frogport will only take packages that match its address. The address can be set by right-clicking the placed frogport or in it's UI. "
		""
		"The frogport will only send packages that don’t match its address unless its set to “only send packages” in its UI."
	]
	quest.135E27A19B935CD7.quest_subtitle: "Package Frogports are used to move Cardboard Packages from and to Chain Conveyors."
	quest.14518E2BE509FE9E.quest_desc: ["An essential tool for managing your ME Network. Breaking AE2 blocks with this wrench keeps your items safely inside the block rather than dropping them."]
	quest.14518E2BE509FE9E.quest_subtitle: "Rotates and disassembles AE2 machines without causing item drops."
	quest.1458BE6B3726A232.quest_desc: ["The Spirited Capacitor enables one of the highest tiers in Powah. Spirited components require rare materials but deliver exceptional performance."]
	quest.1458BE6B3726A232.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Tier Unlocked"
	quest.146E9675E4C747C9.quest_desc: ["Power via AE cables or FE from the top or bottom faces. Each accelerator speeds growth by roughly 90x additively. Leave some faces of the budding block uncovered to maximize crystal yield."]
	quest.146E9675E4C747C9.quest_subtitle: "Greatly accelerates the growth rate of adjacent Budding Certus blocks and other plants."
	quest.147FC2959F9FC5F5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Trains&r are &3&3Contraptions&r&r that travel on Train Tracks."
		""
		"Assembly"
		"1) Place the track and right-click it with a station block. Place the station block near the track."
		""
		"2) Right click on the station and select \"Create Train\" to enter assembly mode (blue flag shown on station)."
		""
		"3) Place one or more Train Casings on the track where indicated with blue. The casings will turn into bogeys."
		""
		"4) When assembled, each bogey will automatically become coupled together as part of the train."
		" "
		"5) Place a Train Controls block facing the direction dictated by the station. Place a Seat or Blaze Burner behind the controls for the driver."
		""
		"6) Use Block Attachment Utilities such as Super Glue to connect all parts together (green highlight)."
		""
		"7) When finished, use the Station's interface to attempt to assemble the Train. If a Train fails to assemble, an error will be shown in the Station's interface. Common errors are detailed below."
	]
	quest.147FC2959F9FC5F5.quest_subtitle: "Train Casings are used for locomotive transportation."
	quest.14F476F9E4DA66F7.quest_desc: ["Crafted via Blueprint at the Engineer's Workbench. Used in Electronic Components, Circuit Boards, and various weapons. A key ingredient for mid-game electrical progression."]
	quest.14F476F9E4DA66F7.quest_subtitle: "A vacuum tube used in electrical components and weapons."
	quest.1505A258938D0BEE.quest_desc: ["Produced by electrolyzing Manganese Sulfuric Solution. Nine tiny dusts combine into one full dust, required in the stainless steel alloy recipe."]
	quest.1505A258938D0BEE.quest_subtitle: "A small amount of manganese, used to craft stainless steel."
	quest.15463C9BF0ED728A.quest_desc: ["Hand-craft 2 iron ingots with 2 coal for a slow start, or set up a pulverizer plus foundry for far better efficiency. Steel is used in huge quantities once multiblock construction begins."]
	quest.15463C9BF0ED728A.quest_subtitle: "A core Oritech alloy used across most machine and structural recipes."
	quest.1552DB72D35B6E47.quest_desc: [
		"Features"
		"-Unbreakable: This tool does not have durability and will never break."
		""
		"-Extended Reach: Grants additional block and entity interaction range when held."
		""
		"-Dual Modes: You can toggle between two modes by pressing Shift + Right-Click."
	]
	quest.1552DB72D35B6E47.quest_subtitle: "The Prometheum Pickaxe is an unbreakable high-tier mining tool. It has very high mining speed and can switch between area mining and silk touch harvesting."
	quest.155C8ED420FB96A0.quest_desc: ["Items dropped near the player are pulled directly into ME Network storage. Toggle the magnet on or off from the terminal interface. Requires the Advanced Card to craft."]
	quest.155C8ED420FB96A0.quest_subtitle: "Adds a magnet to the wireless terminal that automatically picks up nearby dropped items into the network."
	quest.1578CD99BF62B9DF.quest_desc: ["Maximum throughput cables. Use Nitro cables to connect your highest-tier generators and eliminate any transfer bottlenecks in your network."]
	quest.1578CD99BF62B9DF.quest_subtitle: "Maximum Transfer Cables"
	quest.15792F2259536F4F.quest_desc: ["Generates FE from sunlight. Needs a clear line of sight to the sky — any block above it halts production. Place it in the open for consistent passive power."]
	quest.15792F2259536F4F.quest_subtitle: "Solar Powered"
	quest.157E2E320FABF1CC.quest_desc: ["The most powerful Powah crystal. Required to craft all Nitro tier components."]
	quest.157E2E320FABF1CC.quest_subtitle: "Nitro Crystal"
	quest.1599CB66B5FF9631.quest_desc: ["Every multiblock needs hatches to receive steam, water, or other fluids and to eject fluid byproducts. Place them on the multiblock's frame instead of a casing block."]
	quest.1599CB66B5FF9631.quest_subtitle: "Input and output hatches that move fluids in and out of multiblocks."
	quest.1599CB66B5FF9631.title: "Bronze Fluid Hatch"
	quest.15EB55A74D9E45FF.quest_desc: ["Required for the Fusion Reactor, Plasma Turbine, and other endgame multiblocks. Right-click any machine with it to upgrade the machine to quantum tier and its cable interface to the highest voltage."]
	quest.15EB55A74D9E45FF.quest_subtitle: "The ultimate machine hull, built from Quantum Circuits."
	quest.1628EA94239174BF.quest_desc: ["A pressed plate of cadmium, beryllium, and Blastproof Alloy. Used in Nuclear Casings and Nuclear Hatches — the core structural blocks of the Nuclear Reactor."]
	quest.1628EA94239174BF.quest_subtitle: "A dense plate resistant to heat and radiation."
	quest.1640E9FAB3710E00.quest_desc: ["Operates like a standard refinery but accepts recipes involving unholy intelligence and other rare inputs. Needed for some of the mod's more exotic fluid chains."]
	quest.1640E9FAB3710E00.quest_subtitle: "A corrupted variant of the refinery used for special processing chains."
	quest.1674D9532E8AE19C.quest_desc: ["Wirelessly charges items in a linked player's inventory — including armor and offhand — anywhere in the same dimension. Bind it with a Binding Card."]
	quest.1674D9532E8AE19C.quest_subtitle: "Wireless Charging"
	quest.16B623EFDB934ADB.quest_desc: [
		"&4&lNuclear Reactor&r&r"
		"&a&lParticle Accelerator&r&r"
		"&5&lAtomic Forge&r&r"
		"&0&lA Singularity&r&r"
	]
	quest.17133BDB056D6AE9.quest_desc: ["Burns furnace fuels to generate FE at a much higher rate than the Hardened Furnator. Energy per fuel unit stays the same — generation speed is what increases."]
	quest.17133BDB056D6AE9.quest_subtitle: "Blazing Furnace Power"
	quest.177C0E37A35A14F4.quest_desc: [
		"When Powered by kinetics:"
		""
		"Starts rotating the attached structure towards the current hour. If an independent second structure exists in front of the first one, it will serve as the minute hand."
		""
		"The Value Settings Screen can be accessed from the side of the block, and can be used to change the order of the hands or switch to a 24-hour reading resembling the Clock item."
	]
	quest.177C0E37A35A14F4.quest_subtitle: "The Clockwork Bearing is an advanced version of the Mechanical Bearing for rotating up to two clock hands according to the current in-game time."
	quest.179612CD2067008D.quest_desc: ["Near top-tier Energizing Rod. With several Spirited Rods placed around the Orb, most recipes can be processed near-instantly."]
	quest.179612CD2067008D.quest_subtitle: "Near-Max Throughput"
	quest.17E0F7A3AB88C7B0.quest_desc: ["Crafted with aluminum plates and copper wires. Combines with other components in the Assembler to form Electronic Circuits for MV-tier machinery."]
	quest.17E0F7A3AB88C7B0.quest_subtitle: "The aluminum-based board used for MV-tier circuits."
	quest.1837076B0EA3C11A.quest_desc: [
		"A Mechanical Belt is a mechanical component that conveys rotation and moves items and entities."
		""
		"Placing a Belt requires at least two &6Shafts&r. Place the Belt by right-clicking on the first shaft and then right clicking the second. Regardless of the length, this only consumes one mechanical belt. Both shafts must face the same direction."
		""
		"A Mechanical Belt can be placed over any number of Shafts arranged horizontally, vertically, or diagonally (45° towards the y axis) in a single line, provided that no obstructions are present and that the total length is no longer than twenty blocks. The Mechanical Belt also require that the two shafts face the same direction."
	]
	quest.1837076B0EA3C11A.quest_subtitle: "Used to connect two parallel Shafts with a Mechanical Belt for transferring rotation and moving items."
	quest.18534D85674467A2.quest_desc: ["Right-click while standing next to a Fluid Tank, or while holding a bucket of a drinkable liquid, to consume it. Useful for drinking Liquid Experience, potion fluids, milk, honey, or other custom drinkable fluids added by Create addons."]
	quest.18534D85674467A2.quest_subtitle: "A simple drinking straw for sipping fluids straight out of a tank or bucket."
	quest.18594A0013B696D4.quest_desc: ["By default the signal is emitted on the downhill side. The value boxes configure the angle that corresponds to a full 15-strength signal and can invert the output direction. Each axis is read independently, so a single Gimbal Sensor can drive separate auto-leveling circuits for tilt and roll on the same airship."]
	quest.18594A0013B696D4.quest_subtitle: "Outputs analog Redstone based on the Contraption's pitch, roll, and yaw."
	quest.187211CD5B4C5488.quest_desc: ["Heat vented per tick scales with the temperature of the adjacent block — hotter neighbors are cooled faster. Cheap and ice-free, vents are the backbone of most small reactor designs."]
	quest.187211CD5B4C5488.quest_subtitle: "A passive cooling component that removes heat from its hottest neighbor."
	quest.187A33B12FCCFE75.quest_desc: ["Wirelessly charges a linked player's items at a high rate. At this tier it can keep pace with most high-power tools during play."]
	quest.187A33B12FCCFE75.quest_subtitle: "Niotic Wireless Charger"
	quest.18A6C13EDFF60CAF.quest_desc: ["Consumes 800 IF per shot. Use Steel Rods, Iron Rods, or other metal items as projectiles. Damage scales with the projectile material. Upgrade with Heatsinks (faster charge) and a Scope (zoom) at the Engineer's Workbench."]
	quest.18A6C13EDFF60CAF.quest_subtitle: "An electromagnetic railgun that fires metal rods at high velocity."
	quest.18C950FD6B1095E4.quest_desc: ["Uses the same structure as the Steam Quarry but is powered by EU instead of steam, so it overclocks for much faster ore production. Consumes drills while running."]
	quest.18C950FD6B1095E4.quest_subtitle: "The electric upgrade of the Steam Quarry."
	quest.190E3832116C398A.quest_desc: ["Compresses ingots into plates at a 1:1 ratio and doubles output from double ingots. Almost every Steam Age recipe needs plates, making this the first bronze machine you should build."]
	quest.190E3832116C398A.quest_subtitle: "A steam machine that turns ingots into plates."
	quest.193DB50FA4DAE2C6.quest_desc: ["Pylons must form closed rectangles on each axis to define the capture volume. Each continuous line of pylons uses 1 network channel. A minimum of 2 pylons per line is required."]
	quest.193DB50FA4DAE2C6.quest_subtitle: "Defines the boundaries of the spatial field used for Spatial IO capture operations."
	quest.194A90AFBE502859.quest_desc: ["Import Buses pull items in from adjacent inventories, Export Buses push items out, and Storage Buses expose external inventories as network storage. Combine them with upgrade cards for precise control."]
	quest.194A90AFBE502859.quest_subtitle: "Buses connect your ME Network to the outside world, importing, exporting, and accessing external storage."
	quest.1956D5445A6C0348.quest_desc: ["Swap this in when your machines start running out of addon slots. Each tier increases the total number of addons and extender layers a multiblock can handle."]
	quest.1956D5445A6C0348.quest_subtitle: "A high-quality machine core for late-midgame multiblocks."
	quest.19754AE8C11A6317.quest_desc: ["Insert a tool, weapon, or block into the Deployer to give it something to use. It will attack mobs, place blocks, harvest crops, fill buckets, or perform crafting recipes when items are dropped on it from above. A Funnel above can be used to feed it items automatically."]
	quest.19754AE8C11A6317.quest_subtitle: "The Deployer punches and uses items just like a player would, when given Rotational Force."
	quest.197AB0E07A40512F.quest_desc: ["Place a Water Wheel adjacent to flowing water on as many sides as possible to maximize its rotational output. The Large Water Wheel is a 3x3 multiblock that produces significantly more Rotational Force than the small one."]
	quest.197AB0E07A40512F.quest_subtitle: "The Water Wheel is a source of rotational power. It generates Rotational Force when water flows over it."
	quest.19D9034316B75460.quest_desc: ["The Basic Rod offers higher I/O than the Starter. Multiple rods placed around the Energizing Orb stack their throughput for faster crafting."]
	quest.19D9034316B75460.quest_subtitle: "More Power Per Rod"
	quest.1B04A295850D0F00.quest_desc: ["Place adjacent to a Train Track to detect when a Train passes over it. The Track Observer emits a Redstone signal that can be filtered to react to specific Trains, cargo, or schedule entries."]
	quest.1B04A295850D0F00.quest_subtitle: "The Train Observer is used to detect passing Trains."
	quest.1B1874D974567D5F.quest_desc: ["The best core available in Oritech. Ideal for fully loaded machines that rely on several extender layers and a complete set of addons."]
	quest.1B1874D974567D5F.quest_subtitle: "The top-tier machine core, offering the maximum multiblock quality."
	quest.1BB4767075B9534E.quest_desc: ["Feed it Wheat, Potatoes, Sugar Cane, or other plant matter. Ethanol produced here is combined with Plant Oil (from the Squeezer) in the Refinery to produce Biodiesel. Keep this chain automated for a steady fuel supply."]
	quest.1BB4767075B9534E.quest_subtitle: "Converts crops into Ethanol for Biodiesel production."
	quest.1C032D0D0A89C70E.quest_desc: ["Craft it with a Book and a Lever. The manual contains construction diagrams for every multiblock, machine recipes, and wiring guides. Keep it in your hotbar at all times."]
	quest.1C032D0D0A89C70E.quest_subtitle: "The Engineer's Manual — your essential in-game reference."
	quest.1C1750EF62B5F965.quest_desc: ["Insert into an Import or Export Bus to expand the number of filter entries up to 5 cards. More filter slots make it easier to manage selective automation without needing multiple buses."]
	quest.1C1750EF62B5F965.quest_subtitle: "Adds extra filter slots to AE2 devices, allowing more precise whitelists or blacklists."
	quest.1C4BF710A2F8C7A6.quest_desc: ["Produced by combining speed and efficiency addons of the same tier. Less aggressive than pure speed addons but much easier to sustain in always-on machines."]
	quest.1C4BF710A2F8C7A6.quest_subtitle: "Hybrid addons that increase speed while mitigating part of the extra energy cost."
	quest.1C4BF710A2F8C7A6.title: "Efficiency and Speed"
	quest.1C9DE408C1A1246B.quest_desc: ["Place it once on any wall of the reactor. Right-click the controller to assemble or re-check the structure, and use its UI to monitor fuel, heat, and energy output."]
	quest.1C9DE408C1A1246B.quest_subtitle: "The brain of the nuclear reactor multiblock."
	quest.1C9DE408C1A1246B.title: "&4&lNuclear Reactor&r&r"
	quest.1CC319979AA132AB.quest_desc: ["Using the raw power of the Schrödinger equation, any entity struck is instantly killed. The definitive endgame weapon of Modern Industrialization."]
	quest.1CC319979AA132AB.quest_subtitle: "A quantum weapon that instantly vaporizes any target."
	quest.1CDCAC69B9D62348.quest_desc: ["Converts each mb of regular steam into 1 EU and each mb of HP steam into 8 EU, producing up to 16,384 EU/t. Note that it does not return any water — pair it with a Heat Exchanger to recycle HP water."]
	quest.1CDCAC69B9D62348.quest_subtitle: "A multiblock turbine accepting both regular and HP steam."
	quest.1D99B9B0CBE267E0.quest_desc: ["Produced in a Chemical Reactor and used to dissolve manganese-bearing materials and refine oils. A core midgame chemistry fluid."]
	quest.1D99B9B0CBE267E0.quest_subtitle: "A strong acid produced in the Chemical Reactor."
	quest.1DA2A4200ED6542F.quest_desc: ["Insert into a Wireless Terminal after linking it to a Quantum Bridge to maintain wireless access from anywhere without range restrictions. Requires the Advanced Card to craft."]
	quest.1DA2A4200ED6542F.quest_subtitle: "Links your wireless terminal to an ME Network across unlimited distances, even between dimensions."
	quest.1DBA8DD396081924.quest_desc: ["The Interfaces must be placed facing each other at 1-2 blocks apart, one on a Contraption with Fluid Tanks and one stationary. A Fluid Pump is required to insert or extract liquid from the Contraption. To pump liquids to another tank, simply connect the stationary interface and the fluid tank with fluid pipes, although pumps are required to move the liquids."]
	quest.1DBA8DD396081924.quest_subtitle: "The Portable Fluid Interface is used to insert or extract from the fluid inventory of a Contraption."
	quest.1E07FBD17CE427D9.quest_desc: ["Used to safely hold volatile materials such as nuclear fuels, explosives, and black hole components. Required in the recipes of the mod's most hazardous items."]
	quest.1E07FBD17CE427D9.quest_subtitle: "A reinforced container for transporting dangerous endgame items."
	quest.1E22AF3E3AF63D3E.quest_desc: ["Obtained by compressing iridium ingots. A rare, dense plate required for the Quantum Circuit Board and other endgame crafts."]
	quest.1E22AF3E3AF63D3E.quest_subtitle: "A plate of extremely dense precious metal."
	quest.1E6756594847F70D.quest_desc: ["The Energizing Orb processes special recipes using FE. Place at least one Energizing Rod within 9 blocks, connect it to a power source, then right-click the Orb with the recipe ingredients."]
	quest.1E6756594847F70D.quest_subtitle: "The Energizing Setup"
	quest.1E6756594847F70D.title: "Energizing"
	quest.1E7FE1C207ACA95F.quest_desc: ["This 3x5x1 multiblock uses interchangeable Molds to press components. Available molds: Plate, Rod, Wire, Gear, Bullet Casing, and Packing. Automate with conveyors — items fall in from above and exit to the side."]
	quest.1E7FE1C207ACA95F.quest_subtitle: "Stamps ingots into plates, rods, wires, and other shapes."
	quest.1EB7B268E95308DC.quest_desc: ["Produces plates, double plates, and many more shapes far faster than the Bronze Compressor. Overclocks automatically up to 32 EU/t on LV."]
	quest.1EB7B268E95308DC.quest_subtitle: "The LV-tier electric version of the Bronze Compressor."
	quest.1F12AF347184699F.quest_desc: ["Adds extra capacity to the machine's energy storage. Stack several to let machines keep running longer after power loss, or to absorb spikes from fast generators."]
	quest.1F12AF347184699F.quest_subtitle: "Increases the internal RF buffer of a machine."
	quest.1F47050EF1B2DD29.quest_desc: ["Place the Transformer between your LV and MV wire networks to step voltage up or down. LV enters on the small coil side; MV exits from the large coil side. A Screwdriver reverses the direction if needed."]
	quest.1F47050EF1B2DD29.quest_subtitle: "Converts LV power to MV and vice versa."
	quest.1FDBB75ECD39FB24.quest_desc: [
		"The Item Drain can hold up to 1500mb of fluid at a time. A Fluid Pump is needed to extract the fluid."
		""
		"A Basin will automatically deposit output fluids into an Item Drain placed near it."
	]
	quest.1FDBB75ECD39FB24.quest_subtitle: "The Item Drain drains fluid from items such as buckets and bottles inserted onto it."
	quest.1FDD66162316013C.quest_desc: ["Build a hollow rectangular frame with Treated Wood Fences, minimum 3x3x3, then right-click the bottom center with the Hammer. Scale it up as needed for large fluid reserves. Essential for buffering Biodiesel and other process fluids."]
	quest.1FDD66162316013C.quest_subtitle: "Bulk fluid storage in a scalable multiblock tank."
	quest.2030693D3DAA8894.quest_desc: ["Combines qubits, cooling cells, and a quantum circuit board. Required for the Quantum Machine Hull and every quantum upgrade or piece of endgame equipment."]
	quest.2030693D3DAA8894.quest_subtitle: "The endgame circuit used in all quantum-tier machinery."
	quest.205FB8637491CDAE.quest_desc: ["Higher-priority drives fill first and empty last. LED lights on each slot indicate the cell's fill state. Item and fluid cells can be mixed in the same Drive."]
	quest.205FB8637491CDAE.quest_subtitle: "The ME Drive holds up to 10 ME Storage Cells, forming the main physical storage of your network."
	quest.20872740F5F79B26.quest_desc: ["Charges FE items in adjacent inventories at a high rate. Perfect for keeping entire chests of tools or batteries fully charged."]
	quest.20872740F5F79B26.quest_subtitle: "Niotic Item Charging"
	quest.2090C7FA0A352D0E.quest_desc: ["The Nitro Capacitor is the pinnacle of Powah. All Nitro tier components offer maximum capacity and throughput for end-game energy demands."]
	quest.2090C7FA0A352D0E.quest_subtitle: "Nitro Tier: Peak Power"
	quest.20A46CA1B63C7C97.quest_desc: ["Connect to an HV wire network. When active, the Tesla Coil continuously damages all mobs in range. Combine with Redstone Breakers or Breaker Switches to control activation. A powerful automated base defense tool."]
	quest.20A46CA1B63C7C97.quest_subtitle: "Electrocutes nearby mobs when powered."
	quest.20D210486DF2504E.quest_desc: ["Insert into an Import or Export Bus to enable fuzzy matching. Supports four modes: Ignore All, Match Damage, Match NBT, Match Both. Requires the Advanced Card to craft."]
	quest.20D210486DF2504E.quest_subtitle: "Allows AE2 devices to match items regardless of damage value or NBT data."
	quest.20E81D9330FA1564.quest_desc: ["Once your Contraption can move, you need to control it. The blocks unlocked here cover the human-side inputs (Steering Wheel, Throttle Lever, Linked Typewriter), together with sensors and wireless link blocks that turn the Contraption's state into Redstone, and Docking Connectors for joining two ships into one rigid structure."]
	quest.20E81D9330FA1564.quest_subtitle: "Navigation: the cockpit blocks used to actually pilot, instrument, and bind together a Contraption."
	quest.2134C15C42E7C1CD.quest_desc: ["Carries significantly more fluid per tick than a standard pipe. Useful for the main arteries of a refinery or reactor coolant loop, where regular pipes bottleneck."]
	quest.2134C15C42E7C1CD.quest_subtitle: "A dense bundle of fluid pipes with increased transfer rate."
	quest.21A830CC8DAD6566.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a Train Track, then place the Station within 15 blocks of the track. It can only create Trains if placed on a straight Track, and Bogeys may only be placed on a 3 block long straight track."
		""
		"In the interface, the Station can be named; these names are how non-player conducted Trains will identify stations. A conductor cannot be instructed to navigate to a station that is named the same as the station they are currently at, and will otherwise choose the closest accessible station out of multiple stations with the same name."
		""
		"The name will also show up on a Map if it is used on the station, similarly to Banners."
	]
	quest.21A830CC8DAD6566.quest_subtitle: "Train Stations are used to create, disassemble, and guide Trains."
	quest.21B40BEC30B40491.quest_desc: [
		"While held, funnels prevent the player from accessing inventories, instead placing them. Sneak right clicking with a Funnel places it in input mode."
		""
		"Using a Wrench on the funnel switches it between input and output mode. Redstone can be applied to stop the funnel from inputting or outputting. Right-clicking a funnel on a Mechanical Belt causes it to extend one block forward."
	]
	quest.21B40BEC30B40491.quest_subtitle: "The Andesite Funnel is used to extract or insert materials into inventories, similar in nature to the Brass Funnel."
	quest.21B40BEC30B40491.title: "Funnels"
	quest.21CE50730E9BA0B3.quest_desc: ["The highest-tier crafting storage. Ideal for deeply recursive or complex autocrafting chains that involve many different intermediate materials."]
	quest.21CE50730E9BA0B3.quest_subtitle: "Provides 256k bytes of crafting storage to the ME Crafting CPU."
	quest.21DB908D7DFAAD84.quest_desc: ["Functions as a normal conveyor belt but pauses when redstone-powered. Use it to create buffer zones, timed release gates, or controlled item flow between machines in automated production lines."]
	quest.21DB908D7DFAAD84.quest_subtitle: "Stops item movement when a redstone signal is received."
	quest.223202251340B498.quest_desc: ["Transfers huge amounts of FE through the Ender Network. Ideal for large-scale distributed power grids spanning multiple areas."]
	quest.223202251340B498.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Ender Network"
	quest.224113E3E4EFED0D.quest_desc: ["Oritech is a tech mod featuring many new machines and tools. Content ranges from processing machines, world interaction machines, logistical parts, new features integrated into world generation, equipment, and more. Machines are mostly animated multiblocks, with upgrades being implemented using addon blocks."]
	quest.224113E3E4EFED0D.quest_subtitle: "A technology-focused mod, with animated machinery, diverse processing options, and plenty of new mechanics and equipment"
	quest.228124D466758B61.quest_desc: ["Interfaces can automatically stock items from the network and act as bridges between subnets. Subnetworks let you isolate storage, save channels, and build modular automation systems."]
	quest.228124D466758B61.quest_subtitle: "Your network is ready for subnetworks and advanced logistics."
	quest.228CD1314315A9E9.quest_desc: ["Light, RS, and Heavy Engineering Blocks are the structural components used to build the Diesel Generator and other late-game multiblocks. The Generator and Radiator blocks are the functional cores of the Diesel Generator."]
	quest.228CD1314315A9E9.quest_subtitle: "Core structural blocks for IE's large multiblock machines."
	quest.228CD1314315A9E9.title: "Multiblocks Blocks"
	quest.22ADEF33B5CE9504.quest_desc: ["Equip the Jetpack in the chestplate slot. Hold the &eJump&r key to ascend and Sneak to descend. Refill its compressed air at a Banktank station or by inserting filled air bottles. Air consumption increases with vertical speed and altitude."]
	quest.22ADEF33B5CE9504.quest_subtitle: "An air-powered jetpack from Create: Jetpack — fly using compressed air stored in its built-in Banktank."
	quest.2380F699DCA74863.quest_desc: ["Right-click a Capacitor with the Voltmeter to read its stored energy level. Also displays wire loss and other diagnostic info when clicked on wires. An essential diagnostic tool for troubleshooting power networks."]
	quest.2380F699DCA74863.quest_subtitle: "Measures the energy stored in a connected Capacitor."
	quest.23A9A2D399A7BF94.quest_desc: [
		"The Elevator Pulley moves much like the Rope Pulley and shares certain functionalities. Unlike the Rope Pulley, it can phase through blocks, and will not turn back into blocks unless the Pulley is right-clicked."
		""
		"An Elevator Pulley requires a single horizontal Redstone Contact to be on the contraption in order to assemble. If more than one is added, the Elevator will not assemble. If either of these conditions are not met, a corresponding error message will be displayed while looking at the Elevator Pulley."
	]
	quest.23A9A2D399A7BF94.quest_subtitle: "An Elevator Pulley is a Contraption useful for creating multi-floor elevators easily."
	quest.23E8AF1037E20880.quest_desc: ["The Niotic Reactor produces much more FE per Uraninite than lower tiers. Build the 3x4 multiblock with 36 Niotic Reactor blocks for high-output nuclear power."]
	quest.23E8AF1037E20880.quest_subtitle: "Niotic Nuclear Power"
	quest.24CB634D4A52A13E.quest_desc: [
		"Beyond basic ore processing, the pulverizer is commonly used to grind biomass for generators or produce coal dust for carbon composite materials."
		""
		"Small dusts in the output slots will be auto-combined if possible."
	]
	quest.24CB634D4A52A13E.quest_subtitle: "The pulverizer is a slow and simple block that crushes ores and biomass into dust."
	quest.24D36EEF14875117.quest_desc: ["Assembled from enderic compound, adamant, and a processing unit. Acts as the focusing element for every Oritech laser and for several vision-related player augments."]
	quest.24D36EEF14875117.quest_subtitle: "Enderic lenses are compact parts used in sensors, lasers, and vision augments."
	quest.24DDED464AE48E05.quest_desc: ["Place between two Shafts to control rotation. Without Redstone, it transmits rotation normally. When powered by Redstone, the rotation direction is reversed without affecting speed."]
	quest.24DDED464AE48E05.quest_subtitle: "Reverses outgoing Rotational Force when a Redstone signal is applied."
	quest.24E110DD6901A761.quest_desc: ["Place it next to a pipe that already has extraction enabled, then feed it RF. The more power available, the faster items or fluids are drawn out of the connected inventory."]
	quest.24E110DD6901A761.quest_subtitle: "The Pipe Booster is an upgrade for high-throughput logistics networks. When placed adjacent to a pipe extraction point and powered with RF, it massively increases the speed at which items and fluids are pulled from a connected inventory."
	quest.24F3C167EF240473.quest_desc: ["One input tunnel can distribute to multiple outputs for item routing. Link tunnels with the Memory Card: sneak-right-click the input, right-click each output. Each ME P2P tunnel pair uses 1 channel."]
	quest.24F3C167EF240473.quest_subtitle: "Transfers items between two points in the network without using separate item transport."
	quest.25204D6C0F67747A.quest_desc: ["Smelts at the same speed as a vanilla furnace but uses steam instead of solid fuel, making it roughly ten times more fuel-efficient when paired with a boiler."]
	quest.25204D6C0F67747A.quest_subtitle: "A steam-powered furnace for efficient smelting."
	quest.25B581A958F22442.quest_desc: ["The Optical Sensor casts an internal beam and emits a Redstone signal whose strength depends on how close the obstructing block is. Adjust the maximum detection distance from the value panel, and apply a filter to restrict it to specific blocks: useful for runway detection, auto-landing, and avoiding nearby walls during flight."]
	quest.25B581A958F22442.quest_subtitle: "Detects the closest block in front of the sensor and reports its distance as Redstone."
	quest.25B5ED085EF3C1A0.quest_desc: ["The Pressurizer consumes energy to make HP steam, but the Large Steam Turbine does not return HP water. The Heat Exchanger recovers HP water from the spent steam so it can be reused, drastically cutting power costs."]
	quest.25B5ED085EF3C1A0.quest_subtitle: "Recovers HP water from spent HP steam for reuse."
	quest.25C4C27A852AEB1A.quest_desc: ["Uraninite is mined underground and used as fuel for the Reactor multiblock. Smelt Uraninite Ore to obtain it."]
	quest.25C4C27A852AEB1A.quest_subtitle: "Nuclear Fuel"
	quest.26FD4BA4B2780AFF.quest_desc: ["Once a region is captured, the cell is permanently assigned those dimensions. Use the Spatial IO Port to store and retrieve spatial contents. Higher-tier cells support larger volumes."]
	quest.26FD4BA4B2780AFF.quest_subtitle: "Stores a 2x2x2 region of physical space captured by the Spatial IO system."
	quest.271132D9BB3DB4C1.quest_desc: ["Drains FE from charged items and sends it to your network. The Blazing version extracts energy at a faster rate than the Hardened one."]
	quest.271132D9BB3DB4C1.quest_subtitle: "Blazing FE Extractor"
	quest.2740D458F64ED143.quest_desc: ["Cables of the same color connect automatically; different colors do not, letting you run parallel lines in the same space. Use Dense Cables when a single run needs more than 8 channels."]
	quest.2740D458F64ED143.quest_subtitle: "The basic AE2 cable, transmitting up to 8 channels and connecting all network devices."
	quest.276AC4E6504EA7E8.quest_desc: ["High-capacity FE buffer. The Niotic Cell can store enough energy to buffer large generators or several machines simultaneously."]
	quest.276AC4E6504EA7E8.quest_subtitle: "High Capacity Buffer"
	quest.2838DAC61BC66E6D.quest_desc: ["Produces copper, tin, and other wires used in cables and electronic components. Combine its output with rubber sheets to craft cables of the matching tier."]
	quest.2838DAC61BC66E6D.quest_subtitle: "A steel multiblock that draws ingots into wires."
	quest.283CCD1DAFB4EF83.quest_desc: ["Insert into an Import or Export Bus to import/export everything except the listed items. A simple way to set up broad automation without enumerating every item individually."]
	quest.283CCD1DAFB4EF83.quest_subtitle: "Inverts the filter list of a device from whitelist to blacklist."
	quest.289AACEC4A871AC9.quest_desc: ["The ultimate wireless charger. Keeps a linked player's entire inventory charged across the whole dimension regardless of tool energy draw."]
	quest.289AACEC4A871AC9.quest_subtitle: "Nitro Wireless Charger"
	quest.28D6BCECF0282EB3.quest_desc: ["Produced in the Chemical Reactor from salt and sulfuric acid. Used to dissolve chromium-bearing compounds for further processing into stainless steel ingredients."]
	quest.28D6BCECF0282EB3.quest_subtitle: "A strong acid produced in the Chemical Reactor."
	quest.294341A06EB742AD.quest_desc: ["Obtained by smelting bauxite dust in the Electric Blast Furnace, or by electrolyzing bauxite first for better yields. Required for every MV-tier machine hull and circuit."]
	quest.294341A06EB742AD.quest_subtitle: "A lightweight metal smelted in the Electric Blast Furnace."
	quest.29B1C295E5FD899B.quest_desc: ["Route power across long distances without running additional power cables. One input tunnel can serve multiple outputs. Link tunnels with the Memory Card."]
	quest.29B1C295E5FD899B.quest_subtitle: "Transmits Forge Energy (RF/FE) between two points via the ME Network."
	quest.2A404708E175235F.quest_desc: [
		"Fluids can be stored and extracted from fluid tanks via Fluid Pipe. The fluid pipes can be placed on any face of the fluid tank: top, bottom, or sides. The window of a tank can be toggled with a Wrench."
		""
		"The direction of flow in the fluid pipe indicates whether fluids will be put into the tank or extracted from the tank; if fluid is flowing towards the tank, the fluid will be stored in the tank. Likewise, if a fluid pipe is flowing away from the tank (via Mechanical Pump), then fluid from the tank will be extracted into that pipe."
	]
	quest.2A404708E175235F.quest_subtitle: "The Fluid Tank is a fluid storage mechanism that can store up to 8 buckets of fluid per block."
	quest.2A41C8154F3E2FBA.quest_desc: ["Fuel ports take in pellets, absorber ports take in ice for active cooling, energy ports push up to 25,000 RF/t each, and redstone ports gate fuel intake or output reactor data to a comparator."]
	quest.2A41C8154F3E2FBA.quest_subtitle: "The input and output ports of the reactor multiblock."
	quest.2A41C8154F3E2FBA.title: "Reactor Ports"
	quest.2A4B2961FF3B9020.quest_desc: ["An ethereal crystal imbued with spiritual energy. Needed to craft Spirited tier components."]
	quest.2A4B2961FF3B9020.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Crystal"
	quest.2A56950F549955A0.quest_desc: ["Search, view, and edit patterns in any connected Pattern Provider without physically accessing each machine. Essential for managing large autocrafting setups."]
	quest.2A56950F549955A0.quest_subtitle: "Displays all patterns stored in Pattern Providers across the network, enabling remote management."
	quest.2A65DC22E1A254FC.quest_desc: ["Place rods inside the reactor and supply pellets through a fuel port directly above each column. More rods per block produce more heat and RF, but require much more cooling to stay stable."]
	quest.2A65DC22E1A254FC.quest_subtitle: "The fuel-burning core of a reactor, available in single, double, and quad variants."
	quest.2A65DC22E1A254FC.title: "Reactor Rod"
	quest.2AFC646EF1E1FFBD.quest_desc: ["Burns hot fluids like lava to generate FE. Higher tiers produce more FE/t but drain fluid faster. Connect a fluid pipe to keep it supplied."]
	quest.2AFC646EF1E1FFBD.quest_subtitle: "Lava-Powered"
	quest.2B39FC965869395C.quest_desc: ["Consumes lava or other hot fluids to produce substantially more FE/t than the Hardened version. Keep a steady fluid supply to sustain it."]
	quest.2B39FC965869395C.quest_subtitle: "Hotter Lava Power"
	quest.2B5535981ED79938.quest_desc: ["Upgrade a regular Jetpack with a Netherite Ingot in a Smithing Table to obtain the Netherite Jetpack. It holds far more compressed air and protects the wearer from fire and lava during long flights."]
	quest.2B5535981ED79938.quest_subtitle: "A reinforced Netherite-tier Jetpack with greater air capacity and full fire resistance."
	quest.2B82FD333EDA0DED.quest_desc: ["Rapidly extracts FE from charged items and sends it to your power network. Useful for recovering energy from stored or spare batteries."]
	quest.2B82FD333EDA0DED.quest_subtitle: "Niotic FE Extractor"
	quest.2BE4057C9F6A8D31.quest_desc: ["Functionally identical to Fluix Glass Cables with 8 channels. Use covered cables for cleaner builds or to reduce visual clutter. Both types share the same color connection system."]
	quest.2BE4057C9F6A8D31.quest_subtitle: "A visually cleaner variant of the glass cable that hides the cable texture inside solid blocks."
	quest.2C75A3D98E9A8BB0.quest_desc: ["A mid-tier spatial cell for larger builds or mob farms. Once a region is captured, the cell is permanently sized. Combine with Spatial Pylons and a Spatial IO Port."]
	quest.2C75A3D98E9A8BB0.quest_subtitle: "Stores a 16x16x16 region of physical space captured by the Spatial IO system."
	quest.2C860AA192FF0116.quest_desc: ["The ultimate AE2 terminal. Access every network function from one item. Bind it to a Wireless Access Point with the Memory Card and add Wireless Boosters for extended range."]
	quest.2C860AA192FF0116.quest_subtitle: "Combines all terminal types into a single wireless device: storage, crafting, pattern encoding, and pattern access."
	quest.2CD70FCC8B119D7A.quest_desc: ["The Brown arrow symbols on the pump indicate the direction of flow. The flow direction can be changed by using a Wrench. When a wrench is used, the entire valve will appear to have rotated 180 degrees. The brown directional arrows will appear on the other side of the pump's gear."]
	quest.2CD70FCC8B119D7A.quest_subtitle: "Mechanical Pumps will move fluid in only one direction at a time."
	quest.2D2EAA51286CD51A.quest_desc: ["Once a Contraption can fly or roll, it needs ways to read the world around it, latch onto other ships, and brake or steer. The blocks unlocked here cover sensors that emit analog Redstone, magnets and ropes for physical coupling, and the laser system for distance and obstacle detection."]
	quest.2D2EAA51286CD51A.title: "More Blocks"
	quest.2D3144CB915A304C.quest_desc: ["Press copper or gold ingots into wire using a Mechanical Press, then roll the wire onto an empty Spool. Copper Spools and Gold Spools are required to craft Alternators, Electric Motors, Connectors, and other electrical machines."]
	quest.2D3144CB915A304C.quest_subtitle: "A reel of wire that serves as the base for the electrical components from Create: Crafts \\& Additions."
	quest.2D3F0254AB0F9F16.quest_desc: ["Attach it to any machine slot that accepts addons. Multiple processing addons can be combined for significant speed boosts at the cost of extra energy usage."]
	quest.2D3F0254AB0F9F16.quest_subtitle: "Reduces the time a machine takes to complete each operation."
	quest.2D70F503EA6F2994.quest_desc: ["A Propeller Bearing reads the structure in front of it as a propeller; any layout with at least two sail-like blocks counts, but more sails produce more Thrust. Wooden and Andesite Propellers are the simplest blades. Start here, then experiment with larger or hand-built propeller shapes once you understand the bearing."]
	quest.2D70F503EA6F2994.quest_subtitle: "Basic propeller blades: combine them in front of a Propeller Bearing to make a working propeller."
	quest.2D70F503EA6F2994.title: "Propeller"
	quest.2D8D3AD2714AE611.quest_desc: [
		"It can be used to extract ore dusts from ore clumps obtained from a fragment forge, spin coal dust into carbon fiber strands, or process various liquids."
		""
		"This makes the centrifuge one of the main progression machines in Oritech, because it sits between ore refinement, component production, and later oil and plastic chains."
		""
		"&lFluid Separation&r"
		""
		"Fluids can be pumped directly in and out of the centrifuge block itself, not the addon. The addon is only required to enable fluid processing compatibility. Common uses include refining crude oil into different fuel types or processing wheat into plastic sheets."
		""
		"If fluid recipes do not start, the usual problem is that the addon was attached but the machine state has not refreshed yet. Open the machine after placing the addon so it initializes properly."
	]
	quest.2D8D3AD2714AE611.quest_subtitle: "The centrifuge separates and transforms items through high-speed rotation."
	quest.2DA0527BD1EED709.quest_desc: ["Burns 4x longer than regular coal and can be macerated into Coke Dust for the uncooked steel recipe. The key output of the Coke Oven."]
	quest.2DA0527BD1EED709.quest_subtitle: "A highly energetic fuel produced in the Coke Oven."
	quest.2DB25CF289FAAF6C.quest_desc: ["The Powah book is an in-game reference covering every block, item, and energy stat for each tier. Keep it handy."]
	quest.2DB25CF289FAAF6C.quest_subtitle: "The Powah Guidebook"
	quest.2E20E50095EF62F8.quest_desc: ["Produced in the centrifuge by processing wheat with water, or in the refinery from oil derivatives. Appears in circuit boards, machine casings, and many later-game crafting recipes."]
	quest.2E20E50095EF62F8.quest_subtitle: "Plastic is a useful polymer used for insulators, casings, and many mid-to-late game components."
	quest.2E66275A4A0295F6.quest_desc: ["Combines Deuterium, Tritium, or Helium-3 into Helium Plasma after a massive ignition pulse. Feed the plasma to a Plasma Turbine to produce roughly 1 MEU/t — the highest output in the mod."]
	quest.2E66275A4A0295F6.quest_subtitle: "The ultimate energy source, fusing hydrogen isotopes into plasma."
	quest.2E74FA693DB180C5.quest_desc: ["Useful for powering subnetworks from a main network without sharing channels or storage access. Also a cheaper alternative to colored cables for separating adjacent network segments."]
	quest.2E74FA693DB180C5.quest_subtitle: "Transfers AE power between two networks without logically connecting them."
	quest.2EB7C4022E270816.quest_desc: ["The fastest fuel-burning generator in Powah. Consumes fuel extremely quickly — a fully automated and large-scale fuel supply is essential at this tier."]
	quest.2EB7C4022E270816.quest_subtitle: "Maximum Furnace Output"
	quest.2ED5AFA4EAB2809B.quest_desc: ["Burns furnace fuels at a high rate for substantial FE/t. At Niotic tier, automated fueling via hoppers or pipes is strongly recommended."]
	quest.2ED5AFA4EAB2809B.quest_subtitle: "Industrial Furnace Power"
	quest.2EFD3CEC00CFA838.quest_desc: ["Use the Core Sample Drill first to confirm a mineral vein in the chunk — without one, the Excavator produces nothing. This massive multiblock consumes 4,096 IF/t. Each deposit yields approximately 38,400 items before depletion."]
	quest.2EFD3CEC00CFA838.quest_subtitle: "Mines mineral deposits from underground without digging."
	quest.2F0B0D4401AA455E.quest_desc: [
		"A Wrench can be used to give the tunnel windows."
		""
		"The Tunnel does not stop items on the belt from being processed by an Encased Fan, but does stop the airflow from going beyond the belt."
	]
	quest.2F0B0D4401AA455E.quest_subtitle: "A decorative Tunnel for Mechanical Belts."
	quest.2F0B0D4401AA455E.title: "Tunnels"
	quest.2F7C30CFCD7A1215.quest_desc: ["Powered Laser Pointers project a beam that can be obstructed by blocks; a Laser Sensor in the beam's path emits a Redstone signal proportional to the laser's power. Filters can restrict it to specific colors, a Wrench inverts the Redstone behavior, and the maximum casting distance is adjustable on the Pointer's back."]
	quest.2F7C30CFCD7A1215.quest_subtitle: "A laser emitter and matching sensor: point a beam, and read where it lands."
	quest.2F7C30CFCD7A1215.title: "Laser"
	quest.2FB92BC03FFF09EE.quest_desc: ["High transfer rate cables for Niotic tier infrastructure. Avoids bottlenecks when connecting powerful generators to storage or machines."]
	quest.2FB92BC03FFF09EE.quest_subtitle: "High Transfer Cables"
	quest.302779FFD5F13891.quest_desc: ["You can replace your massive room full of chests with a compact ME Network, but that's just the beginning of things. Applied Energistics is meant to work with and allow automation of other mods."]
	quest.302779FFD5F13891.quest_subtitle: "Applied Energistics 2 adds components and mechanics to provide logistics and storage solutions"
	quest.302D29E43E9C9A94.quest_desc: [
		"When placed adjacent to any inventory, Packagers can create Cardboard Packages from the inventory they’re attached to. The process does not require extra materials."
		""
		"When powered with a redstone signal, the packager attempts to fill the package as much as possible. A Cardboard Package has 9 slots of inventory. Placing a written sign on the Packager labels the created Cardboard Package with an address to be sent to."
	]
	quest.302D29E43E9C9A94.quest_subtitle: "The Packager is used to create Cardboard Packages."
	quest.303FC5162271DCA5.quest_desc: ["Configure it to eject a cell when it is full, empty, or done processing. Supports Speed and Redstone Cards. Automate cell feeding with Import/Export Buses."]
	quest.303FC5162271DCA5.quest_subtitle: "Rapidly transfers the contents of ME Storage Cells to and from the network."
	quest.30A84C6A54BD336E.quest_desc: [
		"A stationary Mechanical Drill will break blocks in the block in front of it with a time in seconds of (45 x Hardness)/RPM and will hurt entities in an area around it."
		""
		"A Mechanical Drill moved by &3Contraptions&r will break blocks and damage entities with which it collides without needing a direct supply of Rotational Force."
		""
		"The time it takes for a Mechanical Drill to break a block is based on the Contraption's speed and the block's Hardness value. The damage dealt to entities is also based on the Contraption's speed."
	]
	quest.30A84C6A54BD336E.quest_subtitle: "The Mechanical Drill is a block used to break blocks."
	quest.30AB452E6B222ABA.quest_desc: ["Charges a linked player's entire inventory at a very high rate. At this tier it can sustain high-drain tools indefinitely during normal play."]
	quest.30AB452E6B222ABA.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Wireless Charger"
	quest.30AE6897560E6C83.quest_desc: ["Unlike Regular Sails, which produce Lift perpendicular to their face, Symmetric Sails only resist motion through them. When their face is parallel to the direction of travel they have no effect, but when angled away they apply Drag, perfect for rudders, fins, and air brakes. They attach to blocks and each other without Super Glue, and right-click with Dye to repaint."]
	quest.30AE6897560E6C83.quest_subtitle: "A sail variant that produces only Drag: useful for steering, stabilizing, and braking a Contraption."
	quest.31151795124F0ED3.quest_desc: ["Turns 3 crushed dusts or raw ores into 4.5 dusts for ore hemiquadrupling. Also recycles tools and machinery back into dust, great for reclaiming wrong recipes."]
	quest.31151795124F0ED3.quest_subtitle: "A steam machine that grinds ores into finer dusts."
	quest.3128BFA5B2FB9840.quest_desc: ["Place a Hypertube Entrance at the start of your line, then connect a series of Hypertubes leading to the destination. Items fed into the Entrance via funnels or chutes are accelerated through the tubes at high speed, ideal for long-distance item transport."]
	quest.3128BFA5B2FB9840.quest_subtitle: "The entry point of the Hypertube system. Items inserted here are launched through connected Hypertubes."
	quest.314F493196BF2D0A.quest_desc: ["Access stored items directly from your inventory. Insert the cell into a Drive or Chest to sync its contents with the network. Great for transporting large quantities of items between bases."]
	quest.314F493196BF2D0A.quest_subtitle: "A portable ME Item Cell that stores items and can be accessed without a network connection."
	quest.314F493196BF2D0A.title: "Portable Item Cell"
	quest.31759AC7A34E5440.quest_desc: ["Connects into an HV wire network and disconnects it when a redstone signal is received. Use it to remotely cut power to dangerous machinery or control energy delivery during automation sequences."]
	quest.31759AC7A34E5440.quest_subtitle: "Cuts power to a wire segment based on a redstone signal."
	quest.318BFB09F067D7EE.quest_desc: ["High FE/t solar output. A Spirited Solar array can provide substantial daytime passive power with no running cost."]
	quest.318BFB09F067D7EE.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Solar Farm"
	quest.31A24279B77C8367.quest_desc: ["Passes FE between adjacent blocks and the Ender Network at a high rate. Ideal for machines that need fast wireless power connections."]
	quest.31A24279B77C8367.quest_subtitle: "Niotic Network Gateway"
	quest.31B68E9A65B9404F.quest_desc: [
		"Base generation rate is 64 RF/t. Sheol fire can also be used, and burns much longer than normal lava."
		""
		"Fluid input can be automated with tanks, pumps, or pipes. Manual bucket filling is fine early, but the machine is much better once it is part of a proper fluid network."
	]
	quest.31B68E9A65B9404F.quest_subtitle: "Uses lava as fuel to generate electricity. A pump can be used to collect lava in large quantities."
	quest.3213F0585C961011.quest_desc: ["High-rate Ender Cell for large-scale wireless power distribution. The Niotic version handles far more FE/t than its Blazing counterpart."]
	quest.3213F0585C961011.quest_subtitle: "High-Rate Ender Storage"
	quest.323BCD8DE6E817B3.quest_desc: ["The most powerful lava generator in Powah. Drains fluid very rapidly — an infinite lava source or a very large tank is required for sustained operation."]
	quest.323BCD8DE6E817B3.quest_subtitle: "Maximum Lava Output"
	quest.326E18EEF8A2560A.quest_desc: ["Items traveling on the belt fall through a trapdoor into the block below. Essential for feeding items into machine top inputs such as the Crusher hopper or Item Silo. Pair with an Extract Conveyor to complete the loop."]
	quest.326E18EEF8A2560A.quest_subtitle: "Drops items into an inventory or machine directly below."
	quest.32AD9848A19E9CD8.quest_desc: ["Combine Crafting Units with Crafting Storage, Accelerators, and Monitors to form a complete CPU. Each CPU handles exactly one autocrafting job at a time."]
	quest.32AD9848A19E9CD8.quest_subtitle: "The basic building block of the ME Crafting CPU multiblock structure."
	quest.3302D8AB93B2ED6A.quest_desc: ["Cut from silicon in the centrifuge. The foundation of every advanced circuit in Oritech, from processing units up to the super AI chip."]
	quest.3302D8AB93B2ED6A.quest_subtitle: "A thin slice of purified silicon used as a base for microprocessors."
	quest.3324850B36696E23.quest_desc: ["Made by pressing an Iron Ingot under a Mechanical Press, or by rolling one through a Rolling Mill. Iron Sheets are required to craft Wrenches, Mechanical Pistons, Sturdy Sheets, Andesite/Brass Casings (indirectly), and a wide range of machines."]
	quest.3324850B36696E23.quest_subtitle: "A pressed sheet of iron, the foundational material for many Create components."
	quest.3347297D306113E2.quest_desc: ["Produced by combining Ultradense Metal Balls with a Nuke under extreme processing. The final ingredient required for the Quantum Upgrade."]
	quest.3347297D306113E2.quest_subtitle: "A miniature black hole harnessed through quantum physics."
	quest.337F293179141392.quest_desc: ["Works like standard energy pipes but with much higher throughput. They are thicker than regular pipes. Superconductors cannot connect to regular energy pipes."]
	quest.337F293179141392.quest_subtitle: "High-end energy cable for very large RF transfer. Default transfer rate is 4.1M RF/t."
	quest.34027D1063CA4F80.quest_desc: ["Power from the top or bottom via AE cables or FE. The three input slots (top, middle, bottom) match specific recipe positions. Rotate with the Certus Quartz Wrench for automation. Supports Speed Card upgrades."]
	quest.34027D1063CA4F80.quest_subtitle: "The Inscriber stamps circuits onto components and can crush certus quartz into dust."
	quest.34C9A6A553284203.quest_desc: ["Place a Connector on the side of a generator, motor, or accumulator, then right-click it with copper or gold wire while sneaking on another Connector to link them. Large Connectors carry significantly more power per tick — use them for high-throughput backbones."]
	quest.34C9A6A553284203.quest_subtitle: "Wire connection points that interface FE/RF cables with Create: Crafts \\& Additions electric blocks."
	quest.34C9A6A553284203.title: "Connectors"
	quest.3508D879FCE6FC95.quest_desc: ["Build with 21 Bricks and three Bronze Hatches (item in/out and fluid in), with an optional fluid output for creosote. Cooks coal into coke without oxygen — your first big progression milestone."]
	quest.3508D879FCE6FC95.quest_subtitle: "Your first multiblock, used to bake coal into coke."
	quest.35639D4A6DDF6FF9.quest_desc: ["When the Clutch is not activated, it will transfer rotation like a Shaft. When it is activated, it will stop transferring rotation."]
	quest.35639D4A6DDF6FF9.quest_subtitle: "Stops outgoing rotation when a redstone signal is applied."
	quest.35791C0AEC750F0D.quest_desc: ["Shift-click an Ender Cell with a Binding Card to link it to a network channel. The Dimensional variant works across dimensions."]
	quest.35791C0AEC750F0D.quest_subtitle: "Link Your Network"
	quest.35C37231C1C86294.quest_desc: [
		"Super Glue has two ways to be used: Block by Block Mode and Area Mode. You can mix both methods on the same contraption."
		""
		"Every time you use the glue, it loses one durability point. You can enchant it with Unbreaking and Mending to make it last longer."
		""
		"In Block by Block Mode, the glue works like a Slimeball. Right-clicking a Linear or Radial Chassis applies glue to one face, letting you attach other blocks. To remove the glue from a chassis, sneak and right-click with an empty hand."
		""
		"In Area Mode, you can glue a group of blocks that are already placed. Start by right-clicking one corner of the section, then move to the opposite corner. A green box will show the selected area. Right-click again to glue the blocks. If you want to cancel, sneak and right-click. The second corner can be up to 24 blocks away, and the total volume can be up to 2312 blocks. No matter how big the selection is, it only uses one durability point. Overlapping glued areas will merge while keeping their shape. You can’t select the face of a chassis in Area Mode—it will switch to Block by Block Mode instead. To avoid this, click the side of the chassis instead."
	]
	quest.35C37231C1C86294.quest_subtitle: "Super Glue holds structures in &3Contraptions&r together."
	quest.35C37231C1C86294.title: "&aSuper Glue"
	quest.35C87F2E9A0D4B61.quest_desc: ["Combine a cell housing with any Cell Component (1k–256k) to create an ME Item Storage Cell. The tier determines total byte capacity and maximum number of distinct item types stored."]
	quest.35C87F2E9A0D4B61.quest_subtitle: "The housing that holds ME Item Storage Cell components, creating a functional storage cell."
	quest.35CAEBFD102522F9.quest_desc: ["Insert into an ME Storage Cell or Import Bus to enable void mode. Items exceeding capacity are permanently deleted instead of backing up. Use with care. Requires the Advanced Card to craft."]
	quest.35CAEBFD102522F9.quest_subtitle: "Automatically voids items that cannot be stored because the network or cell is full."
	quest.35E71782230B13B8.quest_desc: ["Burns furnace fuels to produce FE at a very high rate. Automated fuel delivery via hoppers or pipes is strongly recommended at this tier."]
	quest.35E71782230B13B8.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Furnace Power"
	quest.3652962C0D016853.quest_desc: ["Charges FE items in adjacent inventories at the maximum possible rate. One Nitro Energy Hopper can service an entire warehouse of items."]
	quest.3652962C0D016853.quest_subtitle: "Maximum Item Charging"
	quest.36C46B44A143719B.quest_desc: ["Every CPU multiblock requires at least one Crafting Storage block. Higher-tier storage allows the CPU to manage more complex chains with many different intermediate materials simultaneously."]
	quest.36C46B44A143719B.quest_subtitle: "Provides 1k bytes of crafting job memory to the ME Crafting CPU."
	quest.36C87C5F40D3FAE7.quest_desc: ["Uranium pellets are your everyday reactor fuel. Plutonium pellets, made from processed depleted rods, burn hotter and last longer — ideal for advanced reactor builds that can handle the heat."]
	quest.36C87C5F40D3FAE7.quest_subtitle: "The pellet form of reactor fuel, ready to be loaded into fuel ports."
	quest.36C87C5F40D3FAE7.title: "Reactor Fuel"
	quest.36FC74C4E3CE7806.quest_desc: ["The ultimate Energizing Rod. A handful of Nitro Rods around the Energizing Orb makes crafting nearly instantaneous."]
	quest.36FC74C4E3CE7806.quest_subtitle: "Maximum Throughput"
	quest.370E134701621E1C.quest_desc: [
		"When broken, the small tank keeps all of its contents in the item NBT. A comparator output reflects the tank's fill level. Stacked tanks will automatically let the fluid flow downward."
		""
		"You can insert or extract fluids with items either by clicking the tank with the item or by using the slots in the GUI."
	]
	quest.370E134701621E1C.quest_subtitle: "The small fluid tank stores up to 256 buckets of fluid."
	quest.3722E03FC4BE7FE4.quest_desc: ["To establish a connection, use a target designator to bind a sending port to a specific destination. Target ports must be at least 50 blocks away and located in chunk-loaded areas. While a port can only send to one destination, it can receive shipments from multiple external ports. However if one port is continuously sending items, it can \"clog\" a target port and prevent shipments from other ports from arriving."]
	quest.3722E03FC4BE7FE4.quest_subtitle: "The drone port enables long-range logistics by transporting items and fluids via autonomous flying drones. It requires a matching drone port at both the takeoff and landing positions."
	quest.376F3D1A8B4EED1D.quest_desc: ["Used to craft Fuzzy, Crafting, Void, and Equal Distribution Cards. Required for damage-tolerant filtering, on-demand crafting requests, automatic cell voiding, and split storage sections."]
	quest.376F3D1A8B4EED1D.quest_subtitle: "A higher-tier upgrade card enabling advanced options such as fuzzy filtering and autocrafting triggers."
	quest.37CA40F69A0285C4.quest_desc: ["Define the capture volume with Spatial Pylons, then insert a Spatial Storage Cell into the port and supply power. Everything inside the pylon boundaries is cut and stored in the cell."]
	quest.37CA40F69A0285C4.quest_subtitle: "Controls Spatial IO operations, allowing you to capture and restore entire physical volumes of space."
	quest.3832300BBF5991E4.quest_desc: ["MV wires carry up to 8,192 IF/t over 16 blocks with only 0.3% loss. Requires Electrum Ingots to craft. Must be paired with MV Connectors and MV Capacitors. More efficient than LV for long-distance runs."]
	quest.3832300BBF5991E4.quest_subtitle: "Electrum wire coil for the MV (Medium Voltage) power tier."
	quest.383360C7021B2144.quest_desc: ["Required to cool hot ingots of Stainless Steel, Titanium, Platinum, and other high-temperature alloys back into usable form. Built from Frostproof Machine Casings."]
	quest.383360C7021B2144.quest_subtitle: "A multiblock that cools hot ingots into usable ones."
	quest.383D6F1A001A0AEC.quest_desc: ["Chutes pull items from above and drop them below. Stack multiple Chutes to form item shafts. Place an Encased Fan blowing upward into a Chute to reverse the flow and lift items. Right-click with a wrench to toggle direction or to swap to a side-attaching variant."]
	quest.383D6F1A001A0AEC.quest_subtitle: "Vertical item transport. Items fall through naturally; with an Encased Fan blowing upward, items can also be lifted."
	quest.388154CE72614A36.quest_desc: ["Crafted with iridium plates and superconductor wires. The final tier of circuit substrates, used inside Quantum Circuits."]
	quest.388154CE72614A36.quest_subtitle: "The circuit board used for Quantum Circuits."
	quest.3899304D69013639.quest_desc: ["Also works as a straight guide block inside an accelerator ring. Its comparator output scales from 0 at rest up to 15 at 15,000 m/s, making it the main readout for tuning your ring."]
	quest.3899304D69013639.quest_subtitle: "A particle's speed can be measured with a particle sensor. A comparator can then provide a redstone signal based on the particle's speed. "
	quest.38E9C4DB82B1279A.quest_desc: [
		"While stationary, certain items can be applied to the block's filter. If it has a filter, it will only affect that contraption actor. If powered with a redstone signal before and while it is assembled, the contraption actors will start out disabled. Keep in mind that redstone and levers assembled on &3Contraptions&r have no effect."
		""
		"While on an assembled Contraption, Contraption Controls can be right-clicked to enable and disable certain Contraption Actors."
	]
	quest.38E9C4DB82B1279A.quest_subtitle: "Contraption Controls are used to control Contraption Actors."
	quest.38EC378844976A93.quest_desc: ["Equip the Aviator's Goggles in your head slot to read miscellaneous data while looking at blocks: kinetic Stress and Capacity on rotational components, Lifting Gas data on balloons, Thrust and Airflow on propellers, Air Pressure on Altitude Sensors, and inventory or fluid contents on supported blocks."]
	quest.38EC378844976A93.quest_subtitle: "An Aeronautics counterpart to Engineer's Goggles: augments your HUD with information about placed components."
	quest.3912B9486673B33A.quest_desc: [
		"A machine frame is always built as a rectangle, with one or more gantry machines attached to it. The inner blocks of the frame should be empty."
		""
		"It is required for constructing the following machines:"
		""
		"Block Destroyer"
		"Placer Block"
		"Fertilizer Block"
		""
		"The machines always target the blocks below the frame, and they can be attached anywhere along the frame, including the corners."
	]
	quest.3912B9486673B33A.quest_subtitle: "The Machine Frame is the structural base of Oritech's larger industrial machines. It acts as a base chassis for several complex multiblocks."
	quest.39CE9D4413EC1621.quest_desc: ["Mine into the center of the meteorite to find the Mysterious Cube. Destroying it yields the &eLogic&r, &eCalculation&r, &eEngineering&r, and &eSilicon Presses&r — all four are required to produce processors in the Inscriber. If you haven't found a meteorite yet, craft a Meteorite Compass: it points toward the nearest one."]
	quest.39CE9D4413EC1621.quest_subtitle: "The Mysterious Cube sits at the heart of every AE2 meteorite. Breaking it drops all four Inscriber Presses."
	quest.39CE9D4413EC1621.title: "&lThe Mysterious Cube&r"
	quest.3A2633B6030BBC52.quest_desc: ["While worn, the Engineer's Goggles will show the stress impact of the viewed machine while it is running. They will also give numbers and highlight the current rotation when looking at a Stressometer or Speedometer. Additionally, they show how much fluid is in a tank along with the total storage capacity of the tank."]
	quest.3A2633B6030BBC52.quest_subtitle: "Engineer's Goggles are a wearable item that allow the user to see more details about placed machines."
	quest.3AF148AB8FC614A5.quest_desc: ["One of the strongest Powah generators. Place 36 Spirited Reactor blocks in a 3x4 area for massive FE output. The structure auto-assembles."]
	quest.3AF148AB8FC614A5.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Nuclear Power"
	quest.3B3B91A3F98A4078.title: "Immersive Engineering"
	quest.3B4BD7C2E48E59EB.quest_desc: ["Smelted from electrum dust, made by mixing equal parts gold and silver in the foundry. One of the first electronic-grade alloys you will need in bulk."]
	quest.3B4BD7C2E48E59EB.quest_subtitle: "Electrum is a basic alloy used to create wires, connectors, and various electronic components."
	quest.3B60F32F1A23153F.quest_desc: ["Items inside the connected inventory appear in the network as if they were in a storage cell. Set filters and priority to control which items go where. Supports Capacity, Fuzzy, Inverter, and Void Cards."]
	quest.3B60F32F1A23153F.quest_subtitle: "Exposes any adjacent inventory as part of your ME Network's storage."
	quest.3B6763B1CF0427DB.quest_desc: ["Right-click to deposit a stack (shift to dump as much as possible), left-click to withdraw. Breaking a filled barrel preserves its contents, and the barrel item itself can store items for easy transport."]
	quest.3B6763B1CF0427DB.quest_subtitle: "A portable item storage block holding 32 stacks of one item."
	quest.3B97E75CF259701C.quest_desc: ["Attach to a laser arm set up as a quarry to let it also damage hostile mobs in the mining zone. Handy for keeping the dig site clear without manual intervention."]
	quest.3B97E75CF259701C.quest_subtitle: "Adds offensive capability to quarry-mode laser arms."
	quest.3BFD1E8F79FB9C8F.quest_desc: ["Smelted from Battery Alloy Dust. Core ingredient for crafting battery hatches that store EU in electric multiblocks."]
	quest.3BFD1E8F79FB9C8F.quest_subtitle: "A solid ingot of lead-antimony alloy used in batteries."
	quest.3C6DA21DC234CE54.quest_desc: ["Place it next to fuel rods to boost their neutron pulse count without adding another rod. Increases heat and RF output without consuming extra fuel."]
	quest.3C6DA21DC234CE54.quest_subtitle: "Reflects neutrons from fuel rods back into the reactor core."
	quest.3C6E18AC535941AB.quest_desc: [
		"Click a Stock Link with the Factory Gauge to link it to that network. Up to 4 Factory Gauges can be placed in one block."
		""
		"The Factory Gauge can be set to monitor an item by either putting the item in its Filter slot or setting the item in the UI. After the item is set, the main UI becomes available."
		""
		"An Address to send the requested package to can be set in the UI. This allows the package to be sorted to the proper location. An expiration time for Promises can be set."
		""
		"The UI displays the storage level set in the Value Settings Screen and the amount of open Promises. Value Settings Screen Hold right click to open the Value Settings Screen and adjust the amount of the item to maintain in storage. This can be set between any amount (*) or up to 100 items or stacks."
	]
	quest.3C6E18AC535941AB.quest_subtitle: "The Factory Gauge is used to send requests through a Logistics Network to maintain an amount of an item in the linked storage."
	quest.3C9332E790089F40.quest_desc: ["Place the Electric Motor and connect a Shaft to its rear face. Power it with FE through Connectors. Open the GUI to configure the desired RPM and stress capacity, allowing fine control over Create rotational networks without water wheels or steam engines."]
	quest.3C9332E790089F40.quest_subtitle: "Converts FE/RF energy into Rotational Force, the opposite of the Alternator."
	quest.3CEDB498102A6F57.quest_desc: ["Feed it lapis, books, and the target item. It will apply enchantments automatically as long as it has energy and an adjacent enchantment catalyst with charges."]
	quest.3CEDB498102A6F57.quest_subtitle: "An automated enchantment station powered by RF."
	quest.3D2723CB751AD083.quest_desc: ["Produced by electrolyzing Chromium Hydrochloric Solution. Nine tiny dusts combine into one full dust, used in the stainless steel alloy recipe."]
	quest.3D2723CB751AD083.quest_subtitle: "A small amount of chromium, key ingredient for stainless steel."
	quest.3DE11BCB02E56C2A.quest_desc: ["Higher transfer rate than Hardened cables. Use these to connect Blazing tier generators and storage without creating bottlenecks."]
	quest.3DE11BCB02E56C2A.quest_subtitle: "Higher Throughput Cables"
	quest.3E00000000000009.quest_desc: ["Arrange Blast Bricks in a hollow 3x3x3 cube to build the Blast Furnace. Each Iron Ingot plus one Coal Coke produces one Steel Ingot. Slag is generated as a byproduct."]
	quest.3E00000000000009.quest_subtitle: "The building block of the Blast Furnace multiblock."
	quest.3E0000000000000A.quest_desc: ["Arrange Alloy Bricks in a 2x2x2 cube to form the Alloy Kiln. It combines two metals into alloys — for example, Gold + Silver = Electrum, and Copper + Nickel = Constantan — without requiring power."]
	quest.3E0000000000000A.quest_subtitle: "The building block of the Alloy Kiln multiblock."
	quest.3E0000000000000B.quest_desc: ["Produced in the Blast Furnace by smelting Iron Ingots with Coal Coke (1 iron + 1 coke = 1 steel). Steel is required for most mid and late-game machines, wires, and components."]
	quest.3E0000000000000B.quest_subtitle: "The backbone material of Immersive Engineering."
	quest.3E0000000000000C.quest_desc: ["Produced in the Alloy Kiln by combining one Gold Ingot and one Silver Ingot. Electrum Wire Coils carry up to 8,192 IF/t and are required for the MV power tier."]
	quest.3E0000000000000C.quest_subtitle: "A gold-silver alloy used for MV wire coils."
	quest.3E0000000000000E.quest_desc: ["Requires the Component Blueprint in the Engineer's Workbench. Used in many multiblock machine recipes. A cheaper alternative to the Steel Mechanical Component for lower-tier structures."]
	quest.3E0000000000000E.quest_subtitle: "A crafting component made from iron plates at the Workbench."
	quest.3E0000000000000F.quest_desc: ["Requires the Component Blueprint in the Engineer's Workbench. Used in advanced machines and multiblocks. More durable and precise than the iron variant, required for higher-tier structures."]
	quest.3E0000000000000F.quest_subtitle: "A high-quality crafting component made from steel plates."
	quest.3E00000000000014.quest_desc: ["Each LV Connector accepts one wire. Use the Engineer's Hammer to configure the face as input (blue) or output (orange). Connectors are endpoints — use Relays for junctions and corners."]
	quest.3E00000000000014.quest_subtitle: "Attaches to machines and blocks to receive LV wires."
	quest.3E00000000000015.quest_desc: ["Place between your power source and machines to smooth out supply and demand. Configure input/output sides with the Engineer's Screwdriver. Essential for intermittent generators like Water Wheels."]
	quest.3E00000000000015.quest_subtitle: "Stores up to 100,000 IF — LV tier energy buffer."
	quest.3E0000000000001D.quest_desc: ["Functions like the LV Connector but for the Medium Voltage tier. Pair with Electrum Wire Coils and MV Capacitors. Use the Engineer's Screwdriver to configure input/output sides."]
	quest.3E0000000000001D.quest_subtitle: "Attaches to machines and blocks to receive MV wires."
	quest.3E00000000000020.quest_desc: ["The Component Blueprint allows crafting of Iron and Steel Mechanical Components at the Engineer's Workbench. Different blueprints unlock different recipe categories. Blueprints are reusable."]
	quest.3E00000000000020.quest_subtitle: "Blueprints unlock advanced component crafting at the Engineer's Workbench."
	quest.3E00000000000024.quest_desc: ["Connect a power source to the back. Right-click with the item to charge it — a color indicator shows charge level (red, yellow, green). Right-click again to retrieve the charged item. Supports Mining Drill, Railgun, and more."]
	quest.3E00000000000024.quest_subtitle: "Recharges powered IE tools and equipment."
	quest.3E00000000000027.quest_desc: ["Functions like lower-tier connectors but handles High Voltage power. Pair with Steel Wire Coils and HV Capacitors. HV wires always shock on contact — elevate them on posts to protect players."]
	quest.3E00000000000027.quest_subtitle: "Attaches to machines and blocks to receive HV wires."
	quest.3E63AD5B01630DAD.quest_desc: ["Raises the quality rating of a multiblock compared to lower-tier cores. Only the number of allowed addons changes — operation speed and recipe time stay the same."]
	quest.3E63AD5B01630DAD.quest_subtitle: "A mid-tier machine core for multiblock construction."
	quest.3EC2C047A9DCAEB5.quest_desc: ["Produced by the Bronze Compressor at a 1:1 ratio from bronze ingots. Used in most bronze hatches, machines, tanks, and the Bronze Barrel."]
	quest.3EC2C047A9DCAEB5.quest_subtitle: "A flat bronze plate, core component of Steam Age crafting."
	quest.3EC84EB6EA2E0FDC.quest_desc: ["Right-click any tire on the front of a Wheel Mount to attach it. Smaller tires suit lightweight buggies, while larger tires absorb bigger drops, climb steeper terrain, and roll over taller obstacles. Pick the size that matches your Contraption's mass and the ground you intend to cross."]
	quest.3EC84EB6EA2E0FDC.quest_subtitle: "All-terrain tires that snap onto Wheel Mounts: Small, regular, Large, and Monstrous sizes."
	quest.3EC84EB6EA2E0FDC.title: "Tires"
	quest.3ECAB9177F57B67F.quest_desc: ["Useful for compact vertical factory layouts. Items climb the belt column and are deposited at the top. Pair with a basic Conveyor at the top level to redirect items horizontally toward the next machine."]
	quest.3ECAB9177F57B67F.quest_subtitle: "Moves items straight upward instead of horizontally."
	quest.3F61705264EDAFFE.quest_desc: ["Crafted at the Engineer's Workbench. Used as an intermediate ingredient for Electronic Components and advanced circuit items. Required before building the Circuit Table."]
	quest.3F61705264EDAFFE.quest_subtitle: "The base component for electronic circuits."
	quest.3F6C6F2FCE8453A0.quest_desc: ["The best portable battery in Powah. Stores enormous FE and keeps even the most power-hungry tools charged indefinitely."]
	quest.3F6C6F2FCE8453A0.quest_subtitle: "Ultimate Portable Power"
	quest.3F75ADBA5B33A849.quest_desc: ["Greater output than the Hardened Reactor. Requires 36 Blazing Reactor blocks placed in a 3x4 area — they auto-assemble into the multiblock structure."]
	quest.3F75ADBA5B33A849.quest_subtitle: "Blazing Nuclear Power"
	quest.3F78F467D241F10B.quest_desc: ["Greater capacity and faster charge rate than the Hardened Battery. Keep it in your hotbar to passively charge your tools at a higher rate."]
	quest.3F78F467D241F10B.quest_subtitle: "More Portable Power"
	quest.3FCDE0D862F1D5A7.quest_desc: ["Combined with an Ultradense Metal Ball under extreme pressure, the Nuke collapses into a Singularity. Also still a functional TNT-like explosive — handle with care."]
	quest.3FCDE0D862F1D5A7.quest_subtitle: "A weapon of mass destruction used as an industrial ingredient."
	quest.3FE52F9F825798B4.quest_desc: ["Each extra layer unlocks one more output from the refining recipe. A full-height tower can split crude oil into every fraction simultaneously for maximum efficiency."]
	quest.3FE52F9F825798B4.quest_subtitle: "A multi-layer multiblock distilling fluids into several outputs at once."
	quest.402D606916C9F27B.quest_desc: ["Insert into a bus or other compatible device to make it respond to redstone signals. Configure it to activate on high or low signal, enabling clock-based or conditional automation."]
	quest.402D606916C9F27B.quest_subtitle: "Enables redstone-based conditional control over an AE2 device's operation."
	quest.4058BCBC7493D7BB.quest_desc: ["Click two endpoints to create a glued area, then Ctrl-Scroll to expand or shrink it; hold ALT to anchor an endpoint mid-air. Honey Glue does not attach to animated Contraptions, only to Simulated ones, which keeps complex builds free of unwanted connections that Super Glue would otherwise create."]
	quest.4058BCBC7493D7BB.quest_subtitle: "A convenient alternative to Super Glue, designed specifically for Simulated Contraptions."
	quest.406BECED06648BF1.quest_desc: ["Powered with RF through the side. Place it below a chest or hopper so batteries, drills, and other chargeable items refill automatically while you work."]
	quest.406BECED06648BF1.quest_subtitle: "Charges batteries and powered tools placed above it."
	quest.406C745A38597DEE.quest_desc: ["Attach to a laser arm running in quarry mode so it leaves farmland and mature crops untouched. Useful for preserving farms that overlap your mining area."]
	quest.406C745A38597DEE.quest_subtitle: "Prevents the quarry from harvesting crops."
	quest.40FB7ECF967AE45A.quest_desc: ["Without a Redstone signal the Transmission acts like a normal Encased Cogwheel. Feeding the shaft and signaling from the side slows the cogwheel; feeding the cogwheel and signaling speeds the shaft up. Higher signal strengths produce larger ratios, and at full input the two outputs disconnect and rotate independently of each other."]
	quest.40FB7ECF967AE45A.quest_subtitle: "A Redstone-controlled gearbox: vary the gear ratio between a shaft and a cogwheel using analog Redstone."
	quest.4181323BF72047A9.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a valid conductor with a schedule to give it to them. A conductor must either be a mob Seated directly in front of Train Controls on an assembled Train or a Blaze Burner positioned similarly."
		""
		"3 types of commands can be added."
		""
		"&nTravel to Station&r - Navigate to a specified Train Station."
		"&nUpdate Schedule Title&r - Name of route as displayed by the Train Station summary in the Display Link."
		"&nLimit Max Speed &r- Change max speed when traveling to a station."
	]
	quest.4181323BF72047A9.quest_subtitle: "Train Schedules are used to instruct non-player Train conductors."
	quest.41CC2C620D525A81.quest_desc: ["Each module acts as a dedicated tank for the secondary and tertiary fluid products of a refining process. Fluids must be extracted directly from the module blocks rather than the main refinery base. These modules also require their own machine cores to be part of the multiblock assembly."]
	quest.41CC2C620D525A81.quest_subtitle: "Refinery Chamber Modules are expansion components for the Industrial Refinery. Up to two modules can be stacked on top of a single refinery block to enable additional fluid output channels."
	quest.41D61040B686270D.quest_desc: ["Uses Industrial TNT to compress tough materials like Tungsten, Blastproof Alloy, Beryllium, and finally Diamonds. A prerequisite for the Nuclear Reactor tier."]
	quest.41D61040B686270D.quest_subtitle: "A multiblock that compresses tough materials with TNT."
	quest.41F55F09A699E070.quest_desc: [
		"&lThe Mysterious Cube&r"
		"&l&bCertus Quartz&r&r"
		"&l&9Me Controller&r&r"
	]
	quest.4253012E6325DE60.quest_desc: ["Produced in the atomic forge when refining uranium resources. Process it further to obtain the pellets used as fuel in nuclear reactor rods."]
	quest.4253012E6325DE60.quest_subtitle: "Raw uranium extracted from the atomic forge ore processing chain."
	quest.4266BF7FCE3B4330.quest_desc: [
		"The Large Cogwheel is a larger variant of the cogwheel that can relay rotation around corners and power Rotation Speed Controllers."
		""
		"Cogwheels have three main methods of interlocking:"
		""
		"- Two Cogwheels interlock when placed next to each other (not diagonally) and facing the same direction. When rotational force is provided to one of the cogwheels, the force will be provided to the other Cogwheel at the same speed but in the opposite direction."
		""
		"-Two Large Cogwheels interlock when placed perpendicular to each other, effectively changing its axis and direction, but not its speed."
		""
		"-A Cogwheel and a Large Cogwheel interlock when placed diagonally to each other and facing the same direction. The Large Cogwheel will rotate at half the speed of the Cogwheel."
	]
	quest.4266BF7FCE3B4330.quest_subtitle: "The Cogwheel is a basic mechanical component in Create that relays rotation."
	quest.4266BF7FCE3B4330.title: "Cogwheels"
	quest.42B1841C89378829.quest_desc: ["Stores more FE than the Hardened Cell. Also upgrades Ender Network channel capacity when shift-clicked into an Ender Cell GUI."]
	quest.42B1841C89378829.quest_subtitle: "Bigger Buffer"
	quest.42EB5F2CA57DFFC4.quest_desc: ["Required to bridge Medium and High Voltage networks. MV enters from the small coil side; HV exits from the large coil side. Use it near the Diesel Generator to distribute HV power across your factory."]
	quest.42EB5F2CA57DFFC4.quest_subtitle: "Converts MV power to HV and vice versa."
	quest.43E0F14C0FB64186.quest_desc: ["Place several Modular Accumulator blocks adjacent to each other to form a single, larger battery. The total capacity scales with the number of blocks. Connect using Connectors and wires to charge from generators or discharge into machines."]
	quest.43E0F14C0FB64186.quest_subtitle: "A scalable energy-storage multiblock built from stacked Modular Accumulator blocks."
	quest.4480A4F3C97DF34B.quest_desc: ["Stores and transfers significantly more energy than the Blazing Battery. An essential upgrade for high-energy tools and armor."]
	quest.4480A4F3C97DF34B.quest_subtitle: "Mid-High Tier Battery"
	quest.44B0BCF99D6102FF.quest_desc: ["One of the largest portable batteries in Powah. Can charge almost any high-end tool from empty to full without running out."]
	quest.44B0BCF99D6102FF.quest_subtitle: "Near-Unlimited Portable Power"
	quest.44B268631ABBAB0E.quest_desc: [
		"Unlike most machines, the forge does not just pay a constant RF/t cost. Each recipe has to charge the machine to a required energy level before it can complete."
		""
		"That means your main bottleneck is usually laser throughput. More lasers, faster laser operation, and a dedicated power supply all increase production speed."
		""
		"The atomic forge has different input modes to make automation easier. \"Fill-Evenly\" or \"Sided\" variants can be used to make sure each item goes in the right slot."
		""
		"Automation can also be done via AE2 / RS2. Pattern providers work out of the box with the forge."
	]
	quest.44B268631ABBAB0E.quest_subtitle: "The atomic forge is a machine used to create advanced computer chips, reinforce deepslate, and help with high-yield ore processing."
	quest.44B268631ABBAB0E.title: "&5&lAtomic Forge&r&r"
	quest.44D44A289BE87B05.quest_desc: ["Grows near water in areas of magical energy. Required to craft Niotic tier components."]
	quest.44D44A289BE87B05.quest_subtitle: "Niotic Crystal"
	quest.45BA5B8A785E1B82.quest_desc: [
		"Using a Wrench on a component will rotate the component around the face with which you interacted."
		""
		"Using a Wrench on a component, redstone component, rail or vanilla rail variant will dismantle it and place it in your inventory. Any block which can be rotated or otherwise interacted with using right click must be dismantled while sneaking."
		""
		"Hovering over certain configurable components will allow configuration by scrolling."
		""
		"For certain components such as the Linear Chassis, ctrl can be held to configure all connected components at once."
	]
	quest.45BA5B8A785E1B82.quest_subtitle: "The Wrench is a tool used to rotate, dismantle and configure components"
	quest.45D0C73C31EE09F5.quest_desc: ["Forged from uncooked steel dust in the Steam Blast Furnace. Steel is the backbone of all upgraded Steam Age gear, hatches, and tier-2 machines — expect to make a lot of it."]
	quest.45D0C73C31EE09F5.quest_subtitle: "A tough alloy unlocking steel-tier hatches and the Steam Quarry."
	quest.46004D01A142777E.quest_desc: ["Right-click the small filter slot on the side of a Smart Fluid Pipe to specify which fluid is allowed to pass through. Useful for sorting fluids in branching networks where multiple liquids share the same pipe layout."]
	quest.46004D01A142777E.quest_subtitle: "Smart Fluid Pipes can be used to allow only a certain liquid to pass through them."
	quest.463C86AD49125B33.quest_desc: ["Attach to a quarry-configured laser so it mines blocks without breaking them, letting it harvest ores, amethyst, and other silk-only blocks intact."]
	quest.463C86AD49125B33.quest_subtitle: "Gives a laser arm quarry silk-touch mining."
	quest.464608519D87AB04.quest_desc: ["Generates very high FE/t from lava or other hot fluids. Consider an infinite lava source or large fluid tank to sustain it long-term."]
	quest.464608519D87AB04.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Lava Power"
	quest.46530B71D98AEC2F.quest_desc: [
		"How to use:"
		"-Save a position: Right-click a block to save its coordinates."
		"-Give to machine: Shift-right-click a machine while holding the designator to set its new target."
	]
	quest.46530B71D98AEC2F.quest_subtitle: "The target designator is a tool used to tell your machines where to point. You can save a position and then give it to a machine."
	quest.465892DC6DE51597.quest_desc: ["Right-click a machine to rotate it, or sneak-right-click to pick it up intact with its configuration and inventory preserved. It also toggles pipe connections when used on the end of a pipe."]
	quest.465892DC6DE51597.quest_subtitle: "The pipe wrench is the main tool for managing factory logistics. It works with all types of pipes and cables in the mod."
	quest.471473260D03D155.quest_desc: ["Crafted via Blueprint at the Engineer's Workbench. Used in high-tier machines and electrical equipment. Requires Electronic Components and additional materials for production."]
	quest.471473260D03D155.quest_subtitle: "A high-grade electronic component for advanced machines."
	quest.473B4EB6E4484257.quest_desc: ["Built around the Digital Circuit Board. Required for the Distillation Tower, Turbo Machine Hull, Processing Units, and most HV-tier equipment."]
	quest.473B4EB6E4484257.quest_subtitle: "The HV-tier circuit unlocking turbo machinery and advanced multiblocks."
	quest.47799F09127E76B2.quest_desc: ["Crafted at the Circuit Table. The Logic Unit reads input signals from connected wires and outputs redstone signals based on configured logic conditions. Used for advanced automation and circuit-based control systems."]
	quest.47799F09127E76B2.quest_subtitle: "A programmable redstone logic controller."
	quest.47862D044419BCD5.quest_desc: ["The highest-capacity FE storage block in Powah. A single Nitro Cell can power an entire base's worth of machines for extended periods."]
	quest.47862D044419BCD5.quest_subtitle: "Nitro Energy Vault"
	quest.48192BB04A89B98E.quest_desc: ["Made in the atomic forge using a heisenberg compensator and several rare inputs. Its only use is forging unbreakable prometheum tools with special abilities."]
	quest.48192BB04A89B98E.quest_subtitle: "Prometheum is Oritech's final endgame material. It can only be produced in an atomic forge and marks the last major step in progression."
	quest.4823AF94FAB4D628.quest_desc: ["Cuts ingots into bolts, gears, rings, and rods with far better ratios than the crafting table. Consumes a small amount of lubricant per operation."]
	quest.4823AF94FAB4D628.quest_subtitle: "A steam machine for crafting bolts, gears, rings, and rods."
	quest.486045C6B730FCED.quest_desc: ["Generates a steady stream of RF from direct sunlight. Needs an unobstructed line of sight to the sky — any solid block above it will stop production."]
	quest.486045C6B730FCED.quest_subtitle: "A large solar panel that generates more RF than the standard one."
	quest.487FC21C27FDE915.quest_desc: ["Produced by dissolving chromium-bearing dust in hydrochloric acid. Run it through an Electrolyzer to obtain Chromium Tiny Dust."]
	quest.487FC21C27FDE915.quest_subtitle: "An intermediate solution used to extract Chromium."
	quest.48DB190A2FE5736C.quest_desc: ["Higher-tier cells store more total items, but each unique item type still costs 1 type slot. Balance the number of types against total bytes when choosing a tier. Insert cells into the ME Drive."]
	quest.48DB190A2FE5736C.quest_subtitle: "ME Item Storage Cells come in tiers from 1k to 256k bytes, each holding a different number of items."
	quest.48DB190A2FE5736C.title: "ME Item Storage Cell"
	quest.494B52645FFCDB12.quest_desc: ["This 3x5x3 multiblock requires power and processes items dropped into its hopper. Each raw ore produces two grit, and each grit smelts into one ingot — effectively doubling your yield. Essential for efficient ore processing."]
	quest.494B52645FFCDB12.quest_subtitle: "Doubles ore output by grinding ores into grit."
	quest.495A5734B967785B.quest_desc: ["The Directional Gearshift behaves like a regular Gearshift, but reverses rotation only when shafts spin a specific way. Pair two of them to build ratchets, one-way clutches, or braking systems for your physics-enabled ships."]
	quest.495A5734B967785B.quest_subtitle: "A gearshift that only flips rotation in one direction — useful for ratchets and one-way drives."
	quest.49823607583217B7.quest_desc: ["Higher solar output than the Hardened version. Keep it unobstructed for consistent passive power throughout the day."]
	quest.49823607583217B7.quest_subtitle: "Blazing Solar"
	quest.4994FCC30198779D.quest_desc: ["Energy cost scales with loaded chunks: e = 80 + (x*(x+1))/2 AE/t. Works across Quantum Bridges but not across dimensions. Can display a hologram showing which chunks are currently loaded."]
	quest.4994FCC30198779D.quest_subtitle: "Keeps all chunks occupied by the network loaded as long as the network has power."
	quest.49D1093BBD16D760.quest_desc: ["A larger energy buffer for mid-game factories. Accepts MV wires on the top and outputs through configured sides. Ideal for bridging gaps between power generation bursts and machine demand."]
	quest.49D1093BBD16D760.quest_subtitle: "Stores up to 1,000,000 IF — MV tier energy buffer."
	quest.49E8D25D63CC335F.quest_desc: ["Produced by Create: Enchantment Industry machines that handle XP. Right-click while holding the block to absorb its experience, or break a placed Experience Block to release the orbs. A practical way to bank or transport XP between bases."]
	quest.49E8D25D63CC335F.quest_subtitle: "A solid block storing condensed Liquid Experience, droppable and stackable for compact XP transport."
	quest.4A7F96E62A5845C5.quest_desc: [
		"Mechanical Pistons are a Contraption that will collide with unmovable blocks."
		""
		"To extend, the Piston must have Piston Extension Poles at the end as well as Rotational power. The maximum extension pole length is 64 blocks, and this can be changed in the Config."
		""
		"When the rotation is reversed, the piston will retract. The end must be made sticky with a Slimeball to bring the pushed blocks back with it."
	]
	quest.4A7F96E62A5845C5.quest_subtitle: "The Mechanical Piston is a piston that can push &3Contraptions&r when powered with Rotational Power."
	quest.4AA6E52423B4A264.quest_desc: ["Two Redstone Magnets attract or repel each other depending on their poles: opposite poles pull together, similar poles push apart. Attracting magnets actively try to align with each other, which makes them useful for self-aligning docking points, electromagnetic latches, and proximity-triggered controls between two Contraptions."]
	quest.4AA6E52423B4A264.quest_subtitle: "An attractable, repellable magnet that responds to other Redstone Magnets nearby."
	quest.4AB8851EB48B45E9.quest_desc: ["This 3x5x3 multiblock feeds on items inserted from the top hopper. Seeds and Hemp Seeds are pressed into Plant Oil plus some Hemp Fiber byproduct. Plant Oil is one of two inputs needed to produce Biodiesel in the Refinery."]
	quest.4AB8851EB48B45E9.quest_subtitle: "Extracts Plant Oil from seeds and hemp."
	quest.4AC47D023474B69F.quest_desc: ["Requires the 16k Cell Component to craft. Used to create 64k ME Item and Fluid Storage Cells. At higher tiers, type limits become the main bottleneck rather than total bytes."]
	quest.4AC47D023474B69F.quest_subtitle: "Provides 64k bytes of storage, allowing ME cells to hold very large quantities of items."
	quest.4ACD5B2753DA531A.quest_desc: ["Build with Reinforced Blast Bricks (Steel Plates + Blast Bricks). Supports hopper automation: input Iron and Coal Coke from the top, extract Steel from the front, and Slag from the back. Faster than the basic Blast Furnace."]
	quest.4ACD5B2753DA531A.quest_subtitle: "An improved, automatable version of the Blast Furnace."
	quest.4B4650977344381A.quest_desc: ["Forged from quantum-tier processing. Combined with a Nuke under extreme conditions, it becomes a Singularity for the final endgame crafts."]
	quest.4B4650977344381A.quest_subtitle: "An incredibly dense sphere of compressed matter."
	quest.4B689937EE3EAF0B.quest_desc: ["Very high throughput cables. Use Spirited cables to carry large amounts of FE between high-tier machines without bottlenecks."]
	quest.4B689937EE3EAF0B.quest_subtitle: "Very High Throughput Cables"
	quest.4B7DA12F3813CBF1.quest_desc: ["Have machines generate and process all your resources while you are flying around doing anything you could possibly dream of! Of course, there is a long way to go before getting there. Can you do it?"]
	quest.4B7DA12F3813CBF1.quest_subtitle: "Modern Industrialization is a standalone tech mod, where the ultimate objective is total automation."
	quest.4B87EC7969F69A38.quest_desc: ["Place on the ground and it faces the direction you're looking. Use the Engineer's Hammer to rotate or enable incline mode (shift-click). Dye conveyors with any color to visually organize production lines."]
	quest.4B87EC7969F69A38.quest_subtitle: "Moves items along a belt in one direction."
	quest.4B976C143EDA4317.quest_desc: [
		"There are four types of Casings: Andesite Casings are mainly used in basic &3Contraptions&r."
		""
		"Casings can only be crafted through physically applying a valid alloy or ingot to any Stripped variant of Log or Wood. The logs will convert themselves into the casing."
		""
		"Mechanical Belts, Shafts, and Cogwheels can be encased in most casings, creating a decoration around the encased block. Copper casings, however, can be used only on Fluid Pipes. Likewise, a fluid pipe will not accept any other kind of casing."
	]
	quest.4B976C143EDA4317.quest_subtitle: "Casings are blocks used throughout many crafting recipes in Create, as well as for decoration and aesthetic purposes."
	quest.4B976C143EDA4317.title: "&l&6Andesite Casing"
	quest.4BEBD83362A70D55.quest_desc: ["Consumes Bronze Drills to produce raw ores from below bedrock automatically. Requires significant steel investment — build multiple Steam Blast Furnaces before attempting."]
	quest.4BEBD83362A70D55.quest_subtitle: "A steam multiblock that mines ores under the bedrock."
	quest.4C4EAB9BC8244FBD.quest_desc: ["The pump can drain liquid reservoirs of up to 100,000 blocks in size. For larger reservoirs it might not drain the entire thing. It processes fluids into its internal storage at a rate of 4 buckets per second, with an energy consumption of 512 RF per block removed. The scanning process for very large liquid bodies may take several seconds to initialize."]
	quest.4C4EAB9BC8244FBD.quest_subtitle: "The Pump is used to extract large volumes of liquid from the world. When placed, it extends a trunk downward until it finds a liquid source, at which point it begins scanning and draining the entire connected body of fluid."
	quest.4C778D955569D21C.quest_desc: [
		"With the default additive addon setting, it adds 75% speed, meaning the machine runs at 175% of its normal speed while only increasing energy consumption by a modest 10%. A recipe that would normally take 100 ticks will finish in about 57 ticks."
		""
		"Applicable to all machines that consume energy each tick they work."
		""
		"Due to its high efficiency and large speed bonus, it is much more effective than stacking multiple standard speed and efficiency addons."
	]
	quest.4C778D955569D21C.quest_subtitle: "The Synergy Matrix Addon is the highest-tier machine optimization addon."
	quest.4C7CD3858A2BE870.quest_desc: [
		"It is used to press Ingots into Sheets, which are important ingredients for higher-level components."
		""
		"The Mechanical Press is powered by an internal Shaft, accessed from two opposite sides. Much like Shafts, Presses will relay rotation along their axis. It processes items faster when it receives faster &arotational power&r."
	]
	quest.4C7CD3858A2BE870.quest_subtitle: "The Mechanical Press is a mechanical component that applies Pressing, Packing, and Compacting recipes to items below it. "
	quest.4C8DDA689FE8369D.quest_desc: ["Pour the Blend into a mold and apply heat to start the reaction. Once catalyzed, crystallization spreads through the entire fluid and cannot be reversed; some blocks are even destroyed by the process, useful for casting molds. The resulting Levitite keeps a Simulated Contraption afloat without altitude gain, and significantly resists motion at low speeds."]
	quest.4C8DDA689FE8369D.quest_subtitle: "A bucket of Levitite Blend: a fluid that crystallizes into solid Levitite when heated."
	quest.4C9DE3294FAD64F6.quest_desc: ["Place on any face of the Crafting CPU multiblock. Shows the item being crafted and remaining quantities. A useful visual indicator for busy autocrafting setups."]
	quest.4C9DE3294FAD64F6.quest_subtitle: "Displays the status of the autocrafting job currently being processed by the Crafting CPU."
	quest.4CD2258FC3CA2972.quest_desc: ["A more complex circuit than the Analog one, built around the Electronic Circuit Board. Unlocks the Centrifuge, Chemical Reactor, Distillery, Electrolyzer, and the whole MV tier."]
	quest.4CD2258FC3CA2972.quest_subtitle: "The MV-tier circuit required for advanced machine hulls."
	quest.4CD4BEB0362B0FE4.quest_desc: ["Consumes fuel only on demand, so no energy is wasted when the grid is topped off. A reliable secondary generator before oil processing comes online."]
	quest.4CD4BEB0362B0FE4.quest_subtitle: "Burns liquid fuels like creosote to produce LV electricity."
	quest.4CD822763FCBF7EF.quest_desc: ["By default the signal is emitted on the side opposite the direction of motion. The value box sets the speed that corresponds to a full 15-strength signal, and the output side can be flipped to face the direction of travel instead. Velocity is measured only along the sensor's facing axis, so use multiple sensors for full 3D speed readings."]
	quest.4CD822763FCBF7EF.quest_subtitle: "Outputs a Redstone signal proportional to the Contraption's speed along the sensor's facing axis."
	quest.4CE7AD3185C95DC0.quest_desc: ["Right-click the side filter slot to set which items are allowed through. The Smart Chute can also be configured with a maximum stack size per transfer, giving fine control over throughput in mixed-item systems."]
	quest.4CE7AD3185C95DC0.quest_subtitle: "A filtered Chute that only transfers items matching the configured filter."
	quest.4DCD3B98329A6CCC.quest_desc: ["A steel casing lined with rubber and powered by an Analog Circuit. Combined with functional parts like motors, pumps, or pistons to build every basic LV machine."]
	quest.4DCD3B98329A6CCC.quest_subtitle: "The LV-tier shell used to craft most basic electric machines."
	quest.4DFBCB76A6FAF97E.quest_desc: ["Each tier increases how many items are produced per recipe cycle, scaling from tier 2 up to tier 9. Requires matching input throughput and energy to run at full speed."]
	quest.4DFBCB76A6FAF97E.quest_subtitle: "Upgraded processing addons from Oritech Things, granting more items per operation."
	quest.4DFBCB76A6FAF97E.title: "More Processing"
	quest.4E1BC8D45B378A04.quest_desc: ["Attach the Current Transformer to a wire by right-clicking it. Outputs a redstone signal proportional to the current flowing through the wire. Useful for monitoring load and automating shutoffs on overloaded lines."]
	quest.4E1BC8D45B378A04.quest_subtitle: "Measures power flow through a wire network segment."
	quest.4E2324A171263416.quest_desc: ["A mid-tier option suitable for most autocrafting chains. The CPU's total byte capacity determines how many intermediate materials it can track at once during a complex craft."]
	quest.4E2324A171263416.quest_subtitle: "Provides 4k bytes of crafting job memory to the ME Crafting CPU."
	quest.4E482C528E9C1B0B.quest_desc: ["Generates 40 AE/t by default and throttles automatically when the network energy is full. Supports Energy and Speed Cards for up to 150% increased output. A simple early-game power source for small networks."]
	quest.4E482C528E9C1B0B.quest_subtitle: "Burns solid fuel to generate AE power for the ME Network."
	quest.4E5C6F23628A9982.quest_desc: ["Encased chain drives may be placed side by side either vertically or horizontally to form a chain passing rotational power among all the blocks. The blocks must touch on their sides (not axis to side) and be in a single straight line to form a chain. The axes of the encased chain drives may be all parallel or blocks can be rotated to orient the axis perpendicularly. Encased chain drives can also pass &arotational power&r through their rotating axis, but this is not a continuation of the same chain."]
	quest.4E5C6F23628A9982.quest_subtitle: "The Encased Chain Drive is a block that can transfer rotation much like the Mechanical Belt."
	quest.4ECF248F17A9F7B0.quest_desc: ["Produced by slicing silicon ingots in the Electric Cutting Machine. Required for every digital and quantum-tier circuit, memory chip, and processing unit."]
	quest.4ECF248F17A9F7B0.quest_subtitle: "A thin silicon wafer at the heart of digital electronics."
	quest.4EDC13D1D7AC5392.quest_desc: ["Required to create HP steam, which carries 8x the energy density of regular steam. Works in both directions so water can be cycled through HP boilers and turbines."]
	quest.4EDC13D1D7AC5392.quest_subtitle: "A titanium multiblock that converts water and steam into HP form."
	quest.4F0396D84F98B65C.quest_desc: ["Each time a particle passes through a powered motor, its speed increases by 1 m/s. Energy cost scales with current speed at 10 RF per m/s, so high-speed rings need strong power feeds."]
	quest.4F0396D84F98B65C.quest_subtitle: "Powers particles as they pass through the accelerator ring."
	quest.4F1E280925CAE803.quest_desc: ["A block-sized FE buffer. Place it between generators and machines to smooth out power spikes. Shift-click it into an Ender Cell GUI to upgrade that channel's capacity."]
	quest.4F1E280925CAE803.quest_subtitle: "FE Buffer Block"
	quest.4F833B3C9D20C616.quest_desc: ["Recovered by processing depleted uranium rods or crafted through specific atomic forge chains. Smelt into an ingot to produce MOX-style plutonium pellets for higher reactor efficiency."]
	quest.4F833B3C9D20C616.quest_subtitle: "A dust of fissile plutonium, the output of burned uranium rods."
	quest.500FA9792456C013.quest_desc: ["Use Super Glue or Honey Glue to mark a group of blocks, then hold right-click on the Assembler and pull its lever to assemble. Blocks along diagonal edges are included, and once assembled the original Assembler is no longer needed. Any Physics Assembler can later be used to disassemble the Contraption."]
	quest.500FA9792456C013.quest_subtitle: "The heart of every Simulated Contraption: converts a glued group of blocks into a free-moving physics body."
	quest.502DC31C1B136131.quest_desc: ["Transfers FE between blocks. Right-click with the Powah Wrench in Config mode to set each face to input, output, or disabled."]
	quest.502DC31C1B136131.quest_subtitle: "Better Transfer"
	quest.5052F5BF2FDACC38.quest_desc: ["The Powah Wrench removes blocks and configures cable transfer modes. Right-click a cable with Config mode active to toggle its face behavior."]
	quest.5052F5BF2FDACC38.quest_subtitle: "Configure \\& Remove"
	quest.507B64A1544AE806.quest_desc: ["Each tick removes 16 heat from every adjacent hot component, as long as it receives ice through the coolant port above. Most efficient when fully surrounded by heat pipes or fuel rods."]
	quest.507B64A1544AE806.quest_subtitle: "An active cooling component that removes a fixed amount of heat from every neighbor."
	quest.50A4DD76AC5D5C2B.quest_desc: ["Each type requires a unique press found in meteorite loot. Print each circuit in the Inscriber, then combine with printed silicon to make the final processor. Logic is the most common; Engineering is the rarest."]
	quest.50A4DD76AC5D5C2B.quest_subtitle: "Logic, Calculation, and Engineering Processors are the core ingredients for most AE2 devices."
	quest.50A4DD76AC5D5C2B.title: "Processors"
	quest.50AAFB9362931BDB.quest_desc: ["The ultimate Ender Gate. Passes the maximum possible FE between adjacent blocks and the Ender Network with no rate limits."]
	quest.50AAFB9362931BDB.quest_subtitle: "Nitro Network Gateway"
	quest.50CE0BD7B0BC4017.quest_desc: ["Fluid Valves can be switched between open and closed by providing Rotational Force to the side. This is often done with a Valve Handle or Gearshift. A set of directional arrows on the side of the valve will also rotate to indicate whether the valve is open or closed."]
	quest.50CE0BD7B0BC4017.quest_subtitle: "Fluid valves can be used to close or open the flow in a pipe."
	quest.5124AE3540FE86D3.quest_desc: ["Crafted via Blueprint at the Engineer's Workbench using Circuit Boards and Electron Tubes. Required for connectors, capacitors, and other mid-game electrical devices."]
	quest.5124AE3540FE86D3.quest_subtitle: "A basic electronic component used in mid-tier recipes."
	quest.5162D05B4B409264.quest_desc: ["Every other item is sent left or right, splitting the flow 50/50 between two outputs. Ideal for load-balancing items across parallel machines or distributing resources evenly between two production lines."]
	quest.5162D05B4B409264.quest_subtitle: "Alternates items between two output directions."
	quest.51B410F84560B541.quest_desc: ["The particle starts from the particle accelerator block, where you can insert any item to be used as a particle. A straight guide ring needs to be placed right behind the controller, facing to the side, with visuals aligning correctly."]
	quest.51B410F84560B541.quest_subtitle: "The particle accelerator is used to, as you might guess, accelerate particles. When particles of different items collide, they can create new items."
	quest.51B410F84560B541.title: "&a&lParticle Accelerator&r&r"
	quest.51C5881E3693ED00.quest_desc: ["If you place the cursor over some items and press \"G\", you can immediately open the guide for that item."]
	quest.51CCB7ACFD7B45F1.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.51CCB7ACFD7B45F1.quest_subtitle: "Brass Casings are used in more advanced machines."
	quest.51CF03840DB50993.quest_desc: ["Generates significant passive FE from temperature differentials. No fuel needed — just place above lava with water nearby and let it run."]
	quest.51CF03840DB50993.quest_subtitle: "Niotic Heat Exchange"
	quest.51E943FE5F941B7C.quest_desc: ["Generates FE passively from heat differentials. The Blazing version produces more per tick. Set it above lava with water adjacent and leave it running."]
	quest.51E943FE5F941B7C.quest_subtitle: "Blazing Heat Exchange"
	quest.5287D9F564797135.quest_desc: ["Generates Thrust like a normal propeller, but actively rotates its blades around one axis so the lift vector remains pointed up regardless of where the Contraption is heading. Right-click with a Wrench to reverse the Thrust direction. Useful for vertical-thrust drives where keeping a stable upward force matters more than directional control."]
	quest.5287D9F564797135.quest_subtitle: "A propeller that pitches itself along one axis to keep facing upward."
	quest.52F3280E4D03CAA6.quest_desc: ["Needed for crafting jobs that involve many different intermediate materials. Mix multiple storage tiers in the same CPU to fine-tune total capacity."]
	quest.52F3280E4D03CAA6.quest_subtitle: "Provides 16k bytes of crafting job memory to the ME Crafting CPU."
	quest.534DC754FE656C78.quest_desc: ["An ME P2P tunnel takes 32 input channels and outputs them at another location, enabling dense channel routing. Link with the Memory Card. ME P2P tunnels cannot be nested inside one another."]
	quest.534DC754FE656C78.quest_subtitle: "Tunnels up to 32 channels through a single cable connection across the network."
	quest.538EAF614E818A9C.quest_desc: ["Replaces a Machine Core 1 inside a multiblock to raise its total quality. The machine can then support more addons and extender layers without any effect on operation speed."]
	quest.538EAF614E818A9C.quest_subtitle: "The second tier of machine core, slightly stronger than the basic core."
	quest.53C0234C053BF0CF.quest_desc: [
		"Place a Stock Link to start a new Logistics Network. Right-click a placed Stock Link before placement to share that link’s network. Place the link on a Packager to connect the packager’s connected inventory to the network."
		""
		"Stock Links have no range limitations, but the chunk they’re in must be loaded in order to be seen by the network."
		""
		"Stock Links can receive and transmit requests through the Logistics Network."
	]
	quest.53C0234C053BF0CF.quest_subtitle: "The Stock Link is used to connect Packagers to Logistics Networks."
	quest.54778BD66812A1CF.quest_desc: ["Connect Fluid Pipes between Fluid Tanks and machines. Without a Mechanical Pump, fluids will not flow on their own. Use a Wrench to toggle pipe connections, or shift-right-click to remove. Each pipe segment shows water-flow particles when actively transporting fluids."]
	quest.54778BD66812A1CF.quest_subtitle: "Transports fluids between Tanks, Pumps, and machines. Requires a Mechanical Pump to actively move liquids."
	quest.54ABF96F1929FBBE.quest_desc: ["Insert an enchanted item into the Mechanical Grindstone while supplying Rotational Force. The enchantments are stripped from the item and transformed into Liquid Experience, which can then be piped into tanks for use in the Blaze Enchanter or Experience Lantern."]
	quest.54ABF96F1929FBBE.quest_subtitle: "A powered Grindstone that disenchants items and converts the enchantments into Liquid Experience."
	quest.54D739670D221333.quest_desc: ["View and edit all patterns in connected Pattern Providers without a wired connection. Bind it to a Wireless Access Point with the Memory Card."]
	quest.54D739670D221333.quest_subtitle: "A wireless Pattern Access Terminal for viewing and managing patterns in Pattern Providers remotely."
	quest.5533C87913404B05.quest_desc: ["The Niotic Capacitor opens up mid-high tier components with a significant power increase over Blazing tier."]
	quest.5533C87913404B05.quest_subtitle: "Niotic Tier Unlocked"
	quest.5576ED2880B6B14F.quest_desc: ["Connect it to any LV wire network for continuous lighting. Uses Light Bulbs which degrade over time and must be replaced. More aesthetic than torches — ideal for lighting up an industrial factory."]
	quest.5576ED2880B6B14F.quest_subtitle: "A powered lamp that runs on IE's electrical network."
	quest.5584B1F4C4F227BD.quest_desc: ["Stores a large amount of RF as a buffer for demanding late-game machinery. Chain several together to back up reactors, laser arrays, or particle accelerators."]
	quest.5584B1F4C4F227BD.quest_subtitle: "A high-capacity energy storage block for industrial networks."
	quest.55C94BCC704DDE97.quest_desc: ["Performs the arithmetic and control operations inside a Processing Unit. Assembled alongside RAM, MMU, and a Processing Unit Board into the final circuit."]
	quest.55C94BCC704DDE97.quest_subtitle: "The logic core at the heart of a Processing Unit."
	quest.55F36CB628017F16.quest_desc: ["Built from Steel Machine Casings, Steel Pipe Casings, and Chains. Needs an item input for drills, a fluid output for oil, and an energy input to run. Unlocks all oil processing and advanced fuels."]
	quest.55F36CB628017F16.quest_subtitle: "A massive multiblock that drills Crude Oil from under the bedrock."
	quest.55F923F918AFBFA6.quest_desc: ["Link two power poles by right-clicking one with a target designator, then another. They can also be connected to regular energy pipes to fold remote generators or consumers into the same grid."]
	quest.55F923F918AFBFA6.quest_subtitle: "Transmits RF wirelessly between power poles over long distances."
	quest.56246697CB3638D5.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.56246697CB3638D5.quest_subtitle: "A tech mod that adds various ways to generate, store and transmit Energy."
	quest.562C83804B9147B0.quest_desc: [
		"When certain elements collide with excessive energy, they can rip a hole in space-time, leading to a small dimensional incursion. The energy required to achieve this is immense, and little is known about these incursions and their triggers. Researchers have noted that colliding fire charges with a collision energy over 5000 J seems to bring the Nether closer. Ender pearls with more than 10000 J appear to do the same for the End dimension."
		""
		"There are unsettling rumors of reckless scientists attempting to bombard these incursion points with speeds that defy known measurement methods, aiming to create singularities of their own. However, none have returned to share their findings, leaving their fates shrouded in mystery. Ever since, sensors are recording a mysterious tachyon stream from the site of the experiment."
	]
	quest.562C83804B9147B0.quest_subtitle: "Collide certain elements at extreme energies to tear open a small hole in space-time itself."
	quest.562C83804B9147B0.title: "&0&lA Singularity&r&r"
	quest.5662467B224C7B4D.quest_desc: ["Attach to a fragment forge or compatible machine to double the small clump byproducts you already get. Only one yield addon is supported per machine."]
	quest.5662467B224C7B4D.quest_subtitle: "Doubles the byproduct output of ore processing."
	quest.568566551EEEB75A.quest_desc: ["Dielectric Paste is the core material for every Powah component. Craft it first to unlock the rest of the mod."]
	quest.568566551EEEB75A.quest_subtitle: "Foundation of Powah"
	quest.56C393E41CD8B3BD.quest_desc: ["One of the primary ingredients for AE2 blocks, devices, and items. Made by growing it from budding certus."]
	quest.56C393E41CD8B3BD.quest_subtitle: "Certus Quartz Crystals possess the unique trait of accepting large quantities of energy into their crystalline matrix"
	quest.56C393E41CD8B3BD.title: "&l&bCertus Quartz&r&r"
	quest.56D7F8CC3F3FEB4F.quest_desc: ["Extracts FE from charged items placed inside it and stores the energy in an internal buffer. Connect cables to redistribute that power to your network."]
	quest.56D7F8CC3F3FEB4F.quest_subtitle: "FE Extractor"
	quest.56FB8E82C0492691.quest_desc: ["Splits materials into their component dusts by spinning them very fast. Unlocks better steel and silicon recipes and is the main source of rare gases like argon."]
	quest.56FB8E82C0492691.quest_subtitle: "Spins materials at high speed to separate their components."
	quest.5750AF014D40A98E.quest_desc: ["Functionally identical to the wired Pattern Encoding Terminal. Bind it to a Wireless Access Point with the Memory Card. Add Wireless Boosters to the access point to extend its range."]
	quest.5750AF014D40A98E.quest_subtitle: "A wireless Pattern Encoding Terminal for encoding autocrafting patterns without a wired connection."
	quest.575573497C0512B7.quest_desc: ["Requires the 1k Cell Component to craft. Used to create 4k ME Item and Fluid Storage Cells. Balance type slots against total bytes when deciding which tier suits your storage needs."]
	quest.575573497C0512B7.quest_subtitle: "Provides 4k bytes of storage, increasing the capacity of ME storage cells."
	quest.576219F34BCAD0E8.quest_desc: ["More stored energy allows the Energy Acceptor to convert power faster. Cells display fill status on their sides. Chain multiple cells together to build a larger energy reserve."]
	quest.576219F34BCAD0E8.quest_subtitle: "Stores up to 200,000 AE of energy for the ME Network, acting as a buffer during power interruptions."
	quest.5771DB9E5BB9A87E.quest_desc: ["Produced in the centrifuge from coal or biomass inputs. Used to craft carbon plating, biosteel, and a wide range of structural and armored components."]
	quest.5771DB9E5BB9A87E.quest_subtitle: "A strong, light material made from carbon-rich dusts."
	quest.57CB0C8A583BB5C4.quest_desc: ["Right-click the Experience Hatch with experience-storing items, or stand on top of it to drain your own XP into the connected fluid network. Pair with the Mechanical Grindstone or Blaze Enchanter for fully automated XP processing."]
	quest.57CB0C8A583BB5C4.quest_subtitle: "A multiblock interface that exchanges Liquid Experience between players, mobs, and tanks."
	quest.5809D00CF2B9057B.quest_desc: ["Each tier drastically reduces processing time compared to the previous one, at a matching increase in energy usage. Combine with acceptor or capacitor addons so the machine can actually feed them."]
	quest.5809D00CF2B9057B.quest_subtitle: "Upgraded speed addons from Oritech Things, with a large jump at each tier."
	quest.5809D00CF2B9057B.title: "More Speed"
	quest.5853D6B92B5B9CA7.quest_desc: ["Requires the 4k Cell Component to craft. A sweet spot between cost and storage for mid-game networks. Combine with a cell housing to make a 16k ME Storage Cell."]
	quest.5853D6B92B5B9CA7.quest_subtitle: "Provides 16k bytes of storage, greatly increasing ME cell capacity."
	quest.58C815045C964ABC.quest_desc: ["Right-click a Copycat block with any solid block in hand to apply that block's appearance. Combine with shapes like Copycat Steps, Slabs, or Panels to build decorative pieces that look like wood, stone, brick, or metal — but in unique forms not available in vanilla."]
	quest.58C815045C964ABC.quest_subtitle: "A decorative block that mimics the texture of any other block while keeping its own custom shape."
	quest.58E158C8F2C04BEB.quest_desc: ["Pour Levitite Blend onto a heat source, or otherwise start the reaction, to obtain solid Levitite: the magical anti-gravity material that keeps Simulated Contraptions afloat. The advancement triggers as soon as the first crystal forms, marking your real entry into Aeronautics. A propulsion system needs lift to push against."]
	quest.58E158C8F2C04BEB.quest_subtitle: "Crystallize Levitite Blend into solid Levitite for the first time."
	quest.596183C99C77BA6B.quest_desc: ["Alloyed from 2 iron dusts and 1 nickel dust in the foundry or mixed by hand. Appears in most early-tier machinery, the assembler, and the first machine cores."]
	quest.596183C99C77BA6B.quest_subtitle: "Adamant is a basic alloy used to create the assembler, steam engine, machine cores, and various components and tools."
	quest.596CBA47803F1E2D.quest_desc: ["A network cannot consume more energy per tick than it currently has in storage. For large networks with dozens of active devices, or Spatial Storage setups that drain millions of AE in a single tick, a Dense Energy Cell is essential. It stores 8x more than a regular Energy Cell."]
	quest.596CBA47803F1E2D.quest_subtitle: "Stores 1.6M AE — for running a network on stored power or absorbing the massive instantaneous draw of large Spatial Storage operations."
	quest.597C4A2C39E7D8FB.quest_desc: ["The Hardened Capacitor is the key material for all Hardened tier components. Craft it in the Energizing Orb to unlock a major power upgrade."]
	quest.597C4A2C39E7D8FB.quest_subtitle: "Hardened Tier Unlocked"
	quest.5994B1D74A0D61D1.quest_desc: ["Build this 3x5x3 multiblock using Generator, Radiator, Heavy Engineering, RS Engineering, Fluid Pipes, and Steel Scaffolding. Runs on Biodiesel (or Creosote Oil). Outputs up to 4,096 IF/t via HV Connectors on the top bar."]
	quest.5994B1D74A0D61D1.quest_subtitle: "The most powerful power source in IE — outputs 4,096 IF/t."
	quest.599CBC177D3D745D.quest_desc: ["Right-click a Rope Winch with the Coupling, then right-click a Rope Connector to draw a rope between them. The rope behaves as a real physical constraint: pulling, swinging, and transferring momentum across both ends. A pair of Rope Connectors can also be linked, but two Winches cannot connect to each other."]
	quest.599CBC177D3D745D.quest_subtitle: "The item used to physically link a Rope Winch and a Rope Connector with rope."
	quest.59C507D6FF48D97A.quest_desc: ["Produced in the Distillery as part of the oil processing chain. Further refinement turns it into lighter fuels like naphtha and diesel."]
	quest.59C507D6FF48D97A.quest_subtitle: "An intermediate fluid produced during oil refining."
	quest.5A2450162FD24F7E.quest_desc: [
		"Two Crushing Wheels must be placed next to each other horizontally or vertically one block apart. Both wheels must be given opposite rotational force. Any items to be crushed must be inserted where the wheels rotate inwards."
		""
		"Crushing wheels can be automated by placing a hopper at the top directly between the wheels and either a depot or conveyor belt below."
	]
	quest.5A2450162FD24F7E.quest_subtitle: "Crushing Wheels applie Crushing recipes to any items inserted from the direction they are spinning away from."
	quest.5A2450162FD24F7E.title: "Crushing Wheels"
	quest.5AB1F8F69D3865F4.quest_desc: ["Fill its internal tank with Biodiesel to power it. Accepts Sawblades crafted from different metals at the Engineer's Workbench, each with different stats. Can be upgraded for damage, speed, and more."]
	quest.5AB1F8F69D3865F4.quest_subtitle: "A circular saw powered by Biodiesel."
	quest.5AD485C1FFB63CBF.quest_desc: ["Hardened Rods dramatically increase the Energizing Orb's throughput. Place multiple rods around the Orb to stack their I/O for faster processing."]
	quest.5AD485C1FFB63CBF.quest_subtitle: "Faster Energizing"
	quest.5AEB7591C3F34E92.quest_desc: ["Requires the 64k Cell Component to craft. Used to create 256k ME Item and Fluid Storage Cells. Maximizes storage density per cell, ideal for networks with large numbers of different item types."]
	quest.5AEB7591C3F34E92.quest_subtitle: "The highest-tier cell component, providing 256k bytes of ME storage."
	quest.5AEC3DBF64F32212.quest_desc: ["Automates almost every crafting recipe in the game — up to 3 different recipes in one machine with slot locking. Build several immediately to cheaply mass-produce hulls, motors, pistons, circuits, and cables."]
	quest.5AEC3DBF64F32212.quest_subtitle: "The most important machine of the Electric Age."
	quest.5AF03A768711B278.quest_desc: ["This massive 5x5x5 multiblock uses Graphite Electrodes that degrade over time. Accepts up to 12 items per batch and can recycle metal armor and tools back into ingots. Produces Slag as a byproduct."]
	quest.5AF03A768711B278.quest_subtitle: "The ultimate smelter — processes multiple items at high speed."
	quest.5AF9B99B68A2BBFB.quest_desc: ["Carried in your inventory, it silently charges FE items as you play. Higher tiers store and transfer more energy per tick."]
	quest.5AF9B99B68A2BBFB.quest_subtitle: "Portable Power"
	quest.5AFD4912CC8FBBB8.quest_desc: ["Crafted through sequenced assembly: place an Andesite Alloy on a Depot, then Deploy Iron Sheets and Powdered Obsidian onto it in the correct order while supplying Rotational Force. Required for the Railway Casing and other late-game Create items."]
	quest.5AFD4912CC8FBBB8.quest_subtitle: "An exceptionally hardened sheet used to craft endgame Create components and Train tracks."
	quest.5AFDF2B26178E14F.quest_desc: ["Generates FE from sunlight at a high rate. Arrays of Niotic Solar Panels can provide consistent passive power throughout the day."]
	quest.5AFDF2B26178E14F.quest_subtitle: "Niotic Solar Array"
	quest.5BDBD5D3B766B55C.quest_desc: ["Smelt Copper Ore or Raw Copper to obtain Copper Ingots. Press them into Copper Sheets via the Mechanical Press to craft Fluid Pipes, Fluid Tanks, Steam Engines, and other fluid-handling blocks central to Create's mid-game progression."]
	quest.5BDBD5D3B766B55C.quest_subtitle: "Copper unlocks Create's fluid system: pipes, tanks, valves, and the entire pumping infrastructure."
	quest.5BDBD5D3B766B55C.title: "Copper Paradise"
	quest.5C2108BD3DEEB0E6.quest_desc: [
		"The Spout can be filled with up to 1 bucket of any one liquid via Fluid Pipes, and it will empty some of its fluid onto compatible items that pass under it via a Conveyor Belt or Depot. "
		""
		"The spout takes 1 second to process an item regardless of the amount of fluid used, though delay between fills may be caused by the time it takes the spout to fill back up."
	]
	quest.5C2108BD3DEEB0E6.quest_subtitle: "The Spout is a block used for filling liquid containers such as bottles or buckets, or crafting with liquids."
	quest.5C3BE3DA49F5F70C.quest_desc: ["Maximum rate Ender Cell. Transfers FE through the Ender Network faster than any other tier. Essential for end-game distributed power grids."]
	quest.5C3BE3DA49F5F70C.quest_subtitle: "Max-Rate Ender Network"
	quest.5C6E945F38EA9846.quest_desc: ["Right-click a tire item on the front of a Wheel Mount to seat it. Powering the mount from the top brakes the wheel by increasing friction, while powering it from one side steers the wheel toward that side. Combine the two to build offroad rovers with proper acceleration, braking, and turning."]
	quest.5C6E945F38EA9846.quest_subtitle: "Mounts a tire to the side of a Contraption, providing a steerable, brakeable point of contact with the ground."
	quest.5C961A8A3DF4AA5A.quest_desc: ["The Blazing Capacitor unlocks all Blazing tier components. Requires Nether crystals — noticeably more powerful than Hardened tier."]
	quest.5C961A8A3DF4AA5A.quest_subtitle: "Blazing Tier Unlocked"
	quest.5CA1BB6723200937.quest_desc: ["Encode patterns in the Pattern Encoding Terminal. Crafting patterns follow crafting table rules; processing patterns are fully flexible with any inputs and outputs. Insert encoded patterns into Pattern Providers."]
	quest.5CA1BB6723200937.quest_subtitle: "An empty pattern that can be encoded with crafting or processing recipes for autocrafting."
	quest.5CA95DC4EDDB7936.quest_desc: ["When open (no redstone signal), power flows through normally. When closed by a redstone pulse, it breaks the circuit and stops power transmission. Useful for safety shutoffs and controlled power routing."]
	quest.5CA95DC4EDDB7936.quest_subtitle: "Manually disconnects a section of the LV wire network."
	quest.5D1807E0231C7C68.quest_desc: ["Plug it into a centrifuge or compatible machine to unlock liquid-related recipes such as plastic or refined fuels. Fluids are pumped directly in and out of the main machine block."]
	quest.5D1807E0231C7C68.quest_subtitle: "Enables fluid recipes on machines that support them."
	quest.5D8C03BDCC73701C.quest_desc: ["Crafted with titanium plates and digital circuits. Unlocks the Large Steam Turbine, Heat Exchanger, Pressurizer, and Distillation Tower."]
	quest.5D8C03BDCC73701C.quest_subtitle: "The HV-tier hull used for high-power machines and turbines."
	quest.5D987045B401ED86.quest_desc: ["Massive FE storage capacity. The Spirited Cell can act as a centralized power bank for an entire Powah network."]
	quest.5D987045B401ED86.quest_subtitle: "Massive FE Buffer"
	quest.5D9FA42A9A60EDA8.quest_desc: ["Place it in a charger to fill it with RF, then use it to power handheld tools or insert it into a machine as a starting energy buffer. The first step toward portable power in Oritech."]
	quest.5D9FA42A9A60EDA8.quest_subtitle: "A basic energy storage unit for early machines and tools."
	quest.5DA469AF40EF9738.quest_desc: ["Place it next to an Enchanter machine to supply the catalyst charge it needs each time an enchantment is applied. Without a catalyst block the Enchanter cannot operate."]
	quest.5DA469AF40EF9738.quest_subtitle: "A block that stabilizes the enchantment process for the Enchanter."
	quest.5DACF716CBD6E744.quest_desc: ["Place collectors around a collision point. Each one catches tachyons flying in random directions and can recover up to 4x the energy used to accelerate the original particles. Spread them out at higher speeds so they don't overfill."]
	quest.5DACF716CBD6E744.quest_subtitle: "Captures tachyons emitted from high-energy particle collisions and turns them into RF."
	quest.5DB52BA6604B9487.quest_desc: ["Built in the atomic forge from advanced computing engines. Powers the most sophisticated devices in the mod, including the enchantment catalyst, drone port, and spawner controller."]
	quest.5DB52BA6604B9487.quest_subtitle: "The Super AI Chip is one of Oritech's final computing components."
	quest.5DC940A2902E092B.quest_desc: [
		"When the Mechanical Bearing is powered with Rotational Force, right clicking the bearing will start the rotation so long as there is a potential structure connected to the front of it."
		""
		"Structure Behavior"
		"The structure will rotate. If another Mechanical Bearing is used within a Contraption, facing the same way as the original, the blocks attached to that bearing will keep their alignment as the rest of the structure moves."
	]
	quest.5DC940A2902E092B.quest_subtitle: "The Mechanical Bearing is used to create and rotate Contraptions."
	quest.5DDE12D0E3FB6A63.quest_desc: ["Load it with different fluids: Creosote Oil ignites enemies, Ethanol deals fire damage, Herbicide poisons. Consumes 10 mB per spray. Upgrades include Multitank (multiple fluids) and Focused Nozzle (longer range)."]
	quest.5DDE12D0E3FB6A63.quest_subtitle: "Sprays fluids at enemies for various combat effects."
	quest.5DE83161BF01A939.quest_desc: ["Used when your multiblocks need many addons at once. The machine itself does not run faster — only its capacity for upgrades grows."]
	quest.5DE83161BF01A939.quest_subtitle: "An advanced machine core, close to the top of the tier list."
	quest.5E133E00197A6535.quest_desc: ["Placed in the Forge Hammer, it triples ore output and unlocks additional recipes at the cost of durability. Kept in hand, it converts ingots into plates directly, just like an IE-style hammer."]
	quest.5E133E00197A6535.quest_subtitle: "A durable iron tool that improves Forge Hammer output."
	quest.5E43076252F2F382.quest_desc: ["Functionally identical to the wired Crafting Terminal. Bind it to a Wireless Access Point using the Memory Card. Add Wireless Boosters to extend its range."]
	quest.5E43076252F2F382.quest_subtitle: "A wireless Crafting Terminal providing full network and crafting access without a wired connection."
	quest.5E56F602B8815496.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a Stock Link or a Stock Ticker with the Redstone Requester to connect it to the Logistics Network, then place it."
		""
		"The Redstone Requester’s request can be configured in its menu. It can request up to 256 of 9 different item types to be delivered to a specified Address."
		""
		"When powered with a redstone signal, the requester makes the request set in its UI. If the desired items are not found on the network, the request is not made."
	]
	quest.5E56F602B8815496.quest_subtitle: "The Redstone Requester is used to request Cardboard Packages from linked Packagers."
	quest.5E71A9D153C9C00D.quest_desc: ["Ideal for routing fluids over long distances or through walls cleanly. One input tunnel can serve multiple outputs. Link tunnels with the Memory Card."]
	quest.5E71A9D153C9C00D.quest_subtitle: "Transfers fluids between two network points without running fluid pipes."
	quest.5E865A4AE339EA79.quest_desc: ["Crafted from energite and advanced components. Stores far more RF than a basic battery and supports the higher draw of late-game tools and augmented equipment."]
	quest.5E865A4AE339EA79.quest_subtitle: "A higher-capacity battery for mid-to-late game power needs."
	quest.5F0529F84BBC470A.quest_desc: ["Soak wooden planks in Creosote Oil (from the Coke Oven) to produce Treated Wood. Almost every machine in Immersive Engineering requires it. Build multiple Coke Ovens early to stockpile oil."]
	quest.5F0529F84BBC470A.quest_subtitle: "Wood treated with Creosote Oil — a key crafting material."
	quest.5F4DE0F8F3D97A06.quest_desc: ["Terminals give you access to everything stored in the network. The Pattern Provider and Molecular Assembler form the backbone of autocrafting, letting you request items to be crafted automatically on demand."]
	quest.5F4DE0F8F3D97A06.quest_subtitle: "With a Terminal and Pattern Provider ready, it's time to set up ME autocrafting."
	quest.5FFC30447F711C84.quest_desc: ["Placed inside a multiblock in place of lower-tier cores. Adds more headroom for addons and machine extender layers as your factories grow more complex."]
	quest.5FFC30447F711C84.quest_subtitle: "A higher-tier machine core for larger automation setups."
	quest.605337EA27022515.quest_desc: ["Insert cards into the upgrade slot of buses, drives, and other devices. Cards can add redstone control, faster speeds, whitelist/blacklist filtering, void overflow, and autocrafting triggers."]
	quest.605337EA27022515.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade Cards customize the behavior of AE2 devices for greater control and efficiency."
	quest.6108E95FBA6DDFBF.quest_desc: ["Attach to any generator except the basic one. The generator stops producing RF directly and instead outputs steam at a 2:1 ratio, which can then be fed into a steam engine."]
	quest.6108E95FBA6DDFBF.quest_subtitle: "Converts a generator's output from RF to steam."
	quest.6115BB4B5CCD9FDC.quest_desc: ["Used to craft all MV machines, or to upgrade existing LV machines by right-clicking with it. The upgraded machine will only accept MV cables afterward."]
	quest.6115BB4B5CCD9FDC.quest_subtitle: "The MV-tier machine hull made with stainless steel."
	quest.61348E2551E8AD6C.quest_desc: [
		"For the Rotation Speed Controller to work, it must be paired with a Large Cogwheel. The Rotation Speed Controller, when powered by the Large Cogwheel, outputs any desired speed of rotational force from its sides. It also does the opposite; when powered from its sides, it controls the speed of the Large Cogwheel."
		""
		"The rotation speed and direction can be changed in the Value Settings Screen at the front or the back of the machine. The speed can be set to a maximum of 256rpms clockwise or counter-clockwise."
	]
	quest.61348E2551E8AD6C.quest_subtitle: "The Rotation Speed Controller is a mechanical component that allows the player to precisely control rotational speed."
	quest.61394B66E3FE94B2.quest_desc: ["Automatically charges FE items in adjacent inventories. The Blazing version transfers energy at a noticeably faster rate per tick."]
	quest.61394B66E3FE94B2.quest_subtitle: "Faster Item Charging"
	quest.6185B8080800BA40.quest_desc: ["A multiblock FE generator fueled by Uraninite. Hold 36 Reactor blocks and place them in a 3x4 open area — they auto-assemble into the reactor structure."]
	quest.6185B8080800BA40.quest_subtitle: "Nuclear Power"
	quest.61A8395B0B76F622.quest_desc: ["Passes massive amounts of FE between adjacent blocks and the Ender Network. Excellent for connecting high-tier generators directly to the grid."]
	quest.61A8395B0B76F622.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Network Gateway"
	quest.61B98A3B8FAEC1CB.quest_desc: ["Built in the assembler from silicon wafers, electronic parts, and redstone. Required for most mid-game logistics blocks, filters, and any machine that needs complex control logic."]
	quest.61B98A3B8FAEC1CB.quest_subtitle: "The processing unit is a mid-game logic board used once Oritech recipes move beyond basic power storage and motors into automation, control, and machine intelligence."
	quest.61FF140A38E205E3.quest_desc: ["Set it up with an input of blocks and supply RF to place them one at a time in front of its face. Pair it with a destroyer to build loops like automatic cobble farms."]
	quest.61FF140A38E205E3.quest_subtitle: "Places blocks from its internal inventory into the world."
	quest.622F2F211736582B.quest_desc: ["Crafted via Blueprint at the Engineer's Workbench. The Light Bulb is used in the Electric Lantern and some circuit components. It burns out over time if not replaced."]
	quest.622F2F211736582B.quest_subtitle: "Powers the Electric Lantern and other light-emitting devices."
	quest.6235E91D8FE09423.quest_desc: ["Extracts FE from charged items at the maximum rate. The Nitro Discharger can drain even the largest batteries in seconds."]
	quest.6235E91D8FE09423.quest_subtitle: "Maximum FE Extraction"
	quest.626580DB654F128D.quest_desc: ["A compact, low-tier alternative to Crushing Wheels. Place items on top or feed them via Hoppers and Funnels; supplied with Rotational Force from below, the Millstone slowly grinds inputs into outputs that can be extracted from the bottom or sides."]
	quest.626580DB654F128D.quest_subtitle: "The Millstone is capable of applying milling recipes to any valid items inserted from above."
	quest.629536DB0EE7F8D1.quest_desc: ["The highest-capacity capacitor in IE. Used to buffer power from the Diesel Generator. Connect via HV wires and configure input/output with the Screwdriver. Essential for powering energy-hungry late-game machines."]
	quest.629536DB0EE7F8D1.quest_subtitle: "Stores up to 4,000,000 IF — HV tier energy buffer."
	quest.62A63BA875670AAC.quest_desc: [
		"Obtaining"
		""
		"-Entity Capture: Give a Dubios Container to an Allay or interact with a Vex to capture their essence."
		""
		"-Centrifuge (Alternative): Can be synthesized by processing a Dubios Container with Strange Matter. This method costs much more than capturing entities."
	]
	quest.62A63BA875670AAC.quest_subtitle: "A rare logic core obtained by capturing specific magical entities."
	quest.62BAE54B507B7A21.quest_desc: ["Pack items into Cardboard Packages, address them to a Frogport or Stock Link, and the system will route them automatically through chutes, tubes, and trains. The Packager, Stock Ticker, and Redstone Requester form the backbone of this network."]
	quest.62BAE54B507B7A21.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to Create's package logistics: send items across your factory inside addressed cardboard parcels."
	quest.62BAE54B507B7A21.title: "Logistics"
	quest.62D91C2154F462E3.quest_desc: ["Place the Alternator on a Shaft and supply Rotational Force. The faster the rotation and the higher the stress, the more FE is produced. Use Connectors and copper or gold wire to route the generated power into your electric network."]
	quest.62D91C2154F462E3.quest_subtitle: "Converts Rotational Force from Create into FE/RF energy."
	quest.62E51F67812F501F.quest_desc: ["Assembled from a Processing Unit Board, RAM, ALU, MMU, and a digital circuit. Required for highly advanced machines and every nuclear-era piece of equipment."]
	quest.62E51F67812F501F.quest_subtitle: "The EV-tier circuit, combining several advanced sub-components."
	quest.6308617812E40CA5.quest_desc: ["Surround it horizontally with water sources to generate up to 1 bucket every 5 seconds. Consumes 1 EU/t of steam and auto-outputs water to the machine on its output side."]
	quest.6308617812E40CA5.quest_subtitle: "Automates water production for boilers and cooling setups."
	quest.633AEA927B6C926C.quest_desc: ["Configure filters to export only specific items. Supports Speed, Capacity, Fuzzy, Crafting, and Redstone Cards. The Crafting Card lets the bus request autocrafting if the item is not already in stock."]
	quest.633AEA927B6C926C.quest_subtitle: "Pulls items or fluids from the ME Network and pushes them into an adjacent inventory."
	quest.634F916431D828E8.quest_desc: ["The largest available spatial cell tier. Requires significant AE power to operate. Once a region is captured, the cell is permanently assigned those exact dimensions."]
	quest.634F916431D828E8.quest_subtitle: "Stores a 128x128x128 region of physical space captured by the Spatial IO system."
	quest.6350ADB7540C368D.quest_desc: [
		"If the Smart Observer is placed with the front facing a container such as a Mechanical Belt, Funnel or Fluid Pipe, it will emit a Redstone signal when an item is detected inside. A Smart Observer will also emit a signal if the block placed in front of it matches the filter."
		""
		"If a Filter is applied to the Smart Observer, it will only emit a redstone signal when the item in the filter is detected."
	]
	quest.6350ADB7540C368D.quest_subtitle: "The Smart Observer is a machine that emits a redstone signal dependent on the block or items inside a container in front of it."
	quest.6381E9B427FCD5A0.quest_desc: ["Used in crafting Export Buses and Formation Planes. The Formation Plane places blocks from the network directly in front of it. Pair with an Annihilation Core for complete I/O automation."]
	quest.6381E9B427FCD5A0.quest_subtitle: "The Formation Core is the output half of AE2's plane system, placing items from the network into the world."
	quest.638386FA2D6D86B8.quest_desc: ["Uses the same layout as the Coke Oven but with Fire Clay Bricks and one extra hollow top layer. Smelts uncooked steel dust into steel ingots and later burns Raw Synthetic Oil."]
	quest.638386FA2D6D86B8.quest_subtitle: "A steam multiblock capable of forging steel."
	quest.63AEE6C4C4505DD9.quest_desc: ["Obtained by burning Raw Synthetic Oil in a Steam Blast Furnace. Mix it with paper in a Mixer to produce Rubber Sheets."]
	quest.63AEE6C4C4505DD9.quest_subtitle: "Refined oil used to mass-produce Rubber Sheets."
	quest.63C10A24B9BF2E8E.quest_desc: ["Attach addons directly to a machine or to a connected extender. Each machine only accepts addons at specific slots, shown in the addons tab of its UI or by visible markers on the block."]
	quest.63C10A24B9BF2E8E.quest_subtitle: "Addons are the main way to upgrade Oritech machines."
	quest.63C659647BFE3224.quest_desc: ["A plastic board reinforced with copper wires. Combine it with capacitors, resistors, inductors, and copper wires in an Assembler to craft Analog Circuits."]
	quest.63C659647BFE3224.quest_subtitle: "The substrate onto which Analog Circuit components are mounted."
	quest.64615688A753A824.quest_desc: ["Connect to a tank of Liquid Experience via Fluid Pipes. The Experience Lantern emits a strong light level while slowly consuming the fluid, perfect for atmospheric magical builds, enchanting rooms, or decorative lighting near Create: Enchantment Industry machinery."]
	quest.64615688A753A824.quest_subtitle: "A magical lantern that consumes Liquid Experience to glow brightly without ever burning out."
	quest.64BF887B8D1A5C49.quest_desc: ["Arrange 26 Coke Bricks in a hollow 3x3x3 cube, then right-click the center of any face with the Engineer's Hammer to form the Coke Oven. Insert Coal to produce Coal Coke and Creosote Oil."]
	quest.64BF887B8D1A5C49.quest_subtitle: "The building block of the Coke Oven multiblock."
	quest.64D313FF4B35D959.quest_desc: ["Place on top of a hot block (lava, magma) with a coolant fluid like water adjacent. Generates FE passively as long as the temperature difference is maintained."]
	quest.64D313FF4B35D959.quest_subtitle: "Heat Differential Power"
	quest.654FBC78D1C3B35D.quest_desc: ["By default the signal increases as the sensor rises. The value panel sets the minimum and maximum altitudes that map to 0 and 15, and the output direction can be inverted. Wearing Engineer's Goggles reveals the exact air pressure and altitude, and a Wrench shows fine elevation changes: essential for autopilot and altitude-hold logic."]
	quest.654FBC78D1C3B35D.quest_subtitle: "Outputs an analog Redstone signal based on its current elevation."
	quest.65715BCC3BF025C1.quest_desc: ["When powered with Redstone, the Hot Air Burner gradually fills the airtight Envelope above it. The input panel sets the maximum Hot Air output and the Redstone signal scales that output proportionally. Lift is capped by the balloon's volume, so multiple burners can combine into a single large balloon. A Soul-Infused item changes the flame's appearance."]
	quest.65715BCC3BF025C1.quest_subtitle: "The Hot Air Burner generates Lift by filling a balloon with hot air from below."
	quest.657210DE728CE88E.quest_desc: ["Only one Crystal Resonance Generator can be active per network; multiple units will conflict and reduce output. A reliable passive power source for small or early-game networks."]
	quest.657210DE728CE88E.quest_subtitle: "Generates AE power passively without consuming any fuel."
	quest.657CE123F92867DF.quest_desc: ["Far faster than the Bronze Mixer thanks to automatic overclocking up to 32 EU/t on LV. Perfect for mass-producing alloy dusts."]
	quest.657CE123F92867DF.quest_subtitle: "The LV electric upgrade of the Bronze Mixer."
	quest.65EDA8A6BAEA9E6C.quest_subtitle: "To power the Charger manually, place a Wooden Crank on the top or bottom and right-click it until the item is charged."
	quest.6678D1BD61B3D589.quest_desc: ["The built-in Modern Industrialization manual. Right-click to open it and browse the complete progression from Steam Age through Endgame, including multiblock layouts and material chains."]
	quest.6678D1BD61B3D589.quest_subtitle: "The official Modern Industrialization guidebook."
	quest.667FE50D9BAFF3C0.quest_desc: ["Usually obtained as a byproduct of nickel processing or by using a Stainless Steel Drill to reach deeper deposits. Required for Memory Management Units, Processing Unit Boards, and advanced circuits."]
	quest.667FE50D9BAFF3C0.quest_subtitle: "A rare metal used in high-tier electronics."
	quest.668F5E811B63CDF5.quest_desc: ["This 3x5x3 multiblock has two input tanks and one output tank. Add Nitrate Dust as a one-time catalyst (it lasts indefinitely). Pipe in Plant Oil and Ethanol and the Refinery automatically outputs Biodiesel for your Diesel Generator."]
	quest.668F5E811B63CDF5.quest_subtitle: "Combines Plant Oil and Ethanol into Biodiesel fuel."
	quest.6698A0C214E884D2.quest_desc: ["Produced in the atomic forge from superconductors and several exotic materials. Required for prometheum, advanced computing engines, and the particle collector."]
	quest.6698A0C214E884D2.quest_subtitle: "An advanced quantum component used in endgame crafting."
	quest.66AA8ED9D1B0F8B8.quest_desc: ["HV wires carry up to 32,768 IF/t over 32 blocks with only 0.08% loss. Always pose a shock hazard — keep them elevated or out of reach. Use Transformers to step down to MV or LV near machines."]
	quest.66AA8ED9D1B0F8B8.quest_subtitle: "Steel wire coil for the HV (High Voltage) power tier."
	quest.66AC200F6CF1A9CD.quest_desc: ["These basic parts — Motor, Piston, Pump, Conveyor, and Cupronickel Magnetic Wire — are the building blocks of every electric machine. Automate them with Assemblers as early as possible and LV crafting becomes almost free."]
	quest.66AC200F6CF1A9CD.quest_subtitle: "Basic machine parts used in every LV electric machine."
	quest.66AC200F6CF1A9CD.title: "Components"
	quest.6709FB005C1B6BAE.quest_desc: ["Each piece of the Quantum Armor set grants a 25% chance to fully nullify incoming damage. Wear the complete set to become immune to all damage and gain creative-style flight."]
	quest.6709FB005C1B6BAE.quest_subtitle: "Endgame boots, part of the full Quantum set."
	quest.67351B5448868E59.quest_desc: ["A stronger variant of the base particle sensor. Reads particle speeds more precisely through comparators, helping you tune ring layouts that demand very specific velocities."]
	quest.67351B5448868E59.quest_subtitle: "An upgraded speed sensor that also works as a straight guide block in an accelerator ring."
	quest.678B06CDCCBEB089.quest_desc: ["Built from silicon wafers and digital circuits in the Assembler. One of the four advanced sub-components that form a Processing Unit."]
	quest.678B06CDCCBEB089.quest_subtitle: "A memory chip used inside Processing Units."
	quest.679392DF76DBCB26.quest_desc: ["Each tier multiplies the maximum RF a machine can draw from its cables. Necessary alongside higher speed or processing addons so power becomes the bottleneck, not the cable."]
	quest.679392DF76DBCB26.quest_subtitle: "Upgraded acceptor addons from Oritech Things for very high RF/t intake."
	quest.679392DF76DBCB26.title: "More Acceptor"
	quest.67B350EF1D4639A1.quest_desc: ["Built with platinum, silicon wafers, and digital circuits. Essential for assembling high-tier circuits like the Processing Unit."]
	quest.67B350EF1D4639A1.quest_subtitle: "A control chip that directs memory access in Processing Units."
	quest.6819665DA7028C9E.quest_desc: ["Made by pressing a Gold Ingot under a Mechanical Press, or by rolling one through a Rolling Mill. Golden Sheets are required to craft Brass Casings (indirectly), Electron Tubes, Precision Mechanisms, and several mid-to-late-game components."]
	quest.6819665DA7028C9E.quest_subtitle: "A pressed sheet of gold, used in many advanced Create components and circuitry."
	quest.6887C6B7ED8727B3.quest_desc: ["Hot Air sources fill the Envelope from the top down, and the gas must be contained by Airtight Blocks. The Envelope's Encased-Shaft variant lets you pass rotation through the balloon while remaining sealed. Solid blocks placed inside the balloon reduce its usable volume. Right-click an Envelope with Dye to repaint it."]
	quest.6887C6B7ED8727B3.quest_subtitle: "Encloses an airtight volume that holds the Hot Air or Steam used to lift a balloon."
	quest.68C1F956504587C4.quest_desc: ["Central to oil processing before the Distillation Tower is built. Splits crude oil, naphtha, and other intermediate fluids into lighter fuels one output at a time."]
	quest.68C1F956504587C4.quest_subtitle: "Refines fluids into their lighter fractions."
	quest.69063947A26DD21F.quest_desc: ["Charge it in a Storage Unit or Transformer by right-clicking. It prevents fall damage and enables creative-style flight, but offers no other damage protection."]
	quest.69063947A26DD21F.quest_subtitle: "An EU-powered chestplate that grants flight via antigravity."
	quest.692F1705458F1AD1.quest_desc: ["Attach it to the laser arm alongside a target designator to mine whole areas. Drops are collected into the laser's internal inventory and can be extracted from any side."]
	quest.692F1705458F1AD1.quest_subtitle: "Turns an enderic laser into an automated mining quarry."
	quest.693DA91C959A72CC.quest_desc: ["Conversion ratio: 2 FE = 1 AE. Conversion speed scales with how much AE energy storage the network has. Also available as a cable subpart. Adding more Energy Cells increases conversion throughput."]
	quest.693DA91C959A72CC.quest_subtitle: "Converts external Forge Energy (FE/RF) into AE power for the ME Network."
	quest.6965C90600AD43E7.quest_desc: ["Build a hollow tower of Sheet Metal blocks with a Silo block at the bottom, then form it with the Hammer. Stores the equivalent of many chests. Integrate with Extract Conveyors to automate item flow in and out."]
	quest.6965C90600AD43E7.quest_subtitle: "Bulk item storage in a scalable multiblock tower."
	quest.69733A128FA0BEA9.quest_desc: ["Power in Oritech is push-based, so generators and storage blocks push power into the pipes, which then send it to connected machines. There is no extraction mode on the pipe itself. A wrench can be used to disable pipe connections."]
	quest.69733A128FA0BEA9.quest_subtitle: "Transfers energy (RF) between machines and power storage. The default transfer rate is 10,000 RF/t."
	quest.69AD0DAA33150063.quest_desc: ["Drag items from JEI/REI to fill recipe slots. Processing patterns are the most flexible: any inputs can map to any outputs. Encoded patterns are inserted into Pattern Providers to activate autocrafting."]
	quest.69AD0DAA33150063.quest_subtitle: "Encodes crafting, processing, smithing, and stonecutting recipes into patterns for autocrafting."
	quest.6A4BFC1DE5297803.quest_desc: ["Without a Controller, your network is limited to 8 connected devices. The Controller routes channels along the shortest path to each device. Supply power via Energy Acceptors. Can be extended up to a 7x7x7 multiblock."]
	quest.6A4BFC1DE5297803.quest_subtitle: "The ME Controller is the heart of a large network, providing 32 channels per face."
	quest.6A4BFC1DE5297803.title: "&l&9Me Controller&r&r"
	quest.6A7EB5E361DEE769.quest_desc: ["Place Hypertubes between a Hypertube Entrance and the destination. Items travel through curves and corners far faster than Chutes or pipes, making them ideal for connecting distant factories or sorting hubs."]
	quest.6A7EB5E361DEE769.quest_subtitle: "A high-speed item transport tube for routing items over long distances."
	quest.6A8049E2BD7C1F53.quest_desc: ["Configure filters to import only specific items. Supports Speed, Capacity, Fuzzy, Inverter, and Redstone Cards. Enters sleep mode when the source inventory is empty, improving performance."]
	quest.6A8049E2BD7C1F53.quest_subtitle: "Pulls items or fluids from an adjacent inventory and stores them in the ME Network."
	quest.6A84FC7CC5304E10.quest_desc: ["Mix one Copper Ingot and one Zinc Ingot in a Basin heated by a Blaze Burner to produce Molten Brass, then pour it into Ingot Molds (or onto a Depot) to obtain Brass Ingots. Brass is required for Brass Casings, Funnels, Tunnels, Deployers, and most automation tools."]
	quest.6A84FC7CC5304E10.quest_subtitle: "Brass is the material of advanced Create components, made from Copper and Zinc."
	quest.6A8CC3AFF76DDC26.quest_desc: ["Fill the internal tank with Biodiesel. Upgrade with an Iron or Steel Drill Head for better speed. Optional upgrades at the Workbench include Fortune, a Large Tank, and 3x3 mining mode. Recharge at the Charging Station."]
	quest.6A8CC3AFF76DDC26.quest_subtitle: "A fuel-powered mining tool with swappable drill heads."
	quest.6AB8AFB1EC34E2FF.quest_desc: ["A multiblock-like workbench for crafting IE-specific recipes that cannot be made in a standard crafting table. Also used to upgrade tools like the Mining Drill and Railgun. Requires Blueprints for certain recipes."]
	quest.6AB8AFB1EC34E2FF.quest_subtitle: "The Engineer's crafting station for advanced recipes and upgrades."
	quest.6BC833A2D916A0DC.quest_desc: ["Extended Docking Connectors actively try to align with each other, and once close enough they snap into a rigid lock that keeps the two sides as independent Contraptions. Items and fluids can flow either way through the connection, but insertion and extraction must be wired on both halves. Either Connector can retract to undock, and a Comparator reads the docking progress."]
	quest.6BC833A2D916A0DC.quest_subtitle: "A pair of latches that lock two Contraptions into a rigid connection along with item and fluid transfer."
	quest.6BCCCD24597C1846.quest_desc: ["Generates the maximum possible FE/t from heat differentials. A Nitro Thermo Generator array can serve as a near-unlimited passive power source."]
	quest.6BCCCD24597C1846.quest_subtitle: "Ultimate Heat Exchange"
	quest.6BDBE9743156C753.quest_desc: ["Burns any solid furnace fuel (coal, wood, etc.) to produce FE. Higher tiers generate more FE/t but consume fuel at the same energy-per-unit rate."]
	quest.6BDBE9743156C753.quest_subtitle: "Burn It Down"
	quest.6BF1B6F2253A33C4.quest_desc: ["The Toggle Bus blocks channel flow when it receives a redstone signal; the Inverted Toggle Bus does the opposite. Useful for conditionally isolating parts of your network or controlling device activity with automation."]
	quest.6BF1B6F2253A33C4.quest_subtitle: "Toggle Buses enable or disable a cable connection based on a redstone signal."
	quest.6BFA9314B5F51CFD.quest_desc: ["Required to produce sulfuric acid, hydrochloric acid, and the solutions that make chromium and manganese production possible. One of the most important MV machines."]
	quest.6BFA9314B5F51CFD.quest_subtitle: "A machine that mixes items and fluids for chemical reactions."
	quest.6C0DFC9667196100.quest_desc: ["Provides significantly higher I/O than the Blazing Rod. Multiple Niotic Rods around the Energizing Orb reduce crafting time considerably."]
	quest.6C0DFC9667196100.quest_subtitle: "Niotic Throughput"
	quest.6C34728CB6B63A37.quest_desc: [
		"These devices utilize highly enriched nuclear materials to trigger a massive, localized explosion. They are intended for large-scale landscaping and clearing hostile territory."
		""
		"They can be triggered with a redstone signal or a nearby explosion. Be warned, there's no delay between the signal and the explosion."
	]
	quest.6C34728CB6B63A37.quest_subtitle: "The Manhattan Module is a massive explosive device for strategic demolition."
	quest.6C8ECDCBEDCD3677.quest_subtitle: "The Meteorite Compass points at the nearest Mysterious Cube, which thus points it at the nearest meteorite."
	quest.6CD96328B7567F46.quest_desc: ["The Mechanical Harvester will harvest all mature crops it comes in contact with while moving forward."]
	quest.6CD96328B7567F46.quest_subtitle: "The Mechanical Harvester is a component used on &3Contraptions&r to harvest crops."
	quest.6D03D3B4D83C1840.quest_desc: [
		"Right click the front of a Mechanical Crafter with a Wrench to change the direction it sends items during crafting. "
		""
		"Mechanical Crafters can be automatically filled by Funnels or Hoppers."
		""
		"On the back and sides of Mechanical Crafters, a Wrench can be used to connect or disconnect the inventory of two adjacent crafters. Crafters can share inventories while not participating in the same crafting recipe."
		""
		"Items can also be inserted or removed by hand."
		""
		"Each Mechanical Crafter has an internal gear that can only be powered by adjacent Mechanical Crafters or any size Cogwheel. This means only 1 Mechanical Crafter in a setup needs to be powered by a Cogwheel."
		""
		"When powered by rotational force and either powered with Redstone or all crafter slots are filled, Mechanical Crafters will send their items to adjacent crafters. For a successful recipe, the items must eventually meet in one crafter. Once all of the items reach the final Crafter, they will turn into the product."
	]
	quest.6D03D3B4D83C1840.quest_subtitle: "Mechanical Crafters are machines that can automatically craft items."
	quest.6D6B9DEC00212D1A.quest_desc: ["Forged inside the particle accelerator from high-speed collisions involving specific resources. Needed to assemble the deep drill and other devices that channel unstable amounts of energy."]
	quest.6D6B9DEC00212D1A.quest_subtitle: "A crystal resonating with intense, unstable energy."
	quest.6DE566C6E0AD1CB4.quest_desc: ["A small capacitor made from rubber sheets and tin wires around a paper core. One of five passive components required to craft Analog Circuits."]
	quest.6DE566C6E0AD1CB4.quest_subtitle: "A passive electronic component used in analog circuit assemblies."
	quest.6E3DE28E9B0185C8.quest_desc: [
		"With the default additive addon setting, it adds 50% speed, meaning the machine runs at 150% of its normal speed. A recipe that would normally take 100 ticks will therefore finish in about 67 ticks."
		""
		"This performance boost comes at the cost of energy efficiency, increasing the energy consumption of the machine by 20%. Multiple speed addons can be used on a single machine to further increase total speed."
		""
		"Applicable to all machines that consume energy each tick they work."
	]
	quest.6E3DE28E9B0185C8.quest_subtitle: "The Speed Addon is used to accelerate the processing time of a machine."
	quest.6E736E3EFA5C57CC.quest_desc: ["Place an item and an Enchanted Book onto its Depot, then supply Liquid Experience and Rotational Force. The Blaze Enchanter transfers the enchantment from the book to the item. Multiple enchantments can be stacked through repeated runs."]
	quest.6E736E3EFA5C57CC.quest_subtitle: "A Blaze Burner that enchants items by consuming Liquid Experience and Rotational Force."
	quest.6E7AE6371A787560.quest_desc: ["Produces bolts, gears, rings, and rods with excellent ratios and automatic overclocking up to 32 EU/t. Combine with slot locking to automate several part types at once."]
	quest.6E7AE6371A787560.quest_subtitle: "The LV cutting machine for advanced part shapes."
	quest.6E8C6A4A07957E5A.quest_desc: [
		"When Rotational Force is given to the Hose Pully, it can extend the hose infinitely. Reversing the Rotational Force will retract the hose back to the block. The hose of the Hose Pully must be extended by at least one block before it can function."
		""
		"A Fluid Pump is required for the hose to drain or flood liquids."
		""
		"-If a fluid is pumped out, it will drain a body of liquid down to the level of the hose. If multiple hose pulleys draw from the same source, it will effectively expedite the drainage process, provided that the pipe's capacity is maintained."
		""
		"-If a fluid is pumped in, it will flood a room of any size, with the hose marking the highest point of flooding."
	]
	quest.6E8C6A4A07957E5A.quest_subtitle: "The Hose Pulley lets down a hose that can drain bodies of liquids."
	quest.6E9903B7AEDD66CD.quest_desc: ["A multiblock machine that handles high-temperature alloying. Feed it dust mixes like adamant, energite, or biosteel to obtain the matching ingots far more efficiently than hand-crafting."]
	quest.6E9903B7AEDD66CD.quest_subtitle: "Smelts dusts into ingots and combines alloy dusts into molten metals."
	quest.6EEB67A49B23E37C.quest_desc: [
		"Features"
		"-Unbreakable: Like other Prometheum tools, this axe does not have durability and will never break."
		""
		"-Tree Felling: By Sneaking (Shift) while harvesting a log, the Battleaxe will automatically break the entire tree above the targeted block. The logs and leaves will be collected and dropped at the base."
		""
		"-Extended Reach: Grants additional block and entity interaction range when held."
		""
		"-Combat: It deals significant damage, making it a viable weapon in addition to a tool."
		""
		"-Standard Axe Actions: It can be used to strip logs, scrape copper, and perform all other standard axe functions."
	]
	quest.6EEB67A49B23E37C.quest_subtitle: "The Prometheum Battleaxe is an unbreakable multi-purpose harvesting tool. It works as a strong axe for stripping wood and attacking enemies, and it can also fell entire trees in one action."
	quest.6F0C9DAC70081FC9.quest_desc: ["Found inside depleted uranium rods after they run in the Nuclear Reactor. Refine it further into Plutonium Ingots for more efficient fuel rods."]
	quest.6F0C9DAC70081FC9.quest_subtitle: "Fissile dust extracted from spent nuclear fuel."
	quest.6F502CADBF1A4BBA.quest_desc: ["Better cores do not automatically make a machine faster. Their main purpose is to increase how many layers of extenders and connected addons a machine can support."]
	quest.6F502CADBF1A4BBA.quest_subtitle: "Machine cores determine the quality of Oritech multiblock machines."
	quest.6FA74E0E712CEB85.quest_desc: ["Place next to a chest, machine output, or multiblock output face. The belt extracts items and carries them onto the next conveyor segment. No redstone required — works passively as long as items are present."]
	quest.6FA74E0E712CEB85.quest_subtitle: "Pulls items out of adjacent inventories automatically."
	quest.702820D5CD9D1E97.quest_desc: [
		"Power can be provided via the top or bottom, via either AE2's cables, or other mod power cables. It can accept either AE2's power (AE) or Forge Energy (FE). Items can be inserted or removed from any side. Only the results can be removed, so no need for filters to prevent removing certus crystals instead of charged certus. Can be rotated with a Certus Quartz Wrench in order to facilitate automation."
		""
		"Can be used to create Charged Certus Quartz Crystal from Certus Quartz Crystal, and Meteorite Compass from Compass."
	]
	quest.702820D5CD9D1E97.quest_subtitle: "The Charger provides a way to charge supported tools, and Certus Quartz Crystal."
	quest.703D3D5EEF09E72F.quest_desc: ["Combine a fluid cell housing with any Cell Component (1k–256k) to create an ME Fluid Storage Cell. Fluid cells work in the same Drive slots as item cells."]
	quest.703D3D5EEF09E72F.quest_subtitle: "The housing for ME Fluid Storage Cells, which store liquids in the ME Network."
	quest.70512E2BFC236AC9.quest_desc: [
		"In the overworld, platinum ore generates deep underground between Y -60 and Y -20. It is also found much more abundantly throughout The End."
		""
		"Platinum can also be obtained by processing nickel in a fragment forge."
	]
	quest.70512E2BFC236AC9.quest_subtitle: "Platinum is a valuable resource used for high-end electronics, advanced alloys like duratium, and top-tier machinery."
	quest.705C8ABB2339A5D5.quest_desc: ["Hold right-click to grab the wheel and move the mouse to rotate it. Sneaking while turning snaps to 45° intervals, and the maximum turning angle is set on the value panel. A Comparator on the back of the wheel reports whether it is currently being held, useful for auto-disengaging features when the pilot lets go."]
	quest.705C8ABB2339A5D5.quest_subtitle: "A held analog input: grab the wheel and turn it to produce a Redstone signal proportional to the angle."
	quest.7157002074776C07.quest_desc: ["Insert a Navigation Item, such as a compass or lodestone compass, and the Table emits a Redstone signal toward that target. Signal strength weakens when the Contraption is not directly facing the destination, which lets simple steering loops use comparators to home in on a configured waypoint. Different Navigation Items provide unique targets."]
	quest.7157002074776C07.quest_subtitle: "Reads a Navigation Item and outputs Redstone pointing toward its destination."
	quest.719218CEA358D540.quest_desc: ["Right-click the ground to place a Train Track facing away from you. Train tracks can be placed in eight different directions corresponding to the closest of the four cardinal direction and 45° increments in between. Tracks may also be placed on the side of blocks that have no blocks immediately above them. These tracks will have a 45° vertical incline. Break tracks using any pickaxe or by right clicking with a wrench while sneaking. Breaking with any other item will cause a track to disappear."]
	quest.719218CEA358D540.quest_subtitle: "Train Tracks are special blocks used to support Trains."
	quest.71B459D7437E09A8.quest_desc: ["Hammer copper and tin into dusts, mix them for a better ratio, then smelt the bronze dust into an ingot. Bronze is the base material for every Steam Age machine you'll build."]
	quest.71B459D7437E09A8.quest_subtitle: "The first alloy of your industrial journey, made from copper and tin."
	quest.71FFF73784CE49C2.quest_desc: ["Produced by dissolving manganese dust in sulfuric acid. Run it through an Electrolyzer to get Manganese Tiny Dust for the stainless steel recipe."]
	quest.71FFF73784CE49C2.quest_subtitle: "An intermediate solution used to extract Manganese."
	quest.723909D5EE9B71A7.quest_desc: ["Each piece of the Quantum Armor set grants a 25% chance to fully nullify incoming damage. Wear the complete set to become immune to all damage and gain creative-style flight."]
	quest.723909D5EE9B71A7.quest_subtitle: "Endgame chestplate, part of the full Quantum set."
	quest.724123C2B194AA87.quest_desc: ["Search, withdraw, and deposit items from any terminal on the network. Supports regex search and displays total network capacity. The Crafting Terminal variant adds a built-in crafting grid."]
	quest.724123C2B194AA87.quest_subtitle: "The ME Terminal is your primary interface for accessing and managing items stored in the network."
	quest.724A47E73B5B35C5.quest_desc: ["Each piece of the Quantum Armor set grants a 25% chance to fully nullify incoming damage. Wear the complete set to become immune to all damage and gain creative-style flight."]
	quest.724A47E73B5B35C5.quest_subtitle: "Endgame leggings, part of the full Quantum set."
	quest.72548E78CCAECE39.quest_desc: ["Insert into Portable Cells to extend their internal energy buffer. Also improves energy efficiency in other compatible devices. Requires the Advanced Card to craft."]
	quest.72548E78CCAECE39.quest_subtitle: "Increases the energy storage capacity of ME devices, reducing recharge frequency."
	quest.7255AA08F71158E1.quest_desc: [
		"Usage"
		"Feed it biomass-derived fuels and other biological materials accepted by your recipe viewer. This is a multiblock machine that needs machine cores to work."
		""
		"It is one of the easiest generators to automate if you already have tree farms, crop farms, or other systems that produce steady organic waste. Because it supports addons, it can stay useful well after the basic generator has been retired."
	]
	quest.7255AA08F71158E1.quest_subtitle: "Converts biomass and other biological materials into energy. A good way to recycle organic waste from your farms.The base generation rate is 64 RF/t."
	quest.725ABFB0F86E3B84.quest_desc: ["Found in the Nether. Energized with Blazing Crystals to unlock Blazing tier components via the Energizing Orb."]
	quest.725ABFB0F86E3B84.quest_subtitle: "Blazing Crystal"
	quest.728A15DCD6D95495.quest_desc: ["Crafted with platinum plates and digital circuit components. Hosts the RAM, ALU, and MMU that together form a Processing Unit."]
	quest.728A15DCD6D95495.quest_subtitle: "The high-tier board used in Processing Unit assembly."
	quest.728BA6F9043EC5D1.quest_desc: ["Behaves like a regular energy pipe, but transfers much more RF per tick. Ideal for the main power backbone when a single pipe cannot keep up with high-demand machines."]
	quest.728BA6F9043EC5D1.quest_subtitle: "A dense bundle of energy pipes with greatly increased throughput."
	quest.7322A19FDA5B78E1.quest_desc: ["The Valve Handle functions much like the Hand Crank, though the amount and direction it rotates with one use can be adjusted in its Value Settings Screen."]
	quest.7322A19FDA5B78E1.quest_subtitle: "A reusable, hand-cranked source of Rotational Force. Right-click to spin connected machinery."
	quest.732D1A96512F2BFD.quest_desc: [
		"The Steam Engine is a block that provides Rotational Force. It outputs the highest Stress Unit (SU) capacity of all the survival-mode power-generating blocks. It converts the pressure caused by heating Water in a Fluid Tank into Rotational Force, allowing for large scale item production and multiple &3Contraptions&r to be powered."
		""
		"Steam Engines use heated Water for power and are placed on Fluid Tanks, which are then used as a boiler. A Shaft can be used on the engine to create a kinetic output. The direction of said output can be adjusted through the Value Settings on the side of the engine."
		""
		"Increasing the total power generated requires that one or more of the three characteristics (heat, size, water) of the Fluid Tank boiler be increased. This will increase the boiler's level to the lowest level reached by any of the three characteristics, increasing the maximum amount of SU Steam Engines are capable of generating from the boiler. A single Steam Engine can only extract up to 16,384 SU (The equivalent of 1 boiler level). To combat this, multiple Steam Engines can be attached to a single boiler to extract more power; however, this will not increase the total power generated by the boiler."
		""
		""
		"The tank size is the basic characteristic of a steam boiler. The required dimensions are affected by the heat supplied. For a passive steam engine (level 0) the boiler must be a 2x2 fluid tank of preferably one block height (making it any higher will be a waste of resources). For an active steam engine (level 1 or higher) the boiler must have 4 blocks per heat level. For example, a level 1 boiler must have a tank made of at least 4 fluid tank blocks, a level 9 boiler must be made of at least 36 blocks and a level 18 boiler (maximum achievable) must be at least made of 72 blocks."
		""
		""
		"A steam boiler requires heat to function. Heat sources must be placed underneath the boiler tank in order to affect it. All passive heat sources generate the same amount of heat. More heat can be generated with the help of Blaze Burners, which produce varying amounts of heat depending on their state."
	]
	quest.732D1A96512F2BFD.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Engine is a block that provides Rotational Force."
	quest.733682694C9BB657.quest_desc: ["When 2 particles from different particle accelerator controllers collide with each other, they can result in a different item. Depending on the recipe, the required collision energy will differ. The collision energy is the sum of the speeds of both particles. The item type is irrelevant here, only the speeds matter."]
	quest.733682694C9BB657.quest_subtitle: "The starting point of every particle accelerator. Insert any item to launch it into the ring as a particle."
	quest.734AFCD90EC0A6D1.quest_desc: ["Generates high passive FE from heat differentials. Arrays of Spirited Thermo Generators can form a strong passive power backbone."]
	quest.734AFCD90EC0A6D1.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Heat Exchange"
	quest.734FECA2ED34F0D7.quest_desc: [
		"Accepts liquid fuels through pipes or buckets. This is a multiblock that needs machine cores. You can also insert or extract fuel by clicking the machine with a fluid containing item."
		""
		"Raw oil is enough to get it running, but refined fuels are where the machine becomes truly efficient. If you already have a refinery, this is usually the best first consumer for those upgraded fuels."
	]
	quest.734FECA2ED34F0D7.quest_subtitle: "Burns liquid fuels like oil or diesel to produce large amounts of energy. Default generation rate is 256 RF/t."
	quest.73B10BDCA634D5FD.quest_desc: ["Each burst addon duplicates the machine's current recipe across an extra internal slot, multiplying output per tick at the cost of proportionally higher energy usage."]
	quest.73B10BDCA634D5FD.quest_subtitle: "Lets a machine process several items in parallel."
	quest.73FC122F228CEB96.quest_desc: [
		"Some machine components can be crafted without an assembler, but doing so uses significantly more resources."
		""
		"The order of the components in the input slots does not matter. If a machine needs 2 of the same item, it can also take both from the same slot."
	]
	quest.73FC122F228CEB96.quest_subtitle: "The assembler features a 2x2 crafting grid and will automatically assemble items as long as it has energy, items in the input slots, and space for the finished product in the output slot."
	quest.741AC03B9652EF8D.quest_desc: ["Obtain Silicon by smelting sand or certus quartz dust. Inscribe it without a press to make Printed Silicon. Combine Printed Silicon with the appropriate printed circuit in the Inscriber to assemble each processor type."]
	quest.741AC03B9652EF8D.quest_subtitle: "Silicon is inscribed in the Inscriber to produce Printed Silicon, a component used in all three processor types."
	quest.7429FC1E27707218.quest_desc: ["For complex automated crafting chains with many intermediate materials. Combine multiple storage tiers in one CPU to tailor capacity precisely to your automation needs."]
	quest.7429FC1E27707218.quest_subtitle: "Provides 64k bytes of crafting job memory to the ME Crafting CPU."
	quest.742F950FFFDE819F.quest_desc: ["Apply it to a machine to unlock extreme overclocking far beyond every previous upgrade. A trophy of endgame Modern Industrialization."]
	quest.742F950FFFDE819F.quest_subtitle: "The most powerful machine upgrade ever created."
	quest.7437F04E5413A8E0.quest_desc: ["Install to let a machine pull energy faster from its cables. Required when high-draw recipes outrun the default input rate of the base machine."]
	quest.7437F04E5413A8E0.quest_subtitle: "Raises the maximum RF/t a machine can accept."
	quest.746DACE8912A9DE2.quest_desc: ["Alloyed in the foundry from nickel, redstone, and gold. Required for the advanced battery, large storage block, and most high-throughput energy infrastructure."]
	quest.746DACE8912A9DE2.quest_subtitle: "Energite is a high-tier alloy used to create advanced power-related components and machines. It is used for high-capacity energy storage and advanced power distribution."
	quest.74AD9C3B54878FDB.quest_desc: ["Use Gyroscopic Bearings on helicopters and other top-heavy builds where a regular Propeller Bearing would let the lift vector wobble. They actively counter roll and pitch so the propeller stays vertical, and applying a Redstone signal resets the tilt back to zero. Like all propellers, output weakens at higher altitudes."]
	quest.74AD9C3B54878FDB.quest_subtitle: "A self-righting Propeller Bearing: keeps its propeller pointed upright even as the Contraption tilts."
	quest.74B030D7831F13EE.quest_desc: ["This three-block-tall structure grows crops continuously using power and water. Insert seeds, soil, and optionally fertilizer. Power connects to the top; water pipes to the back. Essential for sustaining the Biodiesel production chain."]
	quest.74B030D7831F13EE.quest_subtitle: "An automated crop-growing machine powered by electricity."
	quest.74D3B34DC534515D.quest_desc: ["Place Hypertube Accelerators along a Hypertube line. Each one re-accelerates passing items, allowing virtually unlimited transport range. Useful for cross-base or cross-dimension item logistics."]
	quest.74D3B34DC534515D.quest_subtitle: "Boosts items traveling through Hypertubes, extending range and increasing speed."
	quest.756715CFB394F888.quest_desc: ["Smelted in the Electric Blast Furnace as hot ingots, then cooled in a Vacuum Freezer. The base metal for the Turbo Machine Hull, Pressurizer, and Implosion Compressor."]
	quest.756715CFB394F888.quest_subtitle: "A tough, high-temperature metal used in advanced machinery."
	quest.7578A1015C1ED66D.quest_desc: [
		"Energy Buffer"
		""
		"In addition to providing extra addon slots, this block adds 2 500 000 RF to the machine's total capacity and increases energy throughput by 1 000 RF/t. It is a good choice for powering energy-heavy machines that also require many addons."
	]
	quest.7578A1015C1ED66D.quest_subtitle: "The Power Bank Addon Extender combines the slot expansion of an extender with a large internal energy reserve. Applicable to all blocks with energy."
	quest.7593E42AEBD98923.quest_desc: ["Transfers FE between adjacent blocks and the Ender Network. Unlike the Ender Cell it cannot upgrade network channel capacity, but it is cheaper to make."]
	quest.7593E42AEBD98923.quest_subtitle: "Network Gateway"
	quest.75A7837D3FB78833.quest_desc: [
		"To produce steam, water will be consumed. Water and steam can be pumped in and out directly from the addon, but not the machine itself."
		""
		"To use the steam, a steam engine can be used to produce RF from it. It takes steam as input and outputs water. However, during the process, around 20% of the water will be lost, so a steady supply of water is needed for the generators."
	]
	quest.75A7837D3FB78833.quest_subtitle: "All generators (except the basic generator) can be upgraded to produce steam by adding a steam boiler addon. When added, the machine will no longer directly produce RF. Instead, it will produce steam at a rate of 2:1."
	quest.75E7216AB5411DF6.quest_desc: ["When facing up, the Mechanical Saw processes items dropped onto it (logs into planks, stones into stairs, etc.) given enough Rotational Force. When mounted on a Contraption facing forward, it chops down entire trees and breaks blocks in front of it as the Contraption moves."]
	quest.75E7216AB5411DF6.quest_subtitle: "Cuts logs into planks, processes various recipes, and chops trees when used on a Contraption."
	quest.76014E3C5DE99810.quest_desc: ["Multiblocks receive ingredients through item input hatches and expel results through item output hatches. Each hatch replaces a casing slot on the structure."]
	quest.76014E3C5DE99810.quest_subtitle: "Input and output hatches that move items in and out of multiblocks."
	quest.76014E3C5DE99810.title: "Bronze Item Hatch"
	quest.76107F9E33FF5DC9.quest_desc: ["Used to insulate wires into cables and as a core ingredient for electronic components like capacitors, resistors, and inductors. Automating it is one of the first priorities of the Electric Age."]
	quest.76107F9E33FF5DC9.quest_subtitle: "A flexible insulating sheet made from synthetic oil and paper."
	quest.7640050ABC78F0B2.quest_desc: ["Route MI power across long distances without running additional EU cables. Link tunnels with the Memory Card. Works like other energy P2P tunnels but carries EU instead of FE."]
	quest.7640050ABC78F0B2.quest_subtitle: "Transfers Modern Industrialization EU energy between two network points via P2P tunneling."
	quest.765009CFB3626487.quest_desc: ["A common Oritech component crafted from iron, copper, and redstone. It appears in almost every machine, addon, and tool recipe, so expect to keep a large supply on hand."]
	quest.765009CFB3626487.quest_subtitle: "A standard electric motor used to drive mechanical parts in industrial machines."
	quest.7684343E3C2DB080.quest_desc: ["A multiblock machine that splits crude oil and other mixtures into their refined components. Stack up to two refinery chamber modules on top to unlock additional fluid output slots."]
	quest.7684343E3C2DB080.quest_subtitle: "The refinery is used to process item and fluid mixtures. It has one item input, one fluid input, and multiple output options."
	quest.768789FEB6EBB8F8.quest_desc: [
		"It can be used for heating Steam Engines, Bulk Smoking, Bulk Smelting, and as a decorative light source."
		""
		"Blaze Burners must have Blazes in them to function. To put a Blaze in an Empty Blaze Burner, right-click on a Blaze while holding an Empty Blaze Burner. Alternatively, an Empty Blaze Burner can be filled by right-clicking on a Blaze Spawner. This method can be repeated without risk of destroying the Blaze Spawner."
		""
		"Right-clicking a Blaze Burner with any item that can be used as Furnace fuel will temporarily put it in a Heated state. Right-clicking a Blaze Burner with a Blaze Cake will temporarily put it in a Super-Heated state."
		""
		"The Blaze inside changes its size and texture depending on the amount of fuel provided, following the phases:"
		""
		"Phase 1 — Smouldering — Does not provide any heat for mixing. This is the default state when placing the Burner or when the fuel runs out."
		"Phase 2 — Heated/Kindled — Enables recipes that require heating. Lasts for the fuel's burn time and provides 1 heating level to Steam Engines per Blaze Burner"
		"Phase 3 — Super-Heated/Seething — Enables every Mixing recipe and provides 2 heating levels to Steam Engines per Blaze Burner. Only achievable using the Blaze Cake. Always lasts for 160 seconds. The Blaze Burner cannot be re-fed during this phase."
	]
	quest.768789FEB6EBB8F8.quest_subtitle: "A Blaze Burner is a heating component that is required for certain Mixing recipes. "
	quest.76919513DA354DBC.quest_desc: [
		"The Gearbox can relay rotational power in four horizontal directions. The vertical counterpart, like the normal version, can relay power in four vertical directions. "
		""
		"When receiving input from any input side (sides with a shaft shape), the Gearbox will output/relay &arotational power&r in opposite spin for all of the remaining sides. In another word, when the input is clockwise, the output on the other 3 sides will be anti-clockwise, and vice-versa."
	]
	quest.76919513DA354DBC.quest_subtitle: "The Gearbox is a block used to transfer Rotational power in 4 directions, either horizontally or vertically."
	quest.76CCE7B3F1922436.quest_desc: ["Place a Mechanical Mixer above a Basin and supply Rotational Force. Drop ingredients into the Basin to perform mixing recipes. Some recipes — such as Brass and Andesite Alloy — additionally require heat from a Blaze Burner placed below the Basin."]
	quest.76CCE7B3F1922436.quest_subtitle: "Combines ingredients dropped into a Basin to produce alloys, food, and other mixed products."
	quest.7703F0CA1A8AB6F9.quest_desc: ["Among its many functions, it is an essential ingredient for crafting Shafts and both regular and large Cogwheels. Andesite Alloy is the most basic component construction material in Create."]
	quest.7703F0CA1A8AB6F9.quest_subtitle: "Andesite Alloy is a material used in Andesite Casing and simple kinetic blocks of Create."
	quest.77C3D285E52CCA0E.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.77C3D285E52CCA0E.quest_subtitle: "Table Cloths can be used to sell items to other players."
	quest.77D4B279CB51820E.quest_desc: ["Lets hoppers, pipes, and other transport blocks interact with the machine through the addon instead of the machine itself. Very useful when the main block is blocked in by its multiblock footprint."]
	quest.77D4B279CB51820E.quest_subtitle: "Exposes a machine's inventory on the addon's face."
	quest.77E21E3DC184C363.quest_desc: ["Slowly heats up using solid fuel, then produces up to 8 mb of steam per tick at max temperature — enough to power 4 bronze machines. Sends steam automatically to adjacent machines."]
	quest.77E21E3DC184C363.quest_subtitle: "The heart of any steam factory, converting fuel and water into steam."
	quest.77EA98920E57EB27.quest_desc: ["Powah's most powerful generator. Place 36 Nitro Reactor blocks in a 3x4 area and they auto-assemble into a powerhouse that can supply an entire end-game base."]
	quest.77EA98920E57EB27.quest_subtitle: "Nitro Nuclear Power"
	quest.7817759A925A289B.quest_desc: ["Built from Heatproof Casings and Cupronickel Coils, it produces Aluminum, Stainless Steel, Titanium, and more. Requires an Energy Input Hatch of the right tier to run."]
	quest.7817759A925A289B.quest_subtitle: "The electric multiblock required to smelt advanced alloys."
	quest.786E3F93D5908366.quest_desc: ["Each active channel lights up a colored dot on the cable. Use smart cables near the Controller or in bottleneck areas to diagnose channel usage and plan your cable layout."]
	quest.786E3F93D5908366.quest_subtitle: "The Smart Cable shows how many of its 8 channels are in use via colored indicators on its surface."
	quest.788BD46B45162E49.quest_desc: ["Apply it via crafting table or sneak-right-click on a bronze machine to promote it. Steel machines run twice as fast on up to 4 EU/t and unlock additional recipes."]
	quest.788BD46B45162E49.quest_subtitle: "An upgrade applied to bronze machines to bring them to steel tier."
	quest.78CCA9EC988BA445.quest_desc: ["Refines bauxite dust into aluminum dust, unlocks chromium and manganese tiny dusts, and splits many other compounds. A must-have for advanced chemistry."]
	quest.78CCA9EC988BA445.quest_subtitle: "Splits materials into elements using strong electric currents."
	quest.78DEEE44DA6DC746.quest_desc: ["Add multiple Crafting Accelerators to a CPU for faster autocrafting throughput. Essential for high-volume operations where multiple crafting steps follow each other in rapid succession."]
	quest.78DEEE44DA6DC746.quest_subtitle: "Speeds up the Crafting CPU by reducing the delay between ingredient pushes to machines."
	quest.78EE63AA4A75C011.quest_desc: ["Charges FE items in adjacent inventories at a very high rate. Multiple Spirited Energy Hoppers can service a large storage system simultaneously."]
	quest.78EE63AA4A75C011.quest_subtitle: "Spirited Item Charging"
	quest.7917E75BBA3F0614.quest_desc: [
		"First, use the display link on a Display Block to link it. Then place it on the Source Block that will be read from. Though it will link to any block, not every block can act as a display or source. "
		""
		"Right click the link to access its interface. Additional labels can be added to the output text through this interface. Some sources provide multiple options for formatting the text. Once the interface settings are accepted, the green light on the display link will start blinking, indicating transmission of information to the display blocks."
	]
	quest.7917E75BBA3F0614.quest_subtitle: "A Display Link is used to get information from a block and send it to blocks that can display it."
	quest.794C0CD2DA500874.quest_desc: ["The Portable Engine runs on furnace fuels and can be configured to spin in either direction. Fuel can be inserted by automated means, and feeding it a Blaze Cake superheats the engine for a temporary boost in power output. Pair it with a Propeller Bearing to obtain a fully self-propelled airship that needs no external rotational source."]
	quest.794C0CD2DA500874.quest_subtitle: "A self-contained engine that produces Rotational Force on a moving Contraption by burning fuel."
	quest.7959095B34262545.quest_desc: ["Each Speed Card increases items processed per operation. Up to 4 cards can be inserted into Import/Export Buses and other compatible devices. Requires the Advanced Card to craft."]
	quest.7959095B34262545.quest_subtitle: "Increases the operation speed of supported AE2 devices."
	quest.7988D1BB63A66FC7.quest_desc: ["A faster Ender Cell with higher I/O than the Hardened version. Good for high-throughput ender network setups."]
	quest.7988D1BB63A66FC7.quest_subtitle: "Faster Ender Network"
	quest.798C46DA99925144.quest_desc: ["Configure the filter with items it should allow or block, then place it inline with your item pipes. Essential for directing specific outputs from centrifuges, foundries, and multi-recipe machines."]
	quest.798C46DA99925144.quest_subtitle: "Filters items passing through an item pipe network."
	quest.79BA0067A6864FC6.quest_desc: ["Built with Processing Units and superconductor components. Required for the Nuclear Reactor, Large Diesel Generator, and the other endgame multiblocks."]
	quest.79BA0067A6864FC6.quest_subtitle: "The EV-tier machine hull used for nuclear-era machinery."
	quest.79C053DA124BF68E.quest_desc: ["Configure up to 9 item or fluid slots to be automatically restocked from the network. When a Pattern Provider on a subnet targets an Interface on the main network, it creates an efficient logistics bridge."]
	quest.79C053DA124BF68E.quest_subtitle: "A versatile device that stocks items from the network, accepts returns from machines, and bridges subnetworks."
	quest.7B1F8B964612BFD5.quest_desc: ["Printed in the Inscriber using a Logic Processor Press found in meteorite loot. Combine the printed circuit with printed silicon in the Inscriber to assemble the final Logic Processor."]
	quest.7B1F8B964612BFD5.quest_subtitle: "The Logic Processor is the most common processor, required for many basic AE2 components."
	quest.7B3CE9A0B077B28F.quest_desc: ["When a cell is partitioned via the Cell Workbench, this card fills each section evenly rather than filling one completely before moving to the next. Requires the Advanced Card to craft."]
	quest.7B3CE9A0B077B28F.quest_subtitle: "Distributes items equally across the partitioned sections of an ME Storage Cell."
	quest.7B89FFBFE6C8565A.quest_desc: ["Place an ingot inside the Rolling Mill and supply Rotational Force. The block rolls the ingot into a metal sheet (or a rod, depending on the recipe). Faster and more compact than a Mechanical Press setup, ideal for early sheet automation."]
	quest.7B89FFBFE6C8565A.quest_subtitle: "A compact press from Create: Crafts \\& Additions that rolls ingots into sheets and rods."
	quest.7C074B5E2A0EAA63.quest_desc: [
		"To assemble a Train, the train must have at least one set of controls that face forward relative to the Train Station the train is created at. If a non-player conductor is desired, a Blaze Burner or Seat must be placed directly behind the controls."
		""
		"On a Train, Train Controls can be right clicked to take control of the Train. The player's ordinary movement options will affect the Train instead. Use the controls again or sneak to stop. Hold left or right at a fork to choose a path. Use the scroll wheel to adjust maximum speed. Hold jump to approach and align at a Station. If a Steam Whistle is attached, press the sprint key to blow it."
	]
	quest.7C074B5E2A0EAA63.quest_subtitle: "Train Controls are required in the creation of Trains."
	quest.7C2FC333931AB319.quest_desc: ["Create is a minecraft mod created by simibubi that allows you to make Contraptions and automate processes using Rotational Power. It adds many mechanical components and block variants to the game. This mod has good optimization and FPS, so it can be played on nearly any computer!"]
	quest.7C2FC333931AB319.quest_subtitle: "Aesthetic Technology that empowers the Player"
	quest.7C922886917D04B6.quest_desc: ["Items stored in the network appear as available in the crafting grid. Click any craftable recipe in JEI/REI to auto-fill the grid. Results are stored back in the network automatically."]
	quest.7C922886917D04B6.quest_subtitle: "Combines ME Terminal access with a built-in crafting grid that pulls items directly from network storage."
	quest.7CFBA7624721FE32.quest_desc: [
		"Installing this addon reduces the energy consumption of the machine by 20% per cycle. The machine will not be any faster, but it'll need less RF/t."
		""
		"This is especially useful for machines that run constantly or for setups where energy generation is limited. Multiple efficiency addons can be stacked to further minimize power usage."
		""
		"Applicable to all machines that consume energy each tick they work."
	]
	quest.7CFBA7624721FE32.quest_subtitle: "The Efficiency Addon reduces the energy use of your machinery."
	quest.7D22EAA37519D4FA.quest_desc: ["Extracted from air in the Centrifuge. Used as a shielding gas for advanced EBF smelting recipes, notably for the highest-tier metals."]
	quest.7D22EAA37519D4FA.quest_subtitle: "An inert gas extracted through centrifuging."
	quest.7D28418129EE6957.quest_desc: ["Place the main machine block first, then right-click it to highlight where the cores must go. Higher quality cores do not speed up operation — they only raise the number of addons and extender layers the machine can support."]
	quest.7D28418129EE6957.quest_subtitle: "Some machines require additional machine cores to function. These must be placed at specific positions relative to the machine itself. The number of cores needed for a machine is listed in the machine's tooltip. Cores cannot be shared between machines."
	quest.7D28418129EE6957.title: "Multiblock Machines"
	quest.7DB15E58060E3CF5.quest_desc: ["Combines a circuit board with all five passive components — capacitor, resistor, inductor, copper wire, and the board itself. Required inside every basic electric machine hull."]
	quest.7DB15E58060E3CF5.quest_subtitle: "The first-tier electronic circuit, unlocking LV machines."
	quest.7DE1A43C0269F8B5.quest_desc: ["Crafted from copper wire wound around an iron core. Appears in generator, motor, and most mid-tier machine recipes that rely on electromagnetic components."]
	quest.7DE1A43C0269F8B5.quest_subtitle: "A fundamental component for generating electromagnetic fields in machinery."
	quest.7DF0D95CD3FE879C.quest_desc: ["Mix lead and antimony dusts in a Mixer to produce it. Smelt into Battery Alloy Ingots for low-voltage battery hatches and energy storage."]
	quest.7DF0D95CD3FE879C.quest_subtitle: "A lead-antimony dust blend used for crafting batteries."
	quest.7E1FF283706C48F7.quest_desc: ["A Simulated Contraption needs forces to move. The blocks unlocked here generate Lift through hot-air or steam balloons, or Thrust through propellers, sails, and engines. Combine them to climb, cruise, hover, or fly under power. Note that all of them weaken as Air Pressure drops with altitude, so high-altitude designs need bigger balloons or more propellers."]
	quest.7E1FF283706C48F7.quest_subtitle: "Propulsion: the blocks that turn Rotational Force into Thrust and Lift on a Simulated Contraption."
	quest.7E7202497F167C39.quest_desc: ["Like a Steam Engine, the Steam Vent needs sufficient Heat, Water, and Boiler Space to operate. When powered with Redstone it gradually fills the Envelope above it; the input panel sets the maximum Steam output and Redstone scales it. Multiple vents can combine, but the boiler must supply enough power for all of them to run at full capacity."]
	quest.7E7202497F167C39.quest_subtitle: "Generates Lift by filling a balloon with Steam, like a Steam Engine producing buoyancy instead of rotation."
	quest.7EA42E9B3FBB179E.quest_desc: ["Converts each mb of steam directly into 1 EU, up to 32 EU/t. Connects only to LV cables on its output side — usually the first electrical generator you'll build."]
	quest.7EA42E9B3FBB179E.quest_subtitle: "Converts steam directly into low-voltage electricity."
	quest.7F80C23C2681904D.quest_desc: ["Crafted with cupronickel magnetic wire wrapped around an iron core. An essential component of Analog Circuits."]
	quest.7F80C23C2681904D.quest_subtitle: "A passive electronic component storing energy in a magnetic field."
	quest.7FA5A4EC7599D28E.quest_desc: ["Right-click a water source to fill it, then insert solid fuel by right-clicking fuel items on the drill in your inventory. Mines a 3x3 area with Silk Touch — perfect for early ore collection paired with the Forge Hammer."]
	quest.7FA5A4EC7599D28E.quest_subtitle: "A steam-powered drill that mines 3x3 blocks with Silk Touch."
